(window.DHAMMA_SHARDS=window.DHAMMA_SHARDS||{})["short"]={"v":[["04LoEe00z18","Confidence about what is now","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","m",1195,101,"B2"],["39OHGpRojYg","Clear comprehension of the truth of what is there","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","m",1085,90,"B2"],["3GhBFjg2sOE","Dhamma is right here, so very close: from head to toe","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","m",1188,106,"B2"],["PGTxSd3NZVg","The path is subtle because it goes all the way with no attachment","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","a",2271,92,"B2"],["SSEk95nr8FE","The shame of not yet knowing lobha as nama","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","a",603,121,"B2"],["Twa0DnDebJU","Khanti, the habit of developing right understanding","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","a",926,95,"B2"],["UeJ93tVl_ik","Intention—not the path to understand the truth of reality","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","m",619,97,"B2"],["WBnG8dg-JrA","Sense of self - the reality of imagination","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","m",1105,101,"B2"],["dJkndWTXI6k","Clear comprehension of the benefits of understanding Dhamma","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","m",1379,94,"B2"],["gyuF9cVfuag","There is so much self that is unclear even just talking about it","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","a",1793,93,"B2"],["i_dwz-ptwz4","Dhamma: as soon as it has arisen is gone: no conditions for it to last","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","m",1387,101,"B2"],["kp2ZsIwTewU","All dhammas are like something behind a black curtain","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","a",1018,124,"B2"],["kqdmQYvQRF0","Brahma-vihara, being kind to the beings there at that very moment","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","a",406,112,"B2"],["t_sbFcRkyjw","Not dreaming at moment of understanding—even in a dream","Ajahn Sujin · คลิปสั้น Studying Dhamma","dhamma","INTL","m",1694,90,"B2"]],"s":[[0,5.21,4.79,"[A. Sujin] \"Is it this or that?\" It's not confidence at all!"],[0,12.71,8.8,"So, confidence of understanding the truth of what is there, little by little, until it's so firm."],[0,22.77,3.6,"So, what is there? No confidence at all!"],[0,27.36,2.68,"How to answer: what is there?"],[0,31.36,6.15,"No confidence of what is there as it is - or as something or any idea at all."],[0,38.32,7.25,"So, the greatest confidence is the confidence of [in] the truth, of what is there as it is."],[0,47.36,5.27,"That's why just the question: what is seen?"],[0,54.81,1.67,"What is the answer?"],[0,58.87,5.62,"[Vincent] What is seen can be understood only on the level of the word."],[0,64.75,7.62,"[A. Sujin] It doesn't matter at all; just what conditions the word to answer \"what is seen?\""],[0,73.95,9.52,"Before saying any word the Buddha said: listen, attending carefully to what I'll say."],[0,85.2,5.75,"When a question is asked, so many thoughts about different things — our own thinking,"],[0,91.16,7.77,"but what is seen now? Just answer that question only. What is seen?"],[0,101.22,6.12,"[Vincent] And what is seen is rupa; it is the visible object, according to the Buddha's words."],[0,107.87,2.41,"[A. Sujin] According to the word or to the truth?"],[0,110.89,4.24,"[Vincent] Because there's no direct experience here, I cannot really say it's the truth,"],[0,115.2,5.03,"but I can continue to listen to the discussions. [Yeah.] That means I'm still interested."],[0,120.52,3.25,"[A. Sujin] But that does not answer the question at all."],[0,124.18,7.46,"Just listen carefully, to what? To the question, in order to answer the question."],[0,133.19,6.93,"So, is it sincere now to say: \"What is seen?\""],[0,141.79,3.62,"Being true to the truth of the answer."],[0,146.5,9.28,"How much understanding by answering \"what is seen\"? [Right. It's the rupa that is seen.]"],[0,156.32,8.48,"It's the idea, her own idea before answering the question — just what is seen, it's so short!"],[0,166.16,6.24,"What, what, what is seen? Not the idea or the story of that which is seen."],[0,173.84,3.93,"Answer truly, truly: what is seen?"],[0,179.33,3.95,"[Vincent] Even though I know the answer is a visible object,"],[0,183.28,3.12,"when I look at a table, I still think about the wood."],[0,187.11,1.69,"[A. Sujin] Is that the answer to the question?"],[0,190.09,5.94,"[Vincent] Irene says she's still a bit confused. She still thinks about the story of what is seen."],[0,197.08,6.21,"[A. Sujin] So now, just now, be true to the truth."],[0,204.32,4.74,"Just the answer for \"what is seen now?\""],[0,210.31,8.86,"If the answer is not the direct answer to the question, it's no confidence at all."],[0,220.48,2.42,"We are talking about confidence,"],[0,223.36,6.47,"and this is the way to understand and to be true to what is meant by confidence."],[0,231.08,6.6,"Just the answer indicates how much understanding and how much confidence in the answer."],[0,244.08,6.24,"What is rupa, and what is visible object? [It's real,"],[0,250.32,2.56,"but I've read in some book that it's imagined.]"],[0,255.04,6.61,"What is real is real. It cannot be imagination or imagined at all."],[0,265.2,6.57,"Before imagination, there must be the moment of experiencing an object."],[0,277.63,2.37,"Dhamma is so very subtle."],[0,280.0,6.64,"It has to be your own understanding, your own consideration, not another's answer at all."],[0,286.64,5.84,"It has to be careful consideration: manasikara, yoniso-manasikara,"],[0,292.98,6.78,"attending very carefully to... we are talking about confidence,"],[0,299.82,2.87,"so it has to be right now,"],[0,303.52,5.48,"whether it's confidence, not enough confidence, or no confidence at all."],[0,309.41,7.79,"So the question is, in order to know how much confidence — or no confidence at all, what is seen?"],[0,317.2,6.88,"For everyone, not just for Irene. What is seen?"],[0,325.04,5.04,"This is to understand confidence. What is seen?"],[0,333.6,4.88,"Just a very simple question. It depends on understanding."],[0,339.6,8.88,"Very short, not the story of that which is seen or anyone's idea or my idea or what the book said,"],[0,348.48,6.95,"but being true to the truth, answering just the question — what is seen?"],[0,356.24,2.87,"Because now we are talking about confidence."],[0,360.88,12.11,"See, hesitation is not confidence. What is seen? [Rupa.]"],[0,374.24,4.83,"What is it? What is rupa? What kind of rupa? See."],[0,379.78,2.94,"Confidence about what is seen."],[0,391.93,7.29,"Is that the answer for: what is seen? [Visible object.]"],[0,399.91,4.18,"Okay. Confident? [Yes]"],[0,405.6,6.69,"So, nobody else knows; it is your own understanding, your own answer to be true to the truth."],[0,413.23,7.25,"So, it's time to have a little more confidence about the truth of what is seen."],[0,420.48,6.64,"Otherwise, there will never be a little more confidence about what is seen at all."],[0,427.12,4.06,"What is seen is there right now,"],[0,432.75,8.05,"isn't it what we take for or what appears as red or blue or brown or light?"],[0,441.84,3.42,"No one there at all. What is true?"],[0,446.43,8.61,"What is seen is only that which we are used to taking or experiencing as red or brown,"],[0,455.04,4.08,"different color, or color, or visible object, or light..."],[0,459.12,3.04,"It doesn't matter, because it's now that it's seen."],[0,462.16,5.28,"But the truth is that what is seen cannot be anything at all"],[0,467.44,5.68,"because it is only that which can impinge on the eye-base."],[0,473.12,4.98,"There must be the eye-base, otherwise there could never be seeing."],[0,478.36,4.22,"And even if there is the eye-base, if nothing impinges on it,"],[0,483.68,3.28,"there could never be seeing at all."],[0,486.96,5.65,"So, seeing is not that which is seen. A little more confidence?"],[0,494.03,7.33,"Seeing is a reality. It's real. That which is seen is real, a reality,"],[0,501.36,6.61,"but there are so many realities. Many, many dhammas."],[0,508.19,6.49,"Some experience the object, and some do not experience the object."],[0,515.12,3.76,"They are different. They are dhammas. No one at all"],[0,518.88,4.2,"because there must be conditions for whatever is now appearing"],[0,523.08,3.65,"because it has arisen by conditions."],[0,527.8,6.26,"Its proper conditions to arise to be only that which is now appearing."],[0,535.81,7.02,"Is what is now appearing real? What reality is it?"],[0,544.2,8.82,"Be true to the truth right now, more and more — a little more confidence of the truth."],[0,553.04,2.84,"It has to begin at this moment,"],[0,557.32,4.83,"otherwise there can never be more confidence about what one has heard,"],[0,563.2,3.95,"about the truth, to understand the truth as the truth."],[0,569.2,5.23,"Otherwise, confidence about what, if it's not about the truth?"],[0,575.82,7.83,"Understanding what is there now is the beginning of a little more confidence about the truth."],[0,585.68,2.64,"Not the story about what is there as a whole,"],[0,588.32,5.91,"but at the moment of what is there appearing — no understanding of it as one has heard."],[0,596.22,6.45,"So, what is the point of listening to what is there, more and more and more?"],[0,603.81,1.68,"Not just to believe,"],[0,606.0,6.88,"but just to consider carefully again and again because it's so very deep."],[0,612.88,3.97,"Even it's there appearing, no one knows the truth of it."],[0,618.35,7.41,"So, confidence about being true to the truth, little by little until it's so firm, never change."],[0,627.44,5.91,"So, what about the answer \"what is seen is rupa,\" or \"what is seen is visible object\"?"],[0,633.57,4.67,"But what is it now? Something is seen."],[0,638.6,2.92,"Is that confidence enough?"],[0,641.52,5.4,"Anyone can say — what is seen is that which impinges on the eye-base;"],[0,647.12,3.68,"— it is the reality which cannot experience anything."],[0,650.8,4.08,"While what is seen is something all the time."],[0,655.6,3.6,"So, there must be confidence about the three rounds of the four noble truths."],[0,659.2,6.08,"The first round, the second round, the third round — more and more confidence."],[0,665.28,3.36,"So, no one can say for another how much confidence he or she has;"],[0,668.64,4.45,"it has to be one's own consideration of what is there,"],[0,674.29,2.91,"with how much confidence."],[0,678.58,5.5,"[Vincent] DaZhuang says yes, only that which is visible can be seen."],[0,684.62,3.88,"[A. Sujin] So, how much confidence when one says visible object?"],[0,689.29,8.52,"Firm confidence that it cannot be a doll, or a cat, or a dog that is seen, or anything else at all."],[0,699.14,2.86,"The moment of seeing is so very short,"],[0,702.3,7.75,"how could it see many things around instantly, as something, all the time?"],[0,711.81,7.59,"So, how much wrong understanding with ignorance of that which is seen has been accumulated?"],[0,720.8,4.91,"In order to understand the truth, the ultimate truth of what is seen,"],[0,726.0,8.67,"confidence that it will take a long, long time, not just right now. Is it true?"],[0,735.04,8.08,"Wrong understanding with ignorance and attachment to the idea of self has been accumulated..."],[0,743.12,7.27,"For how long? So, how can there be the gradual, very subtle letting go of it?"],[0,751.03,4.57,"Only by understanding little by little about the truth of it."],[0,756.86,7.39,"At moment of understanding the truth, the confidence gets a little firmer and firmer."],[0,765.85,6.9,"Listen more to the truth, not just \"visible object\", but anything which is around any time."],[0,773.36,3.37,"And right understanding develops little by little."],[0,777.36,6.86,"So, a little more confidence about the truth develops too. Isn't it true? [It is.]"],[0,786.65,5.69,"The answer is \"a little more confidence,\" and it's right."],[0,796.8,2.82,"Is there a little more confidence?"],[0,808.44,4.85,"That's it. Without understanding, there is doubt, not confidence at all."],[0,815.36,3.04,"So, of what level is confidence right now?"],[0,820.12,6.47,"[Vincent] Can I just quickly check with Yong because he was near the ocean and watching the birds."],[0,837.26,7.48,"At moment of seeing, he is \"watching\" the birds; what is there?"],[0,846.72,2.38,"It's not wrong saying \"the five khandhas,\""],[0,849.42,4.46,"but what are the five khandhas at moment of watching the birds?"],[0,860.72,4.88,"How many khandhas, seeing? [Seeing is one khandha.]"],[0,865.91,5.24,"Okay, and what about the other four? [They're also there.]"],[0,871.84,8.95,"What are they? [Vedana khandha is there, and sañña khandha, and sankhara khandha — they are also there.]"],[0,881.76,4.51,"At that moment he was watching the bird, but what is now?"],[0,886.75,6.42,"What is confidence? What is now? [Now it's thinking.]"],[0,894.86,4.56,"This is about confidence. See?"],[0,914.72,6.44,"That's why right understanding is so very subtle; the truth is the truth,"],[0,921.26,5.89,"but what we've said about the truth, what level of understanding is it?"],[0,930.33,3.11,"Different degrees of everything."],[0,936.0,5.08,"So, no matter what we talk about, it concerns confidence too."],[0,942.81,4.35,"When it's one's own understanding of what confidence is,"],[0,948.0,5.54,"there can be the understanding of the degree of confidence too."],[0,955.21,6.68,"That's why right understanding means *right* understanding of the truth, any moment."],[0,964.24,4.67,"Even right understanding has different degrees of understanding too."],[0,969.87,6.8,"Is there now confidence about the different degrees of understanding?"],[0,978.76,5.7,"That's why confidence of the truth goes along with right understanding."],[0,986.96,4.46,"A little, very little understanding, very little confidence."],[0,993.36,5.62,"Are there any more questions about confidence? Or it is clear now?"],[0,999.89,3.66,"[Vincent] He asked: is this how the light operates?"],[0,1005.83,3.12,"[A. Sujin] The understanding or the life operates?"],[0,1011.92,11.4,"What is seen is very, very tiny — only a speck... or things around... people in this room?"],[0,1025.02,12.61,"Or it's just a moment of seeing only that which can be seen, so very tiny."],[0,1039.34,3.34,"So no doubt about how many colors appear right now."],[0,1043.11,5.53,"They seem to be together, but in truth, they can never be together."],[0,1051.06,7.79,"So, no matter what we are talking about, it's just to have right understanding of the truth."],[0,1060.32,4.13,"And without the words of truth from the Enlightened One,"],[0,1064.66,5.58,"there would never be any understanding of the truth of what is there right now at all."],[0,1071.36,6.32,"Being true, even understanding Dhamma — what is it?"],[0,1079.36,5.94,"And being true means to understand that all dhammas are anatta."],[0,1087.47,8.91,"So, understand a dhamma as dhamma, not anything or anyone at all. Is it true?"],[0,1097.92,6.12,"Being true to the truth of that which is seen; it's real, it's only a reality."],[0,1104.82,5.07,"It's there, seen, so it's so real."],[0,1110.8,4.05,"If there is no understanding of the truth of a dhamma,"],[0,1115.11,3.59,"each dhamma is taken for something instantly,"],[0,1120.4,6.22,"because of ignorance, no understanding of the truth, not firm enough."],[0,1127.8,7.07,"So, we will continue on, understanding dhamma, considering it, throughout our whole life."],[0,1136.26,5.69,"Never enough at all if there's no realization of the truth that we've learned."],[0,1143.68,3.84,"And this is the understanding of ariya-sacca-dhamma,"],[0,1147.99,6.74,"isn't it so very subtle? Nothing is as subtle as the truth of what is there right now:"],[0,1155.78,1.75,"visible object;"],[0,1159.08,7.32,"so true so real, it cannot be anything it cannot be anyone because it's a dhamma."],[0,1167.6,4.33,"Is there a little more confidence about that which is seen?"],[0,1172.8,4.46,"Not taking it as someone or something as before."],[0,1179.44,6.8,"Strong confidence about the truth, not to take it as someone or somenthing as before."],[0,1187.34,3.4,"And it's time again; sawadee ka, everyone."],[1,4.79,3.77,"[A. Sujin] All depends on sampajañña."],[1,8.56,8.24,"So now, are we talking about satthaka, or sappāya, or gocara, or asammoha? See."],[1,16.8,7.91,"All depends on understanding the truth, not just the word."],[1,24.71,4.41,"[Tam B.:] Yes, I think these aspects come from understanding."],[1,30.05,5.14,"[A. Sujin:] That's why understand the truth of the very subtle realities,"],[1,35.2,5.97,"the cetasika, the citta and the rupa,"],[1,43.04,5.19,"until understanding the nature of nibbana, see;"],[1,48.72,2.16,"not at the very beginning."],[1,50.88,3.69,"That's why we're learning to understand the ultimate truth,"],[1,54.96,3.36,"the reality, the absolute reality;"],[1,59.25,2.56,"citta is citta, it cannot be cetasika."],[1,64.52,4.22,"Can citta itself be clear comprehension?"],[1,77.64,7.16,"See, and this is the beginning of understanding, the comprehension of citta,"],[1,84.8,7.42,"until it's clearer and clearer, as gocara sampajañña."],[1,96.32,6.14,"[Acharn, citta experiences the object clearly,"],[1,102.88,3.6,"does that mean there is clear comprehension or not?]"],[1,106.98,4.51,"Not at all, it's just the function of citta"],[1,112.16,4.6,"- a reality which experiences the object,"],[1,117.16,5.92,"but it experiences the object so clearly, for the other moments,"],[1,123.08,6.52,"when the sañña and other realities know the difference between the fake and real one;"],[1,129.6,5.6,"fake diamond, real diamond; fake pearl, real pearl, see."],[1,135.2,3.92,"If citta does not experience very clearly,"],[1,139.12,3.92,"how could it be known that these two are different?"],[1,143.04,3.2,"But knowing that the two are different,"],[1,146.24,1.93,"- one is fake and one the other is not fake,"],[1,148.34,2.78,"it's not the function of citta;"],[1,151.12,5.04,"the function of citta is just to experience the object clearly,"],[1,156.16,4.8,"to be the chief, the leader of the world, in going to war or to peace,"],[1,160.96,5.58,"or to whatever is there, to any subject, any thought."],[1,168.69,5.2,"So, the world is under the power of citta,"],[1,174.4,3.35,"which experiences the object so clearly;"],[1,178.39,7.61,"otherwise, how could there be the moment of knowing the difference between this and that?"],[1,190.69,10.31,"So, remembering or sañña just marks and remembers what citta experiences;"],[1,202.4,5.37,"it cannot perform the function of experiencing the object clearly at all,"],[1,208.08,4.72,"because it just experiences the object which citta has already experienced,"],[1,212.8,2.84,"and just marks and remembers that object."],[1,218.16,12.66,"So now, there is citta and there is sañña cetasika, cetana cetasika, manasikara cetasika, phassa cetasika."],[1,231.84,8.59,"No rupa within or arising together with these realities which just experience the object"],[1,241.56,12.62,"- no color, no sound, no smell, no taste at all - just the pure-experiencing-reality."],[1,273.63,4.87,"Is that your purpose? [Yes, Ajahn.]"],[1,279.12,2.78,"So, it's not understanding."],[1,282.67,3.68,"The purpose cannot be the understanding at all,"],[1,288.32,9.23,"because everyone can have purpose in life without understanding,"],[1,302.96,4.32,"but now we are talking about the sampajañña,"],[1,307.28,6.94,"the clear comprehension of the object, gocara."],[1,314.83,6.29,"No matter what, it can be gocara of right understanding,"],[1,321.12,5.52,"when it has developed to the degree that it doesn't matter at all what is there,"],[1,326.92,5.09,"because it can understand the truth of that reality."],[1,332.96,6.72,"While watching the movies, can't there be moments of understanding the object?"],[1,339.68,3.76,"Because right understanding has been developed to that degree,"],[1,343.44,6.16,"it is the condition to experience any object with understanding."],[1,349.6,6.48,"So, no matter what, it can be the object of understanding only when there is understanding,"],[1,356.08,4.87,"but when there's no understanding, it cannot be the object of understanding,"],[1,360.95,8.89,"it is the object of pleasure, of lobha, enjoying it so much, in such situation, see."],[1,369.84,3.76,"But right understanding is not afraid of anything at all"],[1,373.6,6.35,"because it can understand the truth - when it's there."],[1,380.64,7.04,"So can the purpose understand? [Ms. Ha said no.]"],[1,387.68,6.16,"That's why understand each word, what is meant by sampajañña, see,"],[1,393.9,8.99,"pañña and sampajañña and sati and so on, each one is different;"],[1,403.44,4.64,"so, they cannot be the same one at all,"],[1,408.08,5.36,"just one reality at a time, different from the other."],[1,414.96,4.03,"So, understand what is meant by sampajañña,"],[1,419.84,3.68,"and understand the four kinds of sampajañña;"],[1,423.52,9.58,"all depends on understanding, clear comprehension of the truth of what is there."],[1,434.4,4.16,"So, when there is the clear comprehension of the object of understanding,"],[1,438.56,3.3,"no doubt - any object, by conditions;"],[1,442.57,4.39,"being the object of understanding when time comes by conditions,"],[1,446.96,4.55,"not by anyone's will or anyone's purpose at all."],[1,452.88,4.16,"And after hearing what Khun Sarah just said,"],[1,457.04,9.59,"clear comprehension of how pañña develops, sappāya sampajañña, see;"],[1,467.13,7.27,"without the moment of clear comprehension of - how it can begin and develop, as sappāya,"],[1,474.4,4.48,"there cannot be the very clear comprehension at all,"],[1,478.88,4.88,"or even understanding what is there as it is."],[1,484.96,4.72,"So, all depends on understanding; be true to this moment,"],[1,489.68,3.2,"how much understanding is there? It's not clear comprehension yet,"],[1,493.37,7.18,"but how to develop it? Not just - no understanding, not enough understanding;"],[1,500.81,4.6,"let's just have a drink or go to the movies or play and on and on."],[1,505.84,9.59,"That is not the understanding, not the clear comprehension of how right understanding develops."],[1,516.88,5.92,"But now, understanding that those situations - being intoxicated and so on,"],[1,522.8,4.25,"cannot be the beginning of the development of understanding,"],[1,527.36,5.27,"that is clear comprehension of how right understanding can develop."],[1,532.8,10.31,"That's why there is the word clear comprehension of what is suitable - sappāya sampajañña; is it true?"],[1,544.92,10.44,"[Achan, earlier you said that asammoha sampajañña is the level of direct understanding of realities."],[1,555.36,7.01,"So, does that mean that the three other kinds of sampajañña can be of different levels?]"],[1,562.63,8.6,"Leave it to the moment of asammoha - now - otherwise, when will it be?"],[1,571.63,7.89,"No doubt about the nature of that object as just - a reality experiencing the object,"],[1,580.16,2.88,"or that which cannot experience the object."],[1,583.04,7.08,"Hardness appears all day, no thought about it, that it's real, it's a reality;"],[1,590.4,5.52,"it isn't a table, it's not a chair, it's not a glass at all - just hardness."],[1,596.56,10.72,"Isn't that a-sammoha? No-moha, no misunderstanding, taking it for something."],[1,607.28,15.05,"So, the moment of direct understanding with direct awareness, no moha about the truth of it."],[1,633.12,7.68,"And when and where and how can kusala arise? [By conditions.]"],[1,640.8,5.19,"See, by understanding"],[1,645.99,7.61,"- when you don't have anything to do... do you just watch TV or read the tipitaka?"],[1,653.6,5.28,"what one will do, it depends on what purpose is there,"],[1,658.88,11.34,"with clear comprehension about what condition the moment of understanding to arise, little by little."],[1,671.76,9.29,"I don't know how it's translated from Pali to English or in Thai, sampajañña,"],[1,681.25,5.39,"but even if the word purpose is there, it's not the purpose,"],[1,686.64,3.28,"because the purpose can be kusala as well as akusala:"],[1,689.92,8.32,"the purpose to watch TV or the purpose to read Tipitaka, Dhamma;"],[1,698.24,7.52,"that's why even purpose depends on understanding or no understanding,"],[1,705.76,7.86,"but when there's the understanding, there is the purpose to develop wholesomeness"],[1,713.64,8.56,"- understanding that there's not yet understanding enough to realize the truth of gocara-dhamma,"],[1,722.45,4.64,"because it's so deep; that's why the understanding that"],[1,727.2,4.88,"just reading or considering the truth, or having Dhamma discussion, is better,"],[1,732.08,7.04,"it's the only way to have a little more careful considering and understanding."],[1,739.12,8.16,"It has to be right understanding of clear comprehension of that level, of that stage;"],[1,747.28,5.67,"clear comprehension of what is the gocara."],[1,755.28,8.85,"Is there clear comprehension of sappāya sampajañña now? Or not yet?"],[1,766.21,5.23,"If there's no clear comprehension of the four at all,"],[1,771.44,7.68,"how can there be the understanding of the truth of what is there right now?"],[1,780.24,5.12,"From no understanding to the moment of no doubt,"],[1,785.36,9.24,"because at that moment there is direct awareness with direct understanding, asammoha sampajañña."],[1,796.31,9.11,"If it's not there yet, it needs the other three sampajaññas to be condition for the fourth sampajañña."],[1,807.52,6.8,"-[She said that it is understanding of the purpose of developing realities.]"],[1,814.6,5.05,"So, what reality is purpose?"],[1,820.88,6.6,"Is it you... or what is it? [Thinking, Ajahn.]"],[1,828.24,6.5,"What is thinking? What thinks? [Cetasika, Ajahn.]"],[1,834.89,5.67,"What cetasika? [Vitakka cetasika.]"],[1,841.76,9.17,"Is it the purpose? [The purpose is connected to the cetana cetasika.]"],[1,851.68,4.4,"What do you mean by connected? Is it different from cetana?"],[1,856.08,7.92,"Is it another reality, which is connected to cetana or what?"],[1,864.0,9.64,"So, is clear comprehension purpose or not? [The beginning.]"],[1,874.64,4.16,"What is the beginning?"],[1,885.84,4.72,"That's why we have to study again and again to understand clearer"],[1,890.56,4.8,"and clearer the truth of one reality at a time."],[1,896.24,5.04,"We're talking about citta, not cetasikas,"],[1,901.28,3.52,"because citta is different from cetasikas;"],[1,904.8,4.96,"even they experience the same object, arise together,"],[1,909.76,3.52,"but citta cannot be any cetasika,"],[1,913.28,4.08,"or any cetasika cannot be citta at all."],[1,917.36,12.23,"So, what is the difference between citta and cetasika?"],[1,929.6,1.69,"This is comprehension, understanding the difference between citta and cetasikas."],[1,931.28,4.48,"So please, again, to understand citta a little more"],[1,935.76,4.0,"until it becomes clear comprehension"],[1,939.76,5.92,"of that which has to be the object of understanding."],[1,950.0,10.88,"What is sampajañña, is it real? [It's real and it's pañña cetasika, Ajahn.]"],[1,960.88,6.08,"So, it is not citta, is it? [Yes, Ajahn.]"],[1,966.96,16.19,"And it's not vitakka cetasika, is it? [Yes, Ajahn.]"],[1,983.15,0.05,"It is not cetana cetasika, is it? [Yes, Ajahn.]"],[1,983.2,8.08,"So, what cetasika is sampajañña? [It's the pañña cetasika, Ajahn.]"],[1,991.28,5.2,"That's why clear comprehension begins little by little,"],[1,996.48,3.52,"understanding a little more, understanding gets clearer and clearer."],[1,1000.0,4.88,"Clear comprehension, more and more."],[1,1004.88,4.08,"For 45 years, the Buddha taught about the truth,"],[1,1008.96,5.52,"to be realized, to be understood, to be developed,"],[1,1014.48,5.2,"stage by stage, clearer and clearer, see,"],[1,1019.68,6.64,"because dhamma is so very subtle, it's easy to go wrong."],[1,1026.32,5.28,"That's why it takes time again and again to consider just one reality"],[1,1031.6,6.64,"until confidence it's so firm, about its nature, as not that of another reality."],[1,1038.24,7.86,"Citta cannot be any cetasika, it cannot be pañña"],[1,1046.1,0.04,"- it cannot understand, it cannot comprehend;"],[1,1046.15,5.29,"and pañña cannot experience the object clearly - the object, not understanding,"],[1,1051.44,6.56,"but just to experience the nature of the object is not the function of pañña."],[1,1058.0,10.36,"Pañña is moment of understanding the truth of the object; aren't they different?"],[1,1070.4,8.38,"A little more clear comprehension, clearer than before, a little bit."],[1,1078.78,2.9,"Kha, sawadee kha, everyone."],[2,5.2,6.05,"So now, be firmly confident of each reality,"],[2,12.03,4.35,"each reality which arises and experiences the object"],[2,16.38,7.46,"has its proper quality or characteristic and its own function;"],[2,23.84,4.48,"that which arises to experience must have its function."],[2,28.32,5.28,"So, the function of that which is the chief is citta, a reality;"],[2,33.6,5.04,"its function isn't to like or to dislike or to remember or to feel,"],[2,38.64,6.8,"it just performs the function of experiencing the object clearly;"],[2,45.44,7.68,"the other realities, the other nama, cannot experience the object clearly."],[2,53.12,8.08,"That's why there are dhammas, and two different kinds of realities,"],[2,61.2,2.96,"one arises to experience the object;"],[2,64.16,4.72,"the other kind arises but cannot experience the object."],[2,68.88,7.28,"So, from one word, dhamma, there must be the nama-dhamma and the rupa-dhamma;"],[2,76.16,3.28,"from one dhamma to be two kinds of dhamma."],[2,79.44,5.28,"And regarding the nama-dhamma, there are two kinds too:"],[2,84.72,3.68,"the reality which arises and experiences,"],[2,88.4,5.36,"performing the function of experiencing the object clearly is citta;"],[2,93.76,8.0,"and the other nama-dhamma: attachment, aversion, feeling, remembering, are all nama,"],[2,101.76,5.92,"because they experience the object and they perform their own function;"],[2,107.68,2.72,"they cannot perform the other's function."],[2,110.4,4.08,"For example, the reality which arises to attach,"],[2,114.48,8.56,"to like, to cling, is not the one which dislikes or hates, see."],[2,123.04,5.68,"So, there are many different nama-dhammas, and different rupas too;"],[2,128.72,3.08,"so, we learn about the ultimate truth of no-one,"],[2,131.8,5.32,"all are dhammas conditioned to arise and fall away instantly,"],[2,137.12,3.68,"beyond anyone's expectation or understanding"],[2,140.8,3.76,"because it's so very deep and so very profound."],[2,144.56,7.2,"That's why learn to understand the deep, profound characteristics of each reality,"],[2,151.76,5.52,"otherwise, there must be the idea - I see, I hear, I like, I dislike,"],[2,157.28,5.84,"because of the reality which arises and experiences - no-one there, so it's \"I\","],[2,163.12,2.72,"the seeing is \"I\", the hearing is \"I\";"],[2,165.84,2.04,"but the Buddha enlightened the truth"],[2,167.88,3.92,"- no-I, no-one, no permanent reality"],[2,171.8,5.2,"- that which arises and falls away is so very short."],[2,177.2,7.6,"Is it clear? [Ajahn, nama-dhamma, the other kinds of dhamma...]"],[2,184.8,7.2,"Excuse me, the other kind of nama-dhamma also experiences the object, but not as the chief,"],[2,192.0,4.72,"it has its own characteristics, its own function."],[2,196.72,7.6,"For example, the one which arises to attach or to like cannot dislike,"],[2,204.32,4.4,"its function is to arise to be attached;"],[2,208.72,7.36,"that's why they are citta and cetasika, the two kinds of nama-dhamma."],[2,216.08,7.6,"So now, from one word, dhamma, there are two words: nama-dhamma and rupa-dhamma,"],[2,223.68,6.32,"and then there are three words: citta, cetasika, and rupa,"],[2,230.0,2.56,"because there are two kinds of nama,"],[2,232.56,2.08,"citta can never be cetasika"],[2,234.64,6.72,"because its function is just to experience the object, no other functions;"],[2,241.36,4.96,"it cannot like or dislike, it cannot feel, it cannot remember,"],[2,246.32,6.4,"as the other kind of realities which arise and experience."],[2,252.72,6.8,"So these two kinds, the citta and the cetasikas, arise together,"],[2,259.52,5.28,"conditioning each other's arising to perform their function;"],[2,264.8,3.6,"Citta arises to perform the function of citta,"],[2,268.4,4.88,"and cetasikas, the other mental qualities, nama,"],[2,273.28,3.12,"arise and experience the object, the same object,"],[2,276.4,5.36,"because they arise together, experience the same object, fall away together."],[2,283.84,4.72,"That's why citta and cetasikas arise together all the time,"],[2,288.56,5.87,"the citta cannot arise without cetasikas,"],[2,294.43,2.29,"and the cetasikas cannot arise without citta;"],[2,296.72,4.8,"but citta itself cannot be unwholesome or wholesome,"],[2,301.52,4.4,"so, the word for citta is pandara - it's pure,"],[2,305.92,5.76,"but the cetasikas which arise with one citta,"],[2,311.68,3.28,"conditions citta to be unwholesome,"],[2,314.96,3.68,"because there is attachment, ignorance;"],[2,318.64,4.86,"and the other moment ignorance and irritation, and so on."],[2,324.0,2.56,"That's why we learn a little more,"],[2,326.56,5.44,"from dhamma into two kinds of dhamma: nama-dhamma and rupa-dhamma;"],[2,332.0,2.48,"and for nama-dhamma, there are two kinds:"],[2,334.48,4.08,"citta, the chief of experiencing, and cetasikas;"],[2,338.56,2.96,"arising together, experiencing the same object,"],[2,341.52,4.48,"but having different functions, different characteristics."],[2,346.0,5.04,"And no matter in Vinaya or Suttanta or Abhidhamma,"],[2,351.04,3.44,"all about dhammas: citta, cetasika and rupa;"],[2,354.48,8.16,"and the last one, nibbana: not citta, not cetasika, not rupa,"],[2,362.64,2.96,"but it's not daily life."],[2,365.6,6.4,"That's why, understanding the world means understanding what is there from moment to moment,"],[2,372.0,6.96,"and why is it the world? Because it's there, if it wasn't there, no world at all;"],[2,378.96,5.52,"if there is no citta, can there be any world? [No.]"],[2,384.48,9.44,"Not at all, so seeing is a world, of seeing, the world of colors only."],[2,393.92,4.88,"No understanding of the truth, taking it by nimitta,"],[2,398.8,6.0,"by the sign of each reality, the sign of seeing right now, not only one seeing."],[2,406.96,7.68,"Because as soon as one opens one's eye, so many things around, seen,"],[2,414.64,2.56,"not just only one moment;"],[2,417.2,6.8,"so what appears is by way of nimitta, just the sign of seeing,"],[2,424.0,4.08,"and the sign of that which is seen."],[2,428.08,8.48,"Nimitta, the world appears by way of nimitta, the sign of one reality;"],[2,436.56,4.08,"like the sign of seeing, many seeing right now,"],[2,440.64,2.8,"just only one seeing cannot be realized,"],[2,443.44,4.96,"so, it's the world of nimitta."],[2,448.4,4.08,"Eons and eons and eons and eons ago,"],[2,452.48,3.92,"so very deeply rooted or accumulated;"],[2,458.56,4.56,"until just the word of truth, one by one,"],[2,463.12,6.72,"can condition the understanding of the truth - three rounds."],[2,469.84,10.24,"The first round is only hearing, considering the truth of each moment as it's not permanent."],[2,480.08,7.68,"So, in truth, what appears does not appear as it is, is that right? [Yes, Ajahn.]"],[2,487.76,5.04,"By way of nimitta."],[2,493.0,5.72,"So, it has to begin to understand the truth firmer and firmer,"],[2,498.72,3.84,"otherwise it's not the study of dhamma,"],[2,502.56,6.8,"because dhamma is there: from head to toe, is that right? [Yes.]"],[2,509.36,5.52,"So close, so very close, but no thought about it,"],[2,514.88,4.16,"no attention to any reality even it's so close,"],[2,519.04,4.72,"hardness here, hearing here, seeing here;"],[2,523.76,8.24,"so, sound impinges on here, visible object impinges on here, see;"],[2,532.0,2.64,"and thinking is there too, not far away."],[2,535.2,7.04,"That's why we learn to understand what is taken for things, and someone or something"],[2,542.24,8.72,"- in truth, just only a moment of arising of realities - each one is different."],[2,550.96,5.12,"Arising and falling away so very rapidly that can never be known,"],[2,556.08,3.76,"until the enlightenment of the Buddha,"],[2,559.84,3.36,"how precious moment in life."],[2,565.12,6.0,"As the blind cannot see anything, even though the light is there all day,"],[2,571.12,6.56,"likewise no understanding of the truth of what is there at all,"],[2,577.68,6.16,"it does not appear as it is, as it is - to pañña it has to be in darkness,"],[2,583.84,4.32,"because only just one dot of light at moment of seeing,"],[2,588.16,6.24,"otherwise it's all in darkness, darker than when we turn off the light,"],[2,594.4,3.68,"because there is still the idea - it's dark."],[2,598.08,5.6,"So, the darkness of ignorance, see; eons and eons ago,"],[2,603.68,5.6,"that's why listening to the truth, respectful of the truth,"],[2,609.28,3.12,"learning to understand - dhamma is dhamma,"],[2,612.4,4.0,"no one can change it, no one can do anything,"],[2,616.4,5.36,"because actually no-one at all, only dhamma."],[2,621.76,4.24,"That's why understanding the term, the word of Dhamma,"],[2,626.0,4.32,"while the others just take it for the Teachings of the Buddha,"],[2,630.32,7.6,"but what about dhamma, only about dhamma, whatever is real."],[2,637.92,5.36,"So, don't be careless, just taking the word for granted, that it's understood,"],[2,643.28,5.52,"but it's so deep, that the more understanding, the more subtle it gets,"],[2,648.8,8.9,"and that is the way to let go the very subtle truth of each reality right now, one by one."],[2,658.02,7.5,"Even they are together, right understanding begins to understand the truth of each one,"],[2,665.52,4.24,"to know that what are there, not only citta,"],[2,669.76,2.96,"but citta is the chief of experiencing,"],[2,672.72,4.08,"but there is the mental reality, cetasika,"],[2,676.8,4.08,"also experiencing the object, arising together,"],[2,680.88,4.48,"performing its function, different functions for each cetasika,"],[2,685.36,5.6,"and citta itself is only the chief of experiencing the object,"],[2,690.96,3.44,"no matter what cetasikas it arises with,"],[2,694.4,2.8,"performing their functions of cetasika."],[2,697.2,6.28,"So, citta cannot perform the function of cetasika,"],[2,703.48,0.92,"and cetasika cannot perform the function of citta,"],[2,704.4,5.12,"and each cetasika cannot perform the function of the other cetasika."],[2,709.52,4.64,"Each is conditioned to be, and then gone instantly,"],[2,714.18,4.96,"That is the subtlety of life, of the world, of dhammas."],[2,720.94,9.54,"So, is it true? No-one, is it deep? [Yes, it is so deep.]"],[2,730.48,10.75,"And that is the understanding of dhamma, that is so deep, so true,"],[2,741.23,3.57,"abhidhamma, paramattha-dhamma, ariya-sacca-dhamma, see - what is real is dhamma;"],[2,744.8,7.68,"anger is real, it experiences the object it gets angry with."],[2,753.92,4.96,"So, citta experiences the object - no one knows;"],[2,758.88,6.16,"it just attends to the object which is experienced, each moment,"],[2,765.04,2.88,"from seeing what is seen, hearing what is heard, touchig what is"],[2,767.92,5.36,"touched, smelling what is smelled, tasting what is tasted, thinking what is thought about."],[2,773.28,9.84,"But there must be the chief of experiencing that object each moment, so very very rapidly,"],[2,783.12,5.92,"conditioning the whole world: to be the mountain, and the sun, and the moon, and everything,"],[2,789.04,9.92,"but if there was no citta at all, see, nothing could appear."],[2,798.96,5.36,"So, all depends on citta, in one aspect,"],[2,804.32,7.76,"without citta, nothing could be there at all, no sun, no moon, no sky, see."],[2,812.08,7.44,"Is this dhamma? So, more understanding of dhamma,"],[2,819.52,3.84,"more confidence of dhamma: it's the only way."],[2,823.36,8.08,"At that very moment of understanding, it let go, it wears away ignorance and attachment,"],[2,831.44,4.88,"so very little compared to that which has been"],[2,836.32,5.48,"accumulated for eons and eons and eons, see."],[2,842.4,7.68,"So, are you still keeping on studying to understand the truth,"],[2,850.08,7.44,"which can be understood at moment of hearing, considering?"],[2,857.52,6.32,"it leads to the deeper understanding, deeper and deeper."],[2,865.52,2.64,"So now, who's the Buddha? See,"],[2,868.16,10.48,"the great virtues of wisdom, beyond anything in all the universes."],[2,878.64,6.6,"Even devas and brahmas came to see Him, to ask questions and so on, to pay respect to Him, see"],[2,886.88,24.56,"At your land, now, India: places like Savatthi, where one understood the meaning of the word;"],[2,911.44,4.24,"so, it's a good opportunity to share the understanding"],[2,915.68,5.76,"with the others - the most precious gift;"],[2,921.44,5.04,"so now, study just one word in order to understand more."],[2,927.04,8.16,"So, not just the word nama-dhamma: two different kinds of nama-dhamma - citta is the chief,"],[2,935.2,4.88,"it's been arising for eons and eons and eons,"],[2,940.08,4.32,"non-stop, just one moment at a time."],[2,944.4,6.96,"As soon as it's gone, it conditions the next one, and that is anantara-paccaya"],[2,951.36,3.28,"- no one can stop the way citta is,"],[2,954.64,4.88,"because as soon as it has fallen away, it conditions the next citta,"],[2,959.52,3.68,"right now, how many minutes? See;"],[2,963.2,6.32,"citta arises and falls away, by way of anantara-paccaya;"],[2,969.52,5.04,"no one can stop paccayas, conditions for whatever arises."],[2,974.56,3.6,"So, the chief of experiencing, the citta,"],[2,978.16,6.16,"and the cetasikas condition the next citta and cetasikas instantly,"],[2,984.32,4.48,"because each one has anantara-paccaya."],[2,989.28,5.76,"So now, we learn about the truth of what is there, little by little;"],[2,995.04,3.76,"we will learn more, not just about citta and cetasikas only,"],[2,998.8,7.76,"but having firm confidence of dhamma and sankhara-dhamma, conditioned reality."],[2,1006.56,5.52,"It needs conditions, sankharas, for its arising;"],[2,1012.08,4.24,"so, whatever is conditioned is sankhara-dhamma."],[2,1016.32,9.04,"So, is hardness sankhara-dhamma? [Yes, Ajahn.]"],[2,1025.36,2.08,"Why? [I don't know the answer.]"],[2,1027.44,2.48,"That's why we're learning, even just the word"],[2,1029.92,5.04,"- we can read about the word, but no understanding."],[2,1034.96,8.48,"We read about dhamma, but if there's no studying, considering, we take dhamma wrongly,"],[2,1043.44,7.6,"not clear at all, very superficially - nama, rupa, that's all;"],[2,1051.04,6.56,"but the truth is that - nothing can arise alone, see,"],[2,1057.6,5.92,"because it needs the right conditions for its arising;"],[2,1063.52,3.6,"and the conditions arises together, too."],[2,1067.12,5.04,"That's why nothing can arise alone, even hardness,"],[2,1072.16,4.0,"it needs the other rupas, maha-bhuta rupas;"],[2,1076.16,2.48,"everyone's heard about these;"],[2,1078.64,2.24,"even hardness cannot arise alone,"],[2,1080.88,4.88,"without the other rupas arising together, supporting each others to arise."],[2,1085.76,9.84,"There are all together four kinds of rupa, as the mahabhuta rupa, the primary rupas"],[2,1095.6,9.04,"- pathavi, tejo, apo, vayo;"],[2,1104.64,6.08,"and you've heard the word about pathavi, it's not just the earth,"],[2,1110.72,4.4,"but it's whatever is hard or soft."],[2,1115.12,4.32,"It's real, it's one of the main primary rupas,"],[2,1119.44,6.96,"for other rupa to arise, like smell, or visible object or color;"],[2,1126.4,4.16,"without the four primary rupas, no other rupas can arise,"],[2,1130.56,3.84,"that's why it is also sankhara-dhamma."],[2,1134.4,4.24,"So, we don't just learn about the word - no understanding,"],[2,1138.64,4.16,"but to understand the meaning of sankhara-dhamma:"],[2,1142.8,4.8,"whatever arises cannot arise alone, what does it mean?"],[2,1147.6,4.4,"There must be other realities arising together,"],[2,1152.0,4.64,"and each conditions the others to arise;"],[2,1156.64,4.96,"that's why pathavi, the hardness, conditions heat and cold,"],[2,1161.6,2.56,"and heat and cold conditions such and such."],[2,1164.16,6.72,"That's why we learn little by little, but have more and firmer understanding;"],[2,1170.88,5.2,"confidence of the truth is more important than just reading and hearing the word"],[2,1176.08,7.64,"without careful considering. So, is there any question?"],[3,5.44,4.24,"[A. Sujin] Have you heard about the subtlety of the Four Noble Truths?"],[3,9.68,6.48,"All of them. All four. But they seem like they are very easy."],[3,16.16,8.48,"Just wanting to have it, so one goes somewhere thinking that he or she will know."],[3,24.64,9.12,"But when is it known? Only when time comes by conditions."],[3,36.74,3.24,"[Lan] Annie wanted to ask what do you mean \"by conditions.\""],[3,40.23,7.1,"[A. Sujin] Yes. Can seeing arise without the eye-base, without the visible object?"],[3,49.52,5.8,"Like for the blind; it is conditioned, each moment."],[3,55.7,7.1,"Hearing needs another condition—not the eye-base, but the ear-base,"],[3,62.8,5.76,"and not the visible object, but sound to impinge on the ear-base."],[3,68.56,6.58,"And when time comes to experience the result of kamma—the cause which has been done,"],[3,76.16,4.15,"it conditions hearing, at its proper time."],[3,81.52,6.94,"No one can change the time and the object for hearing to hear—by conditions."],[3,92.0,5.46,"And when one learns to understand anattaness, one knows that it's true."],[3,99.52,7.18,"That's why all realities are anatta. Not a single one is atta."],[3,130.01,3.43,"There is touching many, many times a day."],[3,133.44,4.81,"Is there any understanding of that which is touched and the touching?"],[3,139.46,9.42,"Or just learning to know that what is touched is soft or hard, hot or cold."],[3,148.88,4.76,"Just learning, but not the direct moment in which it appears,"],[3,154.0,3.36,"to see that it is just that—nothing is there."],[3,158.24,3.2,"And also sound is not there; the eye is not there anymore."],[3,162.16,6.0,"It is only a moment of experiencing through the body. That's all. And that is anatta."],[3,168.72,3.97,"But touching right now without understanding—can be at any moment."],[3,172.96,7.55,"So the difference between no-understanding and developed understanding—it's quite different."],[3,182.01,4.76,"Little by little, stage by stage."],[3,188.2,10.1,"[In the past when touching...] Now, how can there be such understanding?"],[3,201.52,5.89,"[Once I've read about it...] Just reading? Or understanding little by little?"],[3,208.32,6.17,"That is so true. Whenever there is touching, there must be that which is touched."],[3,214.98,3.26,"Only that in that very moment, no other things at all."],[3,218.72,4.9,"Learn to understand that even touching is not self,"],[3,224.08,4.45,"and the object which is touched is also not-self."],[3,229.12,5.59,"Learning at different times, when there are conditions to understand."],[3,235.28,2.4,"But when there are no conditions to understand,"],[3,237.68,6.64,"it's like ordinary life before hearing anything about the truth, at moment of touching."],[3,248.08,3.26,"[Touching experiences the hardness or softness,"],[3,251.68,6.38,"and then the idea of table or hand.] So what is it?"],[3,258.88,8.3,"At the moment of touching, what is the object of touching? What does touching experiences?"],[3,268.24,7.36,"[The hardness.] Okay. Do you think that it's hard, or do you think that it's a table or microphone?"],[3,275.6,3.84,"[The moment after that.] It doesn't matter."],[3,279.44,6.77,"But how can there be the understanding that there is no self who touches?"],[3,287.84,6.27,"Only through hearing, not direct understanding yet, which is satipatthana."],[3,294.64,5.68,"So don't mind at all about sati or satipatthana, just develop understanding,"],[3,300.32,7.05,"and then right understanding can understand whether it's direct understanding or it's only thinking over it."],[3,308.72,8.4,"[Sometimes I think that this is softness or this is hardness because...] The idea takes it for something like sati,"],[3,317.12,6.75,"but it's only the idea of sati, not the moment that realizes that sati is not self."],[3,324.56,3.8,"It's conditioned, no matter how much one tries to have it,"],[3,328.96,3.2,"and that is not the condition for sati to arise,"],[3,332.16,4.96,"and there is no right understanding that sati is anatta."],[3,338.64,4.92,"But when there is more understanding of what is taught,"],[3,344.32,3.19,"then it can condition a moment of sati;"],[3,347.76,6.14,"and then pañña can see the difference between moment with sati and moment without sati."],[3,355.36,6.03,"Otherwise, there is no pañña, only the assumption that it's there when it's not."],[3,362.16,4.64,"Much difference between touching without sati and touching with sati."],[3,368.24,5.12,"When it's touching with sati, there must be the understanding that sati is not I."],[3,373.76,4.83,"It's conditioned. No selection of time or place and object at all."],[3,379.92,6.21,"Like now: there's touching. Is there any understanding?"],[3,387.12,5.27,"Are there conditions to understand it as non—self, or not yet?"],[3,393.92,6.42,"Because there must be understanding of the anattaness of all realities"],[3,401.36,8.46,"before there can be a moment of understanding it as just a moment of experiencing, no—one there."],[3,414.4,8.8,"Can anyone go to a meditation center to gain understanding without any intellectual understanding at all?"],[3,425.6,8.31,"But they go. They don't know what's what. They're taught that that's the way."],[3,435.12,4.08,"But it's not, because it's not in the Teachings at all,"],[3,439.2,6.54,"to have such level of understanding without intellectual understanding."],[3,448.32,1.57,"What is seen now?"],[3,452.88,3.33,"There is seeing, so what is seen?"],[3,458.34,3.82,"[Annie: An object.] What object?"],[3,462.16,4.32,"[Lots and lots of objects.] Something?"],[3,466.48,6.08,"[Yeah, trees.] Trees? Can trees be seen?"],[3,472.56,13.52,"[Yes. Or, well, is it hardness?] Hardness cannot be seen."],[3,486.08,3.68,"So, can there be sati without any understanding?"],[3,489.76,6.0,"To develop more understanding from hearing and considering."],[3,495.76,6.64,"Even what is seen is not known as it is."],[3,505.44,6.72,"Can there be thinking without seeing?"],[3,512.16,5.76,"[Yes.] Yes. And can there be thinking after seeing?"],[3,517.92,7.6,"[Yes.] What's the difference between the two?"],[3,525.52,4.32,"Because thinking is thinking and seeing is seeing."],[3,530.96,6.32,"They arise and fall away very closely; it seems like together."],[3,537.28,7.68,"But actually, a tree cannot be seen—only the visible object, the only reality that can be seen."],[3,544.96,5.52,"We do not have to call it anything, but whenever there is seeing, it's there."],[3,550.48,4.8,"That which can be seen, and after that, there is thinking."],[3,555.28,8.08,"And when there's more and more understanding, sati begins to arise—very weak, very little,"],[3,563.36,7.04,"to understand right now that what is seen is just that which can be seen, a reality."],[3,570.4,6.64,"No one can condition its arising at all, and it arises and falls away."],[3,577.04,1.84,"Who knows? But it's true,"],[3,578.88,4.16,"so it can be proven through the Eightfold Path—one of"],[3,583.04,3.92,"the Four Noble Truths—which is very subtle."],[3,586.96,8.24,"The path is subtle because it is all the way with no attachment."],[3,595.2,4.48,"But when there is attachment to gain or to get, it's not the path"],[3,599.68,9.04,"because there will be more and more attachment instead of less."],[3,608.72,10.56,"And the Teachings of the Buddha are against attachment and ignorance."],[3,619.28,5.04,"Otherwise, nothing could eradicate ignorance and attachment at all."],[3,627.28,4.32,"Without right understanding, little by little,"],[3,631.6,5.2,"from hearing and considering—not waiting, not doing, not wanting, not hoping,"],[3,636.8,5.76,"not doing anything to get direct understanding of any reality appearing now."],[3,644.32,6.8,"Because it needs its own condition, which is a better and deeper understanding."],[3,651.12,2.16,"Like what is seen now."],[3,654.24,10.48,"If there is no beginning of understanding—it's only there when there is seeing."],[3,664.72,5.68,"But without seeing, that which is appearing could not appear, so it cannot be a tree."],[3,670.4,10.56,"It cannot be anything at all. It's that which can be seen. And where is it?"],[3,680.96,1.6,"Where is visible object?"],[3,695.28,9.44,"Without hardness, softness, the four primary rupas, heat and cold, cohesion,"],[3,704.72,3.92,"can there be that which can be seen?"],[3,708.64,5.28,"Because actually, even there are four primary rupas:"],[3,713.92,9.36,"hardness and softness, heat and cold, motion and pressure, and cohesion;"],[3,723.28,5.6,"there are also other realities arising together."],[3,728.88,2.88,"One is that which can be seen."],[3,731.76,6.32,"When it has impinged on the eye-base and only when seeing arises, it's there."],[3,738.08,6.8,"If I take this away, the mahabhuta rupas are taken away along with the visible object."],[3,744.88,6.48,"So visible object is there with the mahabhuta rupas—here it is again."],[3,751.36,6.64,"And not just the visible object, also smell."],[3,758.0,6.64,"Some might not be able to smell, but when it's keen,"],[3,764.64,7.04,"a reality can smell it when it's strong enough to be smelled."],[3,771.68,5.92,"And taste is there too. Taste it."],[3,777.6,10.48,"And then it's just a taste which can be object of the tasting consciousness, a moment of tasting."],[3,788.08,4.64,"Otherwise, the taste, even it's here, cannot be tasted."],[3,792.72,3.68,"Like the taste here and the taste here, everywhere."],[3,797.36,9.36,"And another thing is nutrition. That's why we eat."],[3,808.72,0.96,"Without hearing this,"],[3,809.68,6.4,"how can there be less attachment to what we take to be something permanent?"],[3,816.08,6.96,"Never appearing to arise and fall away—it seems static, always here,"],[3,823.04,6.72,"but actually only pañña, right understanding, developed from hearing and considering,"],[3,829.76,6.56,"knows that it's true and it can be proven; it can be understood directly."],[3,836.32,6.72,"When right understanding develops; not just when \"I want sati to arise,\""],[3,843.04,4.24,"to be mindful of this and that, because that's not the path."],[3,847.28,3.84,"That's not the way to experience the truth of reality."],[3,853.36,7.52,"Only pañña, right understanding, develops."],[3,860.88,7.2,"So pañña is the opposite of attachment and ignorance."],[3,868.08,12.24,"Can anyone have less attachment with ignorance?"],[3,880.32,10.08,"Impossible."],[3,890.4,5.36,"Attachment arises with ignorance."],[3,895.76,4.08,"So without right understanding, ignorance is there"],[3,899.84,6.4,"and ignorance cannot have less attachment"],[3,906.24,2.72,"because they are there together."],[3,911.92,11.84,"Have you had attachment from morning until now or only few moments?"],[3,923.76,11.36,"Very few moments or what? Can you say?"],[3,935.12,4.56,"After seeing, there is ignorance about seeing."],[3,939.68,3.68,"After hearing, there is ignorance."],[3,943.36,9.12,"Ignorance and attachment follow moments of seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting, touching unknowingly"],[3,953.6,11.76,"because it is not as strong as when one does good deeds, ill deeds or ill speech."],[3,965.36,6.24,"By then, one realizes that it's unwholesome, but unwholesomeness is there."],[3,971.6,5.28,"At moment when whatever appears and that object hasn't fallen away yet,"],[3,976.88,6.0,"it can condition ignorance and attachment instantly by accumulation."],[3,982.88,4.56,"Let time come for it to appear, it will appear."],[3,987.44,5.6,"Let time come for it to arise, it will arise. No one can stop."],[3,993.04,3.12,"After seeing, there is ignorance."],[3,996.16,3.92,"But when there is understanding, it begins to develop,"],[3,1000.08,3.12,"and you don't have to call it sati or anything,"],[3,1003.2,11.04,"but it's a different reality from ignorance."],[3,1014.24,5.28,"Otherwise, the Buddha would have taught for 45 years"],[3,1019.52,6.24,"without anyone knowing what He was teaching about."],[3,1025.76,14.56,"But He taught about everything. Not just long, long time ago, but even now—it's true."],[3,1040.32,6.4,"Like seeing is seeing. Tomorrow's seeing will be seeing, not hearing."],[3,1046.72,4.2,"Ignorance is there."],[3,1053.92,2.56,"[Jonothan] And when you say that after seeing and hearing,"],[3,1056.48,2.87,"there's ignorance of what is seen and heard."],[3,1059.35,4.89,"[A. Sujin] It depends on whether it's ignorance, attachment or aversion."],[3,1064.96,5.44,"It can arise after seeing."],[3,1070.4,6.64,"Or it can be goodness, wholesomeness or right understanding, depending on accumulations."],[3,1077.04,5.92,"Like in the time of Buddha, those who had accumulated a lot of right understanding,"],[3,1082.96,8.8,"after seeing, there would be moments of wholesomeness or even kiriya citta for arahatta."],[3,1095.88,4.44,"That's why Buddha told us in detail about how one moment"],[3,1100.32,3.92,"of seeing is followed by which type of citta,"],[3,1104.24,4.72,"what function of citta is there."],[3,1108.96,6.24,"And there can be javana with kusala or akusala"],[3,1115.2,6.32,"before the rupa or the object which is experienced has fallen away."],[3,1121.52,6.08,"But it's unknown because of ignorance."],[3,1127.6,7.92,"So one can understand by oneself how much understanding one has."],[3,1135.52,10.88,"No need to ask anyone—who can know better than you?"],[3,1146.4,5.2,"So what is the Teacher? Who is the Teacher?"],[3,1154.8,3.12,"The person who helps you to understand"],[3,1157.92,6.32,"or the one who tells you to do something without understanding?"],[3,1164.24,2.96,"The Buddha didn't tell anyone to do,"],[3,1167.2,6.96,"but He taught so that others, the listeners, could understand,"],[3,1174.16,16.64,"to have their own understanding, and not just follow someone."],[3,1190.8,14.88,"If someone is asked to go to a meditation center or retreat, shouldn't that person ask what for?"],[3,1205.68,4.0,"To do or to understand?"],[3,1209.68,4.72,"If it's not for understanding, it's useless to go."],[3,1214.4,10.4,"[Sarah] Going to a retreat or going to the temple or spending more time with the monks,"],[3,1224.8,6.48,"not necessarily for understanding, but just to have a break or some quiet time."],[3,1231.28,1.68,"So I think people have different purposes."],[3,1232.96,5.2,"[A. Sujin] No need to have the Buddha's words as refuge"],[3,1238.16,6.64,"because people, anyone, can tell you about \"how to.\""],[3,1244.8,8.64,"Like when you are thirsty: \"have this,\" but you will be thirsty again and again. Endlessly."],[3,1253.44,6.16,"So what's the use?"],[3,1259.6,9.68,"No need for the Buddha then, when there is no understanding."],[3,1269.28,13.2,"This is the difference between the Sammāsambuddho and the others or the other teachers."],[3,1282.48,8.32,"And who is the Great Teacher? The One who can help others to have their own understanding;"],[3,1290.8,4.84,"rather than just being told—no understanding at all."],[3,1296.64,4.48,"[Annie] But I suppose the retreat I went on"],[3,1301.12,9.03,"gave me time to reflect on the cause of my problems and..."],[3,1310.15,4.17,"[A. Sujin] What is the cause of the problems?"],[3,1314.32,7.2,"If you don't know the cause, how can you get rid of it?"],[3,1321.52,3.52,"Without understanding, there must be problems."],[3,1327.04,9.28,"Because problems come from what? [The self.] And ignorance."],[3,1350.08,5.44,"No understanding, no matter external or internal."],[3,1355.52,5.2,"It is just the object of attachment because you like it that way."],[3,1360.72,10.64,"So there's ignorance and attachment all the time."],[3,1384.9,11.5,"More clinging. A better relationship is clinging, right?"],[3,1396.4,9.52,"You just want a better self, right? [Yes.] Still yours, me."],[3,1405.92,10.56,"[Yeah. Wanting something.] No understanding that there is no you in reality, absolute reality."],[3,1416.48,8.32,"So what's better: to understand or just to have what you'd like to have without understanding?"],[3,1426.08,4.95,"What about learning to understand that what appears now is conditioned"],[3,1432.02,1.98,"or not knowing about it at all?"],[3,1435.84,6.88,"And to cling more or have less clinging—what is better?"],[3,1442.72,7.36,"And clinging itself will lead to... disappointment."],[3,1450.08,7.44,"Because it's not the way you like. You want something permanent,"],[3,1457.52,5.92,"and being good, like a good self or myself."],[3,1463.44,4.56,"But actually there isn't anything that can belong to anyone at all."],[3,1468.0,4.72,"Seeing arises, it falls away. It does not belong to anyone."],[3,1472.72,3.44,"Our whole life does not belong to anyone at all."],[3,1476.16,6.96,"It's conditioned to arise and fall away in succession so very rapidly."],[3,1483.12,3.64,"That's why it conditions ignorance and attachment all the time."],[3,1487.76,7.12,"But when there's understanding, it begins to see: what's the use of just arising and falling away?"],[3,1494.88,7.44,"Just experiencing something—without that which can experience there cannot be life"],[3,1502.32,6.24,"because it seems like there are many things: visible object, sound and everything."],[3,1508.56,6.16,"But without that which experiences, there's nothing."],[3,1517.44,2.15,"So it's not you who experiences."],[3,1520.69,10.67,"It's just a reality that is conditioned by the appropriate conditions only."],[3,1531.36,8.24,"[I still feel though that I have to look after myself in this life."],[3,1539.6,6.72,"I have to take responsibility for my actions, and I have to...]"],[3,1546.32,7.52,"You can do anything with right understanding too, not with ignorance as before."],[3,1553.84,7.76,"It doesn't mean that you would change from ignorance to doing nothing."],[3,1561.6,3.76,"But actually, each moment is conditioned."],[3,1565.36,10.68,"That's why the Buddha's followers were not just monks in the old days, also laypeople too."],[3,1576.04,6.28,"Pañña does not belong to anyone."],[3,1582.32,5.2,"There must be conditions for its arising. It arises and falls away too."],[3,1587.52,12.64,"But it develops from moment to moment, and it doesn't hurt to understand correctly, rightly."],[3,1600.16,3.28,"Are you thinking? [Yes.]"],[3,1604.0,3.6,"Can you stop thinking? [No.]"],[3,1607.6,6.64,"There must be conditions for seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting, touching; and thinking."],[3,1614.24,4.48,"No one can stop it, but it depends on—why these people think like this,"],[3,1618.72,10.08,"and others think differently—by conditions, by accumulation; uncontrollable."],[3,1638.8,4.32,"All for myself, when there is noself. [Yes.]"],[3,1643.12,5.12,"It has to be like this as long as there is ignorance."],[3,1648.24,4.96,"But when there is pañña, life is easier than before"],[3,1653.2,9.2,"because pañña never brings trouble. It understands how it happens."],[3,1662.4,3.92,"[Pañña means...] ...Right understanding."],[3,1666.32,13.52,"The best reality in the world—or is it not? What is better than right understanding?"],[3,1679.84,6.96,"What else would you like to have if you have everything?"],[3,1686.8,7.04,"Nothing more, or what? [No, always wanting more.]"],[3,1696.08,9.6,"Enough? Or even if you have everything, it doesn't really belong to you."],[3,1705.68,3.28,"You think that you have it, in your thoughts,"],[3,1708.96,10.4,"but actually does visible object now belong to you? Sound? The body?"],[3,1719.92,4.88,"So is there anything else that is worth having,"],[3,1724.8,7.52,"instead of having everything that one would like to have in life?"],[3,1732.32,5.52,"This is the difference for those who have something to think about,"],[3,1737.84,8.96,"what is life? Is it worthwhile just to be born, have everything, and then die."],[3,1746.8,2.32,"Not being this person anymore,"],[3,1749.12,6.88,"even just for a split second, after the death consciousness arises and falls away."],[3,1756.0,8.48,"But there are conditions for that reality which can experience an object to arise again and again, right now!"],[3,1764.48,4.32,"Or who brought you to this world?"],[3,1768.8,5.76,"How could you know that you would be here in this world?"],[3,1774.56,4.64,"You call it \"this world,\" but in reality, what is the world?"],[3,1779.2,5.04,"No understanding at all, yet everyone has to die,"],[3,1784.24,5.6,"either with ignorance or with understanding."],[3,1789.84,4.56,"And what is better? Ignorance or understanding?"],[3,1794.4,5.76,"So it's just the most precious moment—learning to understand."],[3,1800.16,4.48,"It doesn't mean that you lose everything in life,"],[3,1804.64,4.32,"the self or everything, just by learning or thinking."],[3,1808.96,7.28,"It takes time to really understand each word as it is, like right understanding."],[3,1816.24,6.56,"It's not that just because someone says \"right understanding,\" so it is right understanding. Not at all."],[3,1822.8,7.12,"Understanding what? If it's not this moment in which a reality appears,"],[3,1829.92,4.72,"then there's no understanding. It has to be this moment."],[3,1834.64,5.36,"That which appears should be understood as it is."],[3,1840.0,3.28,"Like seeing—what does it see?"],[3,1843.28,8.84,"We think that we see the world, things and people on the screen, on television, or now, on the Zoom screen."],[3,1854.48,9.04,"But actually it's only visible object along the idea, with ignorance, taking it for something permanent."],[3,1863.52,5.92,"And this should be developed more than having anything else in the world"],[3,1869.44,8.08,"because it can be accumulated from today to other moments in life."],[3,1877.52,4.48,"While other things cannot follow you or belong to you at all,"],[3,1882.0,6.0,"even the body, what you take for my body, my seeing, my hearing, my thinking."],[3,1888.0,4.64,"They are all different conditioned realities."],[3,1892.64,5.76,"Even thinking cannot be controlled by anyone."],[3,1898.4,8.96,"That's the meaning of anatta, non—self; Uncontrollable."],[3,1907.36,3.04,"Is it worthwhile to talk about the truth?"],[3,1910.4,6.08,"It doesn't mean that you can have an understanding of reality right now, so soon;"],[3,1916.48,4.16,"it takes time to really understand what is seen"],[3,1920.64,7.36,"in order to eliminate the idea of something in it, in the visible object."],[3,1928.0,5.84,"No one, like when you look in a mirror—someone seems to be there,"],[3,1933.84,2.68,"but actually no one there."],[3,1937.52,4.71,"[Sarah] Could you say a little more about being courageous?"],[3,1942.23,5.77,"[A. Sujin] Yeah, because you see what you get from the retreat or meditation center?"],[3,1948.0,4.8,"More attachment to the self."],[3,1952.8,7.6,"Who can get rid of the self? No one. Only right understanding, as it begins to develop."],[3,1960.4,5.52,"To see the truth of what appears now."],[3,1965.92,4.56,"Uncontrollable, it does not stay."],[3,1970.48,9.52,"The moment now is not the moment before or the next moment."],[3,1980.0,7.44,"And no one can imagine how short a moment is."],[3,1987.44,10.4,"But it's true, and we can learn to know about realities, absolute realities."],[3,1997.84,8.24,"Do you have friends? [Yeah.] Only when there is thinking."],[3,2006.08,6.72,"Do you have enemies? Only when there is thinking."],[3,2012.8,7.6,"Seeing does not have any enemies or friends at all. Seeing just sees. That's all."],[3,2020.4,6.4,"It arises to see. The function that it performs is seeing."],[3,2026.8,6.24,"No one can change it because it is a reality conditioned"],[3,2033.04,6.8,"by the eye-base, the visible object and other conditions to arise and see."],[3,2039.84,2.72,"No-one there."],[3,2042.56,11.68,"This is way to have less attachment, which will bring less sorrow or disappointment."],[3,2054.24,7.28,"Whenever there is wishing or wanting, what follows? [More sorrow.]"],[3,2061.52,8.48,"But you know whatever comes must be by conditions."],[3,2070.0,7.76,"No understanding of whatever appears, so the self is there."],[3,2077.76,1.12,"Or you have less self."],[3,2079.28,4.88,"[Lan] The idea of self also arises and passes away..."],[3,2084.16,6.96,"[A. Sujin] When? When does it arise? [Anytime.] Now, is it arising?"],[3,2091.12,4.88,"See, we just talk about it, but it can be object of understanding directly,"],[3,2096.0,8.16,"and we call that sati—a reality which can be aware with right understanding."],[3,2104.16,4.56,"Without right understanding, no for awareness to arise at all."],[3,2114.88,5.44,"[Aren't there many conditions for sati to arise?] Certainly."],[3,2120.32,4.16,"When we talk about satipatthana,"],[3,2124.48,8.08,"right understanding of a reality right now, just one at a time."],[3,2132.56,8.56,"Not just talking about stories of many realities, but the direct understanding, direct awareness."],[3,2141.12,5.52,"How many vipassana—ñanas are there? [Is it 16?]"],[3,2146.64,6.36,"See, anyone can say it. What is the first one? [Nama—rupa—pariccheda.]"],[3,2156.08,3.12,"It's not paccaya—pariggaha—ñana, see?"],[3,2159.2,5.0,"That's why there must be the understanding of the characteristic which is not self,"],[3,2164.2,4.6,"that which experiences or that which cannot experience"],[3,2168.8,10.32,"before there can be more understanding of paccaya or conditions, later."],[3,2179.12,5.52,"There must be right understanding of the difference between each one,"],[3,2184.64,6.16,"like this is moment of experiencing hardness, not moment of seeing,"],[3,2190.8,3.92,"experiencing visible object."],[3,2194.72,8.8,"Before knowing or understanding intellectually what the conditions are for each one."],[3,2203.52,3.28,"Why do we talk about conditions?"],[3,2206.8,4.64,"To have the understanding of non—self, little by little."],[3,2211.44,4.08,"But when it's not direct understanding, the self is there."],[3,2215.52,8.64,"So intellectual understanding alone cannot eradicate the idea of self at all. [Yes.]"],[3,2224.16,5.2,"So the understanding of anattaness, not you who can have awareness,"],[3,2229.36,6.4,"but understanding can see moment without awareness and moment with awareness"],[3,2235.76,6.56,"when awareness arises by conditions, not \"I'll try to have it.\""],[3,2242.32,4.72,"[Even having the idea or the intention that I'm trying, or I'm doing, I'm practicing;"],[3,2247.04,3.52,"or \"I'm learning,\" \"I'm listening,\" it's also...] Wrong view, yes."],[3,2250.56,6.24,"[...arising and passing away.] But who knows the arising and falling away? Ignorance cannot."],[3,2256.8,7.92,"Only pañña, at the level of vipassana—ñana, not the first or the second—stage by stage."],[4,4.03,7.16,"[Nina:] Because he said that truthfulness is such a difficult parami because you may mislead yourself."],[4,11.19,5.48,"[A. Sujin:] So what's the purpose of studying and listening to the teachings and realities?"],[4,17.92,3.47,"When there is understanding of reality, can that be the wrong path?"],[4,22.75,2.75,"[Sarah] It's very difficult to know whether it's right or wrong."],[4,25.5,4.18,"[A. Sujin] It is not the word that we are trying to say, whether it's wrong or right path,"],[4,29.68,3.12,"but it's the understanding of realities."],[4,32.8,6.32,"Whenever there is understanding of realities, can we say that that is wrong or the wrong path?"],[4,39.12,3.55,"So it's not just the words to say whether it's wrong or right."],[4,43.44,5.2,"It's just thinking conditioned by pariyatti understanding."],[4,48.64,5.92,"It depends on what one knows about pariyatti — and pariyatti is not the words."],[4,54.56,6.68,"Pariyatti means the Teachings which help one understand the reality that is now appearing."],[4,61.94,4.94,"[Sukin] Right, and whatever appears now conditions thinking."],[4,66.88,6.71,"And it may be just a vague understanding."],[4,73.59,4.17,"[A. Sujin] When it's right, even it's vague, it's right."],[4,77.76,9.6,"For example, when there is the understanding that this moment right now is a dhamma with the characteristic of a reality,"],[4,87.36,3.0,"that cannot be wrong because it's true."],[4,93.24,3.0,"That moment of thinking is right thinking."],[4,96.24,6.29,"So that's why there should be the understanding of moments with satipatthana and without satipatthana."],[4,103.05,6.15,"Otherwise, it's just talking about the four satipatthana without developing satipatthana"],[4,109.2,3.8,"because of not understanding the characteristic of satipatthana."],[4,114.09,5.42,"[Sarah] And here we are in Kuru where the Satipatthana Sutta was taught."],[4,119.51,5.88,"[A. Sujin] Because it's not just about hearing or thinking, but about direct experiencing too."],[4,126.32,5.96,"I think that it's called satipatthana because everything is satipatthana."],[4,134.0,4.48,"No matter it is kaya, vedana, citta or dhamma."],[4,138.48,4.01,"And there are dhammas right now, satipatthana right now."],[4,143.12,4.24,"So the Satipatthana Sutta includes everything which is real."],[4,150.96,6.15,"[Sukin] It's better to know the difference between nama and rupa."],[4,157.83,2.93,"[A. Sujin] To understand their different characteristics."],[4,161.36,4.16,"That which cannot experience anything is here and now"],[4,165.69,3.47,"— the visible object cannot understand anything."],[4,169.6,3.52,"But we don't have to think in words at all."],[4,173.12,4.91,"Just getting used to the characteristic as a reality. That's all."],[4,180.22,4.66,"[Sarah] Higher wisdom can really see the danger of akusala."],[4,184.91,3.04,"[A. Sujin] It depends on the level of pañña,"],[4,188.23,6.01,"because for a person who is developing right understanding to become a sotapanna,"],[4,194.24,3.52,"no time to know whether that is kusala or akusala"],[4,197.76,7.2,"because the manasikara with pañña is attending just to the characteristic of nama which is not self."],[4,206.4,8.16,"Lobha is there, but there is no attention to lobha as lobha, only as a reality — just a reality."],[4,214.56,4.23,"[Jonothan] Ajahn, you said \"lobha is there, but...\" Could you explain?"],[4,218.79,7.53,"[A. Sujin] Because, you see, that person doesn't yet know the characteristics of nama and rupa very clearly,"],[4,226.32,4.32,"and realities arise and fall away so fast, even it's lobha,"],[4,230.64,6.8,"but the characteristic of not-my-lobha, not-myself-but-just-a-reality."],[4,237.44,4.09,"So pañña of that level just attends the characteristic of nama."],[4,242.72,4.61,"Even it is lobha, it doesn't mind at all whether it is lobha or dosa."],[4,247.84,6.5,"Just that characteristic of nama is there, being known that it's not self, just a reality."],[4,255.76,4.83,"No attention to the characteristic of lobha as lobha;"],[4,260.68,2.84,"or to what kind of vedana is there, things like that..."],[4,263.52,3.04,"For example, this is hard, do we have to say anything?"],[4,266.56,5.2,"Because hardness arises and falls away before we can measure it,"],[4,271.76,1.85,"whether it's this level or that level,"],[4,274.03,7.2,"but pañña is just beginning to attend to the characteristic of no-self-in-there. That's all."],[4,281.92,6.72,"In order to be able to differentiate the characteristic of nama from rupa,"],[4,288.64,5.22,"so it can appear without doubt, without avijja at all."],[4,299.44,5.2,"When it's known as lobha, there would be shame of lobha"],[4,304.64,6.64,"because at that moment it has already understood lobha as a nama."],[4,311.28,4.64,"Better than that, deeper than that, subtler than that - so there can be shame."],[4,315.92,4.24,"But at that level, there can only be shame for not knowing lobha as nama yet."],[4,320.16,7.2,"That's why before becoming sakadagami or anagami, there must be the understanding of reality,"],[4,327.36,2.85,"no matter whether it's lobha, dosa or anything."],[4,330.72,4.58,"Nobody can change that, but the attention is just there,"],[4,335.65,4.92,"beginning to know or to get closer to the characteristic of nama as a reality."],[4,341.58,3.48,"[Sukin] With the understanding of dhammas, there are many levels of knowing them."],[4,346.15,2.47,"[A. Sujin] Otherwise, there would only be Arahatta."],[4,348.98,3.42,"For example, we are talking about nama and dhamma now,"],[4,352.4,5.51,"but it depends on whether pañña arises with satipatthana or not,"],[4,357.9,9.14,"and when it arises, whether it's just at the beginning or more advanced, to understand quicker. See, it depends."],[4,373.36,8.8,"[Sarah] You said adhisīla is satipatthana. Does that mean that adhicitta and adhipañña are also satipatthana?"],[4,382.16,5.1,"And at the same time because there cannot be adhisīla without adhicitta."],[4,389.04,6.0,"And we can see the difference between the moment with satipatthana, that it is different from other moments."],[4,395.04,6.65,"That's why it is adhisīla, adhicitta and adhipañña, through direct awareness."],[4,410.16,6.3,"It can be fulfilled at moment of lokuttara to be adhisīla, adhicitta and adhipañña."],[4,417.2,3.87,"But before that there must be moments of development too."],[4,421.92,4.85,"[Sukin] So knowing metta as metta is also adhisīla?"],[4,430.64,1.68,"When it is satipatthana."],[4,433.04,3.68,"It is much more than just knowing by words or by thinking."],[4,436.72,4.06,"So one can see the moment of being directly aware."],[4,446.28,5.08,"Because it is the self who has sīla, while this is the understanding of realities."],[4,452.24,5.76,"So it's much better, seeing even the moment of akusala"],[4,458.0,3.15,"instead of letting it come in through body and speech and then knowing it."],[4,466.24,5.67,"Certainly. That's why there is the prefix adhi — adhisīla, adhicitta."],[4,471.91,3.77,"[It has to do with...] ...Understanding and direct awareness."],[4,483.04,2.34,"Little by little, little by little."],[4,489.13,4.54,"[Azita] This morning I was reading my small book about Paticca Samuppada."],[4,494.31,3.58,"[A. Sujin] Now there is akusala citta, okay?"],[4,498.56,6.36,"Should we talk about the avijja which conditions this akusala citta?"],[4,505.68,2.64,"So we can begin with anything."],[4,508.32,5.01,"It doesn't mean that there must be avijja, and then later sankhara."],[4,514.08,4.92,"But we can talk about avijja, and we know avijja arises with each akusala."],[4,519.44,4.41,"And when we talk about akusala, we know that there is avijja as condition."],[4,525.68,6.16,"We have to talk about them one at a time, but they go together, arise together."],[4,532.4,5.36,"[So each part of that...] It's there; it depends on whether you would talk about phassa."],[4,537.76,3.88,"Because you see when it is akusala citta, there must be phassa."],[4,542.57,5.11,"So we don't have to wait before talking about phassa."],[4,547.68,2.0,"But we can talk about phassa."],[4,549.68,3.2,"So that's why the Buddha talked about avijja conditions sankhara,"],[4,552.88,5.04,"and then the other way around: from here to there, from there to here."],[4,557.92,8.48,"See, or from the middle — even right now, there is phassa which conditions tanha or lobha."],[4,570.48,7.28,"I think that with the understanding of realities, whenever you read whatever, you will understand."],[4,577.76,4.16,"But when there is no understanding of reality so well,"],[4,581.92,8.64,"we have doubts about this subject, paticca samuppada or the noble truths and so on."],[4,590.56,3.76,"But when there is the understanding of realities, no doubt."],[4,594.32,3.6,"No matter we talk about this subject or other subjects,"],[4,597.92,3.02,"the same thing — must be about realities."],[5,6.04,5.01,"[T. Bach] So, Ajahn, Sister Hua asked about the kinds of khanti (patience)."],[5,11.39,2.85,"From what I heard, it is khanti-ñāṇa."],[5,14.24,3.75,"Could you please tell us more about these?"],[5,20.79,2.84,"[A. Sujin] What is khanti again?"],[5,28.8,4.42,"A reality. What is it?"],[5,42.16,6.43,"So if it is just a few moments of khanti,"],[5,49.28,7.19,"can it develop to the degree that it can understand the truth of what is there, as we have heard?"],[5,57.16,5.55,"Like, what arises falls away instantly, for example."],[5,67.36,7.23,"Is that ñāṇa or not ñāṇa yet? And what is meant by ñāṇa?"],[5,80.5,7.37,"Okay. So if there is not the habit of khanti, a little more, a little more,"],[5,88.51,7.03,"to understand the truth little by little until it's so firm, it cannot be ñāṇa yet."],[5,96.72,5.26,"For the first round of the Ariya Saccas, it's not vipassana-ñāṇa."],[5,102.78,6.43,"But without khanti, without the understanding of the truth,"],[5,110.23,6.5,"khanti not to do something different, but to develop the understanding of the truth,"],[5,117.42,5.46,"can there be the degree of understanding which can realize the truth?"],[5,127.12,1.72,"Not at all, right?"],[5,131.12,8.59,"For example, now, if there is no considering or discussing the truth of this moment,"],[5,140.24,6.88,"can that be ñāṇa to realize the truth? Not yet. Not at all."],[5,147.12,1.51,"That is why: how long will it take?"],[5,148.66,6.7,"And that is khanti, each moment of understanding that the truth is right here and now,"],[5,155.36,1.55,"but it's not known yet."],[5,157.82,4.74,"So without hearing it again, considering it again,"],[5,162.56,6.47,"there can never be getting closer to understanding or realizing the truth of this moment at all."],[5,169.59,2.96,"Isn't that khanti with pañña?"],[5,172.56,6.75,"Developing on and on and on to understand the truth, stage by stage."],[5,182.88,6.39,"So it's just right understanding conditioning, a little more khanti on and on and on."],[5,190.16,6.16,"Without right understanding at all, there cannot be khanti to hear it again,"],[5,196.32,5.2,"to consider it again, to let go it again, gradually"],[5,201.52,11.68,"until the truth appears to ñāṇa, not just the first round of the Ariya Saccas."],[5,213.2,6.8,"Is it true? When that hasn't happened yet, what is it now?"],[5,220.0,4.72,"It can be known: without khanti, without understanding,"],[5,224.72,2.88,"how can it develop moment to moment"],[5,227.6,5.6,"to be able to penetrate the truth of what is there,"],[5,233.2,7.52,"which is experienced and has just gone instantly?"],[5,240.72,8.64,"The truth can be realized when there is more khanti, firm confidence in the truth,"],[5,249.36,5.2,"not doing anything else, but listening again and again."],[5,254.56,3.84,"And the more there is understanding the more khanti gradually develops"],[5,258.4,5.52,"- so much khanti for the first round to become the second round -"],[5,263.92,2.16,"because it has to be unexpected."],[5,271.68,5.36,"So samma-sati of the Eightfold Path is there instantly,"],[5,277.04,6.32,"conditioned by the understanding of the object which is there."],[5,283.36,7.44,"So it can develop understanding of the truth as it is, little by little."],[5,290.8,10.24,"How come for visible object to appear as no one, not anything? See, the ultimate truth."],[5,301.04,8.4,"It takes khanti with right understanding."],[5,309.44,6.88,"Without expectation, because at the moment of expecting, it is lobha."],[5,316.32,5.28,"It hinders instantly."],[5,325.84,7.2,"So it's the development of right understanding now that will become khanti-ñāṇa."],[5,333.04,7.36,"And each moment of understanding the truth shows that it is so very, very subtle."],[5,340.4,3.36,"It becomes a habit, adhivasana-khanti."],[5,347.12,4.24,"Not just one or two weeks or years,"],[5,351.36,9.2,"but uncountable moments of khanti for the development of understanding."],[5,360.56,11.12,"As habit of doing nothing else. Not doing anything, not trying to do other things,"],[5,371.68,7.12,"but understanding the words of truth, which are so very deep."],[5,378.8,6.48,"Hearing again about that which is seen, again and again."],[5,385.28,6.8,"There is no way to experience it as it is without khanti"],[5,392.08,4.56,"until it becomes the habit of developing right understanding,"],[5,396.64,5.12,"the ñāṇa which can experience the truth of it."],[5,401.76,3.55,"So these are just words, but the truth is now."],[5,405.31,5.17,"Is there khanti enough to know that it's so far,"],[5,410.48,4.8,"the experiencing of that which is seen now as it is?"],[5,415.28,6.0,"No one at all. No Khun Tam Bach. See? See?"],[5,421.28,8.0,"No table. Not anything at all - adhivasana-khanti."],[5,429.28,8.08,"And more than that, even right understanding at the degree of the first vipassana-ñāṇa,"],[5,437.36,7.44,"is never enough, and so far away from the strong ones because it's just taruna-vipassana."],[5,444.8,0.88,"It's still weak,"],[5,446.03,9.25,"not strong enough to experience the arising and falling away of nama and rupa clearly."],[5,455.28,8.8,"So now it's not clear at all when we talk about how what is there has arisen and gone instantly."],[5,464.08,4.96,"But right understanding is not enough to experience that."],[5,469.04,7.52,"So the truth is not as clear as vipassana-ñāṇa."],[5,476.56,6.64,"From adhivasana-khanti until it is khanti-ñāṇa."],[5,483.2,5.92,"Without khanti, that ñāṇa cannot arise at all."],[5,489.12,12.48,"So khanti-ñāṇa is not doing anything at all, just understanding a little more."],[5,501.6,7.36,"With right understanding, developing on and on, little by little, so very little."],[5,508.96,6.52,"But each moment conditions a little more understanding, getting closer to the truth."],[5,516.48,8.48,"When there is firm confidence in the dhammas, which are so very subtle."],[5,524.96,6.96,"For example, that which is seen does not appear as it is."],[5,531.92,2.32,"Be true to the truth."],[5,534.24,4.8,"When pañña, which has been developed through khanti,"],[5,539.04,6.84,"before there can be the khanti of the third round, there must be the khanti of the first round."],[5,546.48,7.36,"With right understanding of the truth of Dhamma, of that very moment, not just the word."],[5,553.84,13.2,"So even doubt is real. It requires so much khanti to understand doubt as not I at all. See?"],[5,567.04,6.88,"Until then, how much khanti is needed to understand not just doubt,"],[5,573.92,9.52,"but anything now as it is. No selection. All are dhammas, all are anatta. Great patience."],[5,583.44,5.2,"Even if it is not yet the khanti-ñāṇa of vipassana-ñāṇa, the third round."],[5,588.64,5.44,"But it is the beginning of being so khanti."],[5,594.08,5.74,"Not to count, not to hope, not to wish, not to try."],[5,600.99,10.91,"But careful considering is the only factor or condition to understand the truth as it is, as dhamma."],[5,613.76,7.84,"So now, what appears when there is the awareness or direct understanding,"],[5,621.6,2.64,"it is just a reality."],[5,624.24,6.08,"No need to say it's that which experiences or that which cannot experience"],[5,630.32,9.2,"because the characteristic of that shows up as it is: hardness. See? No word. It's there."],[5,639.52,3.68,"Not that which experiences hardness."],[5,643.2,9.36,"And hardness cannot be my head, my toe, my arm at all. Hardness is just hardness."],[5,654.0,7.04,"So many moments experiencing that which has arisen and fallen away instantly."],[5,661.04,9.2,"That's why the question can be: where is seeing? See?"],[5,670.24,6.32,"In the plane of the five khandhas, rupa is there as the base for seeing to arise."],[5,677.2,8.74,"No thought about it, until even that which is a condition for seeing also arises, only to fall away."],[5,686.4,5.2,"Not anyone at all from head to toe."],[5,691.6,3.12,"Is that true? Dhamma?"],[5,695.53,4.38,"Is there any patience to understand more and more firmly"],[5,700.76,4.84,"that what is there has arisen and gone unknowingly?"],[5,706.56,5.04,"No matter what, the eye base or that which impinges on it,"],[5,711.6,4.8,"the seeing or that which is seen, all have gone."],[5,716.4,3.84,"Is there patience enough not to do anything?"],[5,720.24,8.88,"Doubt is there. No understanding of doubt as just a reality, not anyone's doubt at all."],[5,729.12,4.6,"So whatever is taken for me, instantly, by conditions"],[5,733.72,5.08,"- the accumulation of wrong understanding and ignorance -"],[5,738.8,7.28,"can there be letting go of that? Little by little."],[5,746.08,6.96,"Great patience. Listening, considering, and developing at any time,"],[5,753.04,7.36,"understanding the difference between the first round of the Ariya Saccas and the second round,"],[5,760.4,3.92,"how much khanti is there?"],[5,764.32,9.76,"Not to do anything, not trying to do anything, but carefully considering the truth."],[5,774.08,7.12,"So there can be the instant awareness with right understanding of what is there right now."],[5,781.2,4.08,"We are not just talking about them in words,"],[5,785.28,5.28,"but they are there arising and falling away all the time."],[5,790.56,8.48,"And great khanti, from the first round of the First Ariya Sacca to become the second round."],[5,799.04,4.4,"So great, and greater, and greater, and greater,"],[5,803.44,7.92,"to let go even of the very slight attachment to the idea of something and someone"],[5,811.36,7.56,"which appear now as someone and something."],[5,819.52,6.0,"So no matter what word we use for khanti: khanti-ñāṇa, adhivasana-khanti, or whatever,"],[5,825.52,7.68,"it depends on patience to understand the truth and to be true to the truth."],[5,833.2,8.16,"How much - or how little - understanding of what is there compared to the way it is?"],[5,841.36,16.91,"How long will it take to let go of the idea of self, or someone seen, or something seen, all day,"],[5,858.27,9.49,"all life, all moments in one's life. Khanti is there, isn't it?"],[5,876.96,12.8,"So now, a little more understanding of khanti, not as self or anyone."],[5,894.56,4.32,"That's why there are many degrees of khanti."],[5,898.88,4.32,"So very little now compared to the great khanti to realize the truth."],[5,912.0,9.68,"No doubt now about different words for different degrees of khanti..."],[6,4.4,3.5,"[Vincent] There's a question about the soul."],[6,10.64,2.01,"[A. Sujin] Is there soul now?"],[6,18.96,2.46,"When there is the understanding of citta —"],[6,22.0,4.96,"the reality which experiences the object, no matter what words we use,"],[6,26.96,4.45,"but it has to be right understanding of the reality of that,"],[6,31.76,2.88,"which is what we are talking about."],[6,35.84,3.68,"So, no matter what idea about the soul we had before,"],[6,39.52,5.76,"the truth is that soul, since we use that word, means that reality,"],[6,46.02,1.82,"like that which experiences the object."],[6,47.84,5.9,"And in Pali terms, the words of the Buddha, that word is citta."],[6,54.72,6.93,"Otherwise, the words of the Buddha about citta can be mixed with the idea of soul as before."],[6,63.84,8.86,"That's why we have to have a clear understanding of the reality which we are talking about."],[6,73.68,9.17,"Is citta soul? [Da Zhuang somehow said that kamma is the intention, the cetana.]"],[6,83.84,6.48,"But we're talking about just one word at a time which represents only one reality at a time,"],[6,90.32,3.51,"in order to have a clearer understanding of that reality,"],[6,93.98,7.64,"in order to understand clearly any reality later, one by one."],[6,103.52,4.08,"We are talking about the truth of each reality."],[6,107.6,5.77,"What is kamma? Is kamma citta, or is kamma a soul?"],[6,115.34,6.88,"Is kamma soul? [Not sure; it's not clear if kamma is soul or not.]"],[6,122.72,2.52,"That's why we have to understand the reality."],[6,126.16,2.4,"Each one has its own characteristic."],[6,128.96,2.02,"It cannot be the other at all."],[6,131.68,4.03,"Each has its own characteristic to be different from the others"],[6,136.05,3.27,"because whatever is real is dhamma."],[6,140.24,2.75,"Each one which is real is a dhamma."],[6,153.26,3.35,"No. There is no understanding of kamma."],[6,157.28,4.36,"That's why there's the idea of kamma here and kamma there, and so on."],[6,161.88,8.12,"But what is it? Is there kamma right now? [He is not clear about what cetana is.]"],[6,171.47,8.13,"Okay. Shall we begin with whether cetana is dhamma or not? [Not quite sure.]"],[6,179.6,4.64,"That's why we have to have a clear understanding of reality,"],[6,184.24,5.44,"in order to understand the truth that they are realities;"],[6,189.68,4.25,"they have their own characteristics; each one is different."],[6,199.44,5.31,"Is it a dhamma? [Yes, we call that dhamma.]"],[6,205.12,5.24,"We call it *that*, or it has its own characteristic, to be a reality."],[6,215.16,5.55,"Okay. Can it experience an object? [Yes.]"],[6,221.03,3.06,"Is there cetana at the moment of seeing?"],[6,229.2,3.76,"That's why we cannot talk about cetana further if there's"],[6,232.96,4.13,"not a clear understanding of what cetana really is."],[6,240.44,5.56,"Dhamma is so very subtle; it's so deep that there has to be very"],[6,246.0,5.2,"careful consideration of one reality at a time"],[6,251.2,5.21,"to have more understanding of \"no-one-there-at-all.\""],[6,256.71,2.04,"Each one is a different dhamma."],[6,260.59,6.61,"So, doesn't cetana also experience the object, but not as the chief,"],[6,267.2,5.28,"because it is not the reality which experiences the object clearly?"],[6,275.92,3.37,"And this is the difference between the citta"],[6,279.61,4.07,"and the reality which arises with it, shares the same object,"],[6,283.68,3.6,"but has a different characteristic and a different function."],[6,287.28,3.96,"And they also experience the object, but not as the chief."],[6,293.76,5.39,"That's why there are two kinds of reality which experience the object."],[6,300.07,4.73,"Only one can be that which experiences the object clearly."],[6,304.8,5.41,"It's conditioned to arise to see clearly the object which is seen."],[6,311.92,7.03,"But the other realities, which also experience the same object, arising together,"],[6,320.24,4.8,"each one cannot perform the function of that which experiences the object clearly."],[6,325.04,3.56,"So they are cetasikas, not citta."],[6,330.13,5.01,"So, does cetana also experience the object? What object?"],[6,343.73,4.96,"At the moment when anger is there, doesn't it experience its object?"],[6,349.68,3.08,"Now we're talking about another reality, not cetana."],[6,353.31,6.74,"Is anger or irritation a reality? [Yes.]"],[6,360.93,8.84,"At the moment of getting angry, doesn't anger also experience an object? [Maybe.]"],[6,369.89,12.59,"Not maybe. At all. It has to be precise about each reality; otherwise, they're all mixed up."],[6,389.63,3.81,"So, each reality is so very subtle."],[6,393.44,3.37,"When it's so slight, very weak,"],[6,397.38,5.98,"it cannot appear to be known to very little understanding."],[6,403.36,6.24,"That's why we learn to understand each reality — to understand it,"],[6,409.6,3.48,"no matter whether it arises this moment or at other moments."],[6,413.32,5.16,"So, doesn't cetana arise with each citta, at each moment, now?"],[6,425.81,2.98,"Right. But we have to proceed little by little,"],[6,429.2,5.58,"to understand a little more about not only intention or cetana."],[6,435.01,7.96,"Is there memory now, remembering? [Yes, there is.]"],[6,443.61,5.67,"Okay. What is the function of memory? [To mark, to memorize.]"],[6,450.17,6.31,"Okay. And what about the feeling now? Isn't it there too? [Yes.]"],[6,457.36,3.25,"So, we begin to understand little by little."],[6,460.87,5.61,"Cetana is the will, or the willing to coordinate the other cetasikas"],[6,466.48,6.28,"to perform their functions — the intention to coordinate;"],[6,474.48,6.48,"so it appears as the will or intention to do something when it's there, clearer."],[6,481.68,6.25,"Just like, \"What are you going to do today?\" See, that is intention or cetana."],[6,489.6,9.6,"So when it arises with each citta, it coordinates, like it wills to do or intends to do:"],[6,499.2,5.28,"the eyes are closed, and then the eyes open;"],[6,504.48,5.12,"what is there to open the eyes?"],[6,509.6,2.48,"Is there any will?"],[6,512.08,3.12,"Isn't it related to will by coordinating the"],[6,515.2,6.96,"other cetasikas to perform their own functions? [Yes, there is.]"],[6,522.16,7.2,"That's why it's there unknown, because only one reality can be known at a time."],[6,529.36,6.16,"Even there is cetana now, saññā now, feeling now, other cetasikas now,"],[6,535.52,6.4,"what can be known is only when it is the object of citta."],[6,541.92,4.16,"That's why there are so many different realities;"],[6,546.08,5.12,"those which experience the object are quite different by"],[6,551.2,8.64,"their characteristics and the level they perform."],[6,559.84,7.6,"The intention to kill, the intention to help — that is cetana."],[6,567.44,9.2,"So cetana arises with each citta, performing its function at different moments."],[6,577.84,10.0,"So, is there cetana at the moment of speaking, walking, doing, or sitting?"],[6,587.84,4.8,"And furthermore, can cetana be the path leading"],[6,592.64,8.88,"to understanding the truth of what is there right now as it is? [It cannot.]"],[6,601.52,14.24,"Okay. Is he sure now that cetana arises with each citta?"],[7,3.48,2.25,"[Vincent:] ...because there's no one, no thing."],[7,12.83,2.49,"That's why: no doubt anymore."],[7,16.96,3.99,"So there's no one, but there is seeing right now, isn't there?"],[7,22.86,5.13,"Can seeing be anyone? [Seeing is just seeing.]"],[7,29.17,8.4,"Why can seeing not be anyone? [Because it's just a conditioned dhamma.]"],[7,38.0,8.0,"So it's there by conditions. It arises and is gone instantly, doesn't it?"],[7,47.0,3.61,"That's why it cannot be anyone at all."],[7,52.0,8.0,"There are realities which arise and fall away: seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting, touching—anything."],[7,61.0,5.15,"All of them are different dhammas, different realities, not anyone at all."],[7,68.27,4.31,"Isn't it true that seeing has arisen now and is gone?"],[7,85.0,3.98,"Isn't that moment real?"],[7,89.86,6.98,"Isn't the idea of \"I see\" when there's seeing—isn't that idea real?"],[7,102.8,3.09,"So, there is imagination, isn't there?"],[7,107.83,5.64,"Isn't it just thinking after seeing?"],[7,115.28,3.3,"So, isn't imagination real?"],[7,118.61,3.76,"Or, in other words, isn't it a moment of thinking?"],[7,123.14,7.44,"At the moment of seeing, can there be thinking as well, experiencing the visible object together with seeing?"],[7,136.44,9.77,"So, where are \"you\"—in seeing or thinking? [The \"I\" is imagined.]"],[7,147.0,6.17,"So, at the moment of seeing, there is the idea of \"I see.\" Is that right?"],[7,154.49,7.51,"Can seeing be \"I,\" or is seeing just seeing—not thinking, not an idea?"],[7,164.41,7.57,"So there are many different moments: seeing, hearing, thinking about \"I see\" and \"I hear,\" and so on."],[7,172.33,7.67,"That's why we learn to understand each different moment, which is conditioned just to arise—and it falls away."],[7,185.0,3.98,"That's why—be true to the truth, little by little."],[7,189.48,5.5,"Learn to become the understanding person, or the reality"],[7,195.0,4.89,"which can understand the truth of what is there, firmer and firmer."],[7,201.61,3.91,"Seeing just a moment ago—gone. Thinking just a moment ago—gone."],[7,205.58,2.39,"Each moment arises and is gone instantly."],[7,208.64,4.66,"That's why the idea of \"I\" is not right at all."],[7,213.54,5.25,"It's wrong understanding—another reality, not anyone."],[7,220.0,5.98,"That's why we discuss what is there right now as it is, little by little."],[7,226.88,5.04,"No matter what moment, it's there by conditions; no one's there at all."],[7,233.52,8.2,"So is it Irene's life, or just that which is conditioned to arise-and then it falls, by conditions only?"],[7,242.85,7.12,"From birth to death. From the moment of birth, it's taken for \"Irene\" until the moment of death."],[7,250.0,2.98,"Where will Irene be afterward?"],[7,255.31,5.46,"So seeing is seeing, hearing is hearing, thinking is thinking, liking is liking."],[7,261.0,6.37,"All are different moments of that which is conditioned, arising and falling away instantly."],[7,269.04,8.97,"Seeing is there now... ignorance, no understanding of the truth of what seeing is, for just a split-second moment... then gone,"],[7,278.49,7.51,"conditioning the idea, taking that which experiences objects as \"I\" all the time."],[7,287.0,5.37,"That's why we learn about what is there in life from moment to moment."],[7,293.57,4.86,"What is real is real. It's a dhamma, not anyone at all."],[7,299.64,4.66,"So, isn't it true that, from birth to death, it's the way dhamma is—"],[7,304.46,7.54,"conditioned to arise and then fall away, different moments by different conditions, until the end, death?"],[7,313.0,5.12,"Seeing arises and is gone. Can we say it's born and dies?"],[7,319.0,8.45,"Because each moment is gone, never to arise again, like death."],[7,328.84,3.93,"So, it's not Irene at all; it's just arising and dying."],[7,333.43,6.4,"But it's by conditions, no matter what follows this moment on and on, quickly."],[7,340.48,4.68,"Be true to the truth from now on, little by little, each moment."],[7,346.34,6.11,"No one is there now, but seeing arises and sees, so seeing is a reality."],[7,352.72,2.87,"No one is there, because it's gone instantly."],[7,356.4,7.58,"But if there isn't more careful consideration of the truth, there still will be the idea of \"I,\""],[7,364.0,5.98,"because of not understanding the reality of seeing or anything from moment to moment."],[7,370.83,5.82,"So, learn again and again to understand a little more of the truth of seeing,"],[7,376.97,6.17,"otherwise there will never be moments of understanding seeing as not \"I\" at all."],[7,384.44,4.8,"As long as there's no attention to the nature, the truth of seeing,"],[7,389.71,4.68,"there needs to be the moment of discussing seeing on and on,"],[7,395.0,6.98,"until it conditions the moment of attending gradually to the reality which sees"],[7,402.0,6.3,"as—it's just a reality which experiences an object."],[7,409.39,4.98,"Because only saying that seeing is not \"I,\" and that it's conditioned to arise and fall away,"],[7,414.77,5.01,"is not enough to let go of the idea \"I see.\""],[7,420.75,3.3,"How long have ignorance and the idea of self been there?"],[7,424.58,7.49,"For eons and eons, at every moment—seeing, hearing, smelling, on and on, up to now."],[7,433.75,2.95,"And there's not just one moment of seeing."],[7,436.85,8.52,"So many different moments need to be learned to understand the truth of dhamma, not anyone."],[7,446.0,7.43,"Each dhamma is real; it has its own characteristic to be realized when the time comes,"],[7,453.69,2.64,"when paññā has developed to that degree."],[7,458.39,6.22,"So it's time to learn more about what is there, to understand the truth of it."],[7,466.25,5.72,"Because it's so real that it can be realized,"],[7,472.0,6.72,"not by ignorance, but by a little more understanding of the truth, stage by stage."],[7,480.38,6.52,"Just hearing about seeing, as we are hearing right now, is not enough to realize the truth."],[7,488.0,4.99,"That's why we learn a little more about the truth of what is there right now,"],[7,494.33,3.35,"at any moment, to have firm confidence in the truth:"],[7,497.94,5.27,"it cannot be taken for anything; no atta at all."],[7,510.0,7.94,"Is there sense of self now? [Yes.]"],[7,518.69,5.39,"Is it real? [Dazhuang said - that which thinks is real.]"],[7,524.32,8.66,"So, it's sense of self after seeing, isn't it? Instantly, unknowingly;"],[7,533.27,2.99,"that's why we learn to understand that"],[7,536.44,3.98,"because of ignorance, not understanding the truth of seeing"],[7,540.52,4.14,"as just the moment of that which is conditioned to see,"],[7,545.25,2.88,"the idea of self is there instantly."],[7,549.0,3.72,"But it's so very, very subtle that no one is able to know it."],[7,554.0,5.27,"And that's the reality of that which is so very subtle, āsava:"],[7,559.3,4.69,"ditthāsava, avijjāsava, bhavāsava are there."],[7,565.96,6.54,"There are many degrees of akusala dhamma; no matter what kind of dhamma, there are many degrees."],[7,574.0,8.45,"The accumulation—the latent tendencies of that which has arisen after seeing and hearing without understanding—"],[7,582.64,5.4,"is accumulated for eons and eons up to now, in citta."],[7,590.0,6.28,"When there's no right condition for anything to arise, that reality cannot arise,"],[7,596.58,5.25,"but it's there, ready to come out, ready to arise."],[7,603.1,3.38,"As soon as one wakes up in the morning, it's there,"],[7,606.68,7.32,"ready to arise, to be the very, very subtle attachment to the idea of self."],[7,615.0,8.96,"The idea that something is there, atta, is there after seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting, touching, and thinking in life."],[7,625.24,4.98,"Until the enlightenment of the Buddha, enlightened to the truth of everything,"],[7,630.35,3.62,"what he said was just about each moment in life."],[7,634.48,5.04,"What is there? While one is asleep, what is there?"],[7,639.78,1.89,"While one wakes up, what is there?"],[7,641.85,2.94,"At the moment of seeing, what's there? And so on."],[7,644.82,6.25,"Otherwise, there cannot be any understanding of what is there at all as it is."],[7,653.0,8.8,"What about ignorance? It arises; it cannot understand the truth of what is there,"],[7,662.62,5.92,"so it is avijjāsava: no understanding of anything appearing at all."],[7,670.63,4.34,"So this is the sense of self, unknown,"],[7,675.77,7.23,"after seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting, touching, thinking, liking, and disliking."],[7,685.57,10.76,"So be true to the truth. Is there any understanding of seeing right now? [Yes, there is.]"],[7,696.8,7.2,"Understanding or no understanding of seeing? [Yes, there is understanding.]"],[7,705.0,3.72,"Of what? [Of seeing.]"],[7,709.24,11.32,"How so? By thinking, considering, or what? [Through learning, hearing the teaching, and studying the teaching.]"],[7,720.85,7.43,"Isn't the sense of self there, too? [At the moment of understanding, there's no sense of \"I.\"]"],[7,730.0,3.98,"But right now, seeing is there."],[7,734.0,8.8,"Is there the sense of self or the understanding of the reality which sees as not-self?"],[7,744.48,3.52,"So there is no understanding of seeing, right?"],[7,749.39,5.79,"So there is the idea, the sense of self, \"I see\" right now."],[7,772.0,5.98,"Only at moments of understanding, not other moments."],[7,778.0,6.42,"At other moments, it is still \"I see\" because understanding is not strong enough."],[7,786.44,5.52,"So, what did the Buddha say again and again? The three rounds of the four noble truths."],[7,793.37,5.87,"That's why we learn to understand each moment as different realities."],[7,801.0,7.17,"Can there be sense of self at the moment of seeing, together? [No.]"],[7,809.58,8.14,"And what about that which is seen—is it something? [What is seen is just color.]"],[7,819.03,13.09,"Can there be anyone like Dazhuang or Vincent in it? [Now, Dazhuang's reply is: Dazhuang's visible object is seen.]"],[7,833.77,7.23,"No, visible object is visible object—not anyone, not Dazhuang, not Sujin, not Vincent."],[7,843.0,6.64,"That's why we learn a little more about what it is, where it is, how it comes to be seen, and so on."],[7,849.85,6.13,"Without the four primary rupas, could there be that which is seen?"],[7,861.38,5.14,"That's the answer, right? All by conditions."],[7,866.76,10.29,"That's why everything is a dhamma; no one is there at all. [Dazhuang still had the idea that there must be someone or something there.]"],[7,877.58,13.04,"So, who is that person? Where is that one? [Okay. Ajahn, Dazhuang said they're just names.]"],[7,891.0,5.98,"Is visible object now Dazhuang? [No.]"],[7,897.0,2.98,"That's why we have firm confidence of the truth:"],[7,900.61,11.49,"that which appears to seeing is only the reality which can appear as visible object right now."],[7,912.36,3.23,"Seeing is only one doorway; no one is there at all."],[7,917.81,8.99,"So the sense of self is there instantly, taking that which is seen as Vincent or someone else."],[7,931.64,7.95,"Is there sense of self now? Again and again. [Yes.]"],[7,940.0,6.88,"Is it real? [Dazhuang asked, \"What does real mean?\"]"],[7,948.42,11.31,"Is it there or not at all? [Dazhuang's still not sure...] Isn't the sense of self a reality?"],[7,961.0,10.36,"Is there any sense of self now? [\"I\" is just an idea, but there must be dhamma there to have this idea.]"],[7,972.0,5.97,"So, isn't idea a dhamma? [Idea is not dhamma.]"],[7,978.69,4.28,"So, no idea! But there are so many ideas."],[7,983.52,7.04,"How can it not be a reality? How can it not be real? It's so real when it's there."],[7,991.97,6.01,"We're just talking about the sense of self because some mentioned the sense of self."],[7,998.0,6.48,"Doesn't everyone acknowledge that there is sense of self or there is no sense of self at all?"],[7,1006.49,3.47,"So, what about the sense of self?"],[7,1011.09,5.33,"Isn't it real? Isn't it a reality? Isn't it now? [Ajahn, sense of self is an idea.]"],[7,1018.08,10.26,"It doesn't matter whether it's an idea or what. Is it real? Is it a reality? [No.]"],[7,1029.66,2.29,"So, there's no sense of self?"],[7,1035.88,5.89,"The truth is the truth. [Uh...] Yes, go on, please. [Ajahn, please go ahead.]"],[7,1042.31,4.12,"We are learning about the truth, the ultimate truth as it is."],[7,1046.77,4.59,"That's why it's so very delicate, very subtle, and intricate."],[7,1051.91,6.07,"That's why it's not just the words we learn and remember and can follow anytime to give an answer."],[7,1058.19,8.18,"But understanding is very important, even regarding the sense of self and the idea of self and so on."],[7,1070.0,7.98,"All dhammas are so very subtle. It has to be one's own understanding, one's own consideration."],[7,1078.55,3.42,"Otherwise, there can never be the understanding of the truth—"],[7,1082.29,4.41,"of the truth at all, rather than just about the idea."],[7,1090.34,5.01,"So what about the idea of self and the sense of self?"],[7,1095.77,5.22,"We'll continue next time. Sawadee ka. [Sawadee krab, Ajahn.]"],[8,5.75,9.11,"[Tam B.] The question of the Sister concerns the four kinds of sampajañña, clear comprehension."],[8,16.23,5.11,"[A. Sujin] Each word should be considered and reconsidered,"],[8,21.75,2.57,"until it's clearer and clearer;"],[8,24.32,3.28,"so, what is the clear comprehension?"],[8,27.6,6.72,"See, it's not just the word, it's not just the text,"],[8,34.32,4.16,"but the clear comprehension of what?"],[8,38.48,4.61,"And what is the clear comprehension? See,"],[8,45.84,9.49,"meaning that - now - is there clear comprehension of what appears - now - or not yet?"],[8,56.0,7.27,"And so, what should be there at moment of clear comprehension of that which is appearing?"],[8,64.96,3.73,"So, what is clear comprehension? Right understanding, isn't it?"],[8,70.72,3.56,"And there are many levels of right understanding,"],[8,74.66,5.98,"just saying - citta is the chief of experiencing the object,"],[8,81.76,3.54,"can't that bring clearer understanding, little by little,"],[8,85.64,5.53,"until that is so clear, whether it's known or not yet,"],[8,91.2,3.92,"even we understand what is meant by clear comprehension;"],[8,95.12,11.52,"but is it now clear understanding of just the reality which is the chief of experiencing"],[8,106.64,9.92,"- right now, see; it's there, it experiences the object, no one there at all."],[8,116.56,3.36,"So, seeing experiences the object"],[8,120.73,6.31,"- is there clear comprehension of seeing as - it's just a reality,"],[8,127.04,6.49,"no shape, no form, it's not white, it's not green, it doesn't smell, it doesn't have any taste..."],[8,134.06,8.41,"Imagine how it is, that which just arises and experiences the object as the chief;"],[8,142.99,1.57,"what does it mean?"],[8,144.56,5.86,"There must be other realities which arise together, experience the object together,"],[8,150.55,2.81,"but not as the chief."],[8,153.36,5.72,"From understanding little by little, there can be the understanding that the citta"],[8,159.44,7.47,"- the chief of experiencing - is the reality which experiences the object so clearly."],[8,167.38,6.86,"No matter it's dark or it's beginnng to light up gradually, little by little,"],[8,174.24,4.42,"the reality which is experiencing it can know clearly the difference,"],[8,179.47,3.63,"from what is so dark until it's so bright, see."],[8,183.52,9.49,"So, the reality which is the chief of experiencing the object is the leader of the world;"],[8,194.0,3.04,"there could never be the world at all"],[8,197.04,5.02,"if there was no reality which experiences the object so clearly;"],[8,202.42,4.78,"just experiencing the object clearly, that is its function,"],[8,207.2,4.4,"but since it's there, experiencing the object so clearly,"],[8,211.6,6.4,"other realities follow it, by way of such thinking, of such knowledge,"],[8,218.0,7.68,"and such form of way of living and so on, even the war or the peace, see;"],[8,225.68,4.07,"all by that which experiences the object clearly."],[8,230.65,7.34,"And this is the clear comprehension, to understand what is there in the world;"],[8,238.18,5.42,"without that which arises and experiences the object so clearly,"],[8,243.6,3.18,"there cannot be anything at all, no world;"],[8,247.28,3.68,"so, the world follows because of the citta,"],[8,250.96,4.5,"which experiences the object so clearly, leads to it,"],[8,255.49,11.87,"it's the leader in any incident, in any situation, any moment of war or peace, see."],[8,267.52,8.08,"This is the clear comprehension that the reality which is there - no shape, no form, no smell, no taste -"],[8,275.6,2.64,"is not known as it is yet;"],[8,278.44,2.76,"but learn to understand the world,"],[8,281.84,6.74,"and this is the beginning of gradually letting go of ignorance,"],[8,288.8,5.84,"not just by thinking of how many kinds of citta are there and so on, see."],[8,294.64,7.28,"That's why understanding the clear comprehension of just a reality is very important."],[8,302.32,5.92,"So, when we understand what performs - or what is - clear comprehension,"],[8,308.24,4.28,"we can talk about the way it is achieved;"],[8,313.04,5.58,"we can talk about the four clear comprehensions, one by one."],[8,318.64,10.79,"And this is the only way to gradually let go of the clinging to that which appears as something from life to life,"],[8,329.44,2.16,"no understanding of what is what,"],[8,331.73,6.15,"because it's not clear comprehension of the truth."],[8,338.58,3.36,"Is there any question about clear comprehension,"],[8,341.96,5.18,"so that we can go on, one by one, with the four."],[8,348.18,4.22,"Is there now clear comprehension of citta?"],[8,355.44,6.4,"We keep on talking about this just in order to have clear comprehension of other things,"],[8,361.84,6.32,"one by one, little by little, what is meant by clear comprehension;"],[8,368.16,4.88,"can it develop clearer and clearer, stage by stage,"],[8,373.04,6.8,"to become the clearest moment, that of realizing the truth."],[8,382.08,4.48,"We're talking about right understanding, clear comprehension;"],[8,386.99,10.13,"there must be the object of the moment of clear comprehension too; is that right?"],[8,397.12,5.92,"So now, clear comprehension is pañña;"],[8,403.04,7.36,"when we say citta is a reality which experiences the object clearly, is that enough?"],[8,410.4,5.36,"Is it already clear comprehension of citta?"],[8,415.76,5.4,"That's why understanding the clear comprehension is not just hearing,"],[8,421.46,3.98,"listening, understanding the term, the word,"],[8,425.44,3.74,"but understanding the reality which is there,"],[8,429.43,6.07,"which is very deep, very subtle to understand, to get closer, to realize the truth of it."],[8,436.2,5.3,"That's why clear comprehension has to begin with what we are talking about,"],[8,442.0,3.02,"to develop or to have clear comprehension of"],[8,445.26,6.66,"- what is there in life at any moment, is that true?"],[8,452.52,9.34,"Otherwise, how come the term clear comprehension, what does it mean?"],[8,464.88,5.36,"So, it's the development of right understanding, clearer and clearer,"],[8,470.24,4.95,"of the object which is there, as it is."],[8,475.52,2.91,"Now, it's there, what about its comprehension?"],[8,478.95,5.12,"What about clear comprehension?"],[8,484.88,6.27,"It's different from just - what is there is real, it's a reality;"],[8,491.32,4.35,"is that clear comprehension?"],[8,498.08,4.1,"That's why it means that right understanding is not enough at all"],[8,502.96,5.65,"when it's just learning about the word and the term and the story of it,"],[8,509.92,4.32,"but beginning to understand the nature of it"],[8,515.17,8.83,"- clear comprehension of the truth of each reality which is there,"],[8,524.0,9.9,"little by little. No doubt about clear comprehension now, or is there still doubt?"],[8,550.03,5.44,"Are there only stories, no realities at all? [There has to be reality.]"],[8,556.02,5.48,"That's why - clear comprehension of the reality, not of the story."],[8,563.62,8.14,"Beginning to understand how deep, how subtle Dhamma is - the words about the truth,"],[8,571.76,5.23,"it's there all the time, unknown, until it is known or heard,"],[8,578.2,9.31,"until it is clear comprehension of the object appearing at any time."],[8,588.56,3.44,"So now, is it clear understanding of seeing?"],[8,592.0,3.87,"Is it clear understanding of that which is seen?"],[8,596.88,3.13,"Are they yet gocara?"],[8,600.72,2.08,"That's why learning a little more,"],[8,602.8,5.2,"to have clear comprehension of - dhamma, not anyone at all;"],[8,608.0,1.44,"the more developed is understanding,"],[8,609.44,3.76,"the deeper understanding can let go of the idea"],[8,613.2,4.84,"of self or something which has been accumulated for... how long?"],[8,619.55,5.81,"Uncountable moments of not hearing, considering about the truth"],[8,625.36,4.08,"and then the moment of hearing, considering, little by little,"],[8,630.88,2.6,"from time to time, from life to life,"],[8,633.89,4.51,"before becoming eon and eon of firmer understanding,"],[8,638.4,4.89,"clear comprehension of what is there right now."],[8,644.88,4.81,"So now, no doubt about what is meant by clear comprehension..."],[8,650.59,5.26,"not of other things, but of that which is now appearing,"],[8,657.04,4.17,"to understand the four sampajañña."],[8,669.92,4.73,"What kind of sampajañña is there now? See,"],[8,675.68,4.56,"not clear comprehension of gocara yet, isn't it?"],[8,687.12,4.18,"But beginning to understand what the four are,"],[8,692.32,6.8,"otherwise, how can it become clear comprehension?"],[8,703.0,2.71,"And these are the new habits,"],[8,706.58,6.72,"careful considering, to be one's own understanding,"],[8,713.68,6.31,"not just following the word, remembering the word, reciting the word."],[8,723.04,5.44,"So now, no doubt about what is meant by clear comprehension;"],[8,728.48,6.97,"so, we can talk about the four, one by one."],[8,748.0,2.0,"What is clear comprehension?"],[8,750.0,6.4,"Right understanding of the object which is there, clearer and clearer,"],[8,758.4,5.21,"otherwise how can it become clear if there's no thought,"],[8,764.4,5.28,"no careful considering of what is there at all?"],[8,769.68,5.84,"So, understand what is meant by clear comprehension, at moment of seeing,"],[8,775.52,3.92,"whether it's clear comprehension or not;"],[8,779.44,5.66,"so, what is meant by clear comprehension? It understands the truth,"],[8,785.87,11.6,"it's not just thinking about the truth or remembering the word of truth."],[8,801.36,15.12,"So, what is the first sampajañña? [The first one that is mentioned is satthaka sampajañña.]"],[8,816.48,5.64,"Satthaka sampajañña: while listening to the truth,"],[8,822.39,4.21,"is there any understanding that it's so worthwhile,"],[8,826.8,9.6,"so very precious in life, to have such clear understanding of what is there as it is;"],[8,836.4,3.2,"not just: dhamma, no one there,"],[8,839.6,3.76,"but what is dhamma at that very moment?"],[8,843.36,5.43,"and - no one there at all at that very moment, or - not anything at all,"],[8,849.4,5.9,"it's just anatta, even just the word anatta,"],[8,855.49,6.69,"it's such a precious moment, understanding the truth of the word."],[8,862.69,8.27,"No matter at what time, long time ago or at this moment, or in the future, it's so true."],[8,870.96,7.68,"That's why the truth is very precious to understand, that it cannot be changed at all,"],[8,878.64,3.92,"sacca - so true, parami - firm confidence"],[8,882.56,7.17,"to condition a little more clear comprehension of the truth of what is there right now,"],[8,889.97,4.31,"as not anyone, not anything at all."],[8,894.8,7.47,"Little by little, to know the changing from - no understanding at all,"],[8,902.28,5.9,"conditioning such wrong deeds and wrong speech in a day,"],[8,908.65,2.51,"almost all the time in a day,"],[8,911.16,5.72,"to be moment of understanding - beginning to understand,"],[8,917.36,3.04,"from what is there as it is, little by little,"],[8,920.4,7.97,"it's there so real, it's conditioned to arise, it has arisen and gone instantly, see;"],[8,930.32,4.08,"It's kept, it's remembered, it's enrooted,"],[8,934.4,3.2,"to be firmer and firmer, to understand the truth,"],[8,937.6,3.68,"no matter what we hear after this topic,"],[8,941.28,6.18,"it's been said, so true, just about the truth of what is there as it is."],[8,948.96,7.76,"No matter what we talk about - the citta, the reality, the chief of experiencing"],[8,957.54,4.38,"- because it's the chief, it experiences so clearly;"],[8,961.92,4.0,"so, it's the one which is the leader of the world,"],[8,965.92,4.08,"following moments of experiencing, on and on and on and on,"],[8,970.0,6.96,"to be this or that, war or peace, akusala or kusala, and so on."],[8,978.56,4.8,"Isn't this clear comprehension? Little by little,"],[8,983.36,5.5,"not to forget that it's quite far away, the understanding of the truth"],[8,989.63,9.57,"because even if it's so close, ignorance covers it up each moment,"],[8,999.2,5.6,"to make it so far to know, even if it's so close."],[8,1005.2,6.62,"That's why, learn to understand little by little, as parami,"],[8,1011.82,3.94,"without parami, how can there be moments of realizing the truth?"],[8,1015.76,5.16,"Because ignorance is there, conditioning such akusala moment,"],[8,1021.92,3.19,"so much that no one can possibly know how much,"],[8,1025.39,3.13,"until hearing again, reading again,"],[8,1028.64,5.96,"considering again each moment of what is there right now, little by little."],[8,1034.62,12.51,"Isn't that satthaka sampajañña, what is useful in life?"],[8,1050.8,6.91,"Is there any doubt about the first sampajañña, satthaka sampajañña?"],[8,1074.72,7.21,"What about: the clear comprehension of the benefits of understanding the Truth - Dhamma?"],[8,1084.61,2.91,"Nothing is more precious,"],[8,1088.96,8.0,"is there anything better than understanding the truth of what is there right now?"],[8,1097.6,10.08,"Clearly, a little more, until it's clear comprehension of the truth of it."],[8,1109.59,5.43,"[Jonothan:] In the text mentions the purpose is growth according to the Dhamma."],[8,1123.38,7.55,"Clear comprehension of the benefits of understanding,"],[8,1131.57,6.88,"otherwise, what else would be better, more beneficial?"],[8,1139.38,6.18,"If someone takes something to be more beneficial than understanding what is there as it is,"],[8,1145.73,7.61,"can that be clear comprehension of what is there right now as it is?"],[8,1154.96,6.23,"So, the way it's translated depends on the way of words, grammar, or so on,"],[8,1161.43,2.95,"but the truth is there."],[8,1165.84,5.36,"I'll ask Khun Khampan about the translation of satthaka sampajañña,"],[8,1171.2,2.16,"whether it's purpose,"],[8,1174.16,6.64,"because what is the nature, the reality of purpose? See,"],[8,1180.8,6.1,"it has to be a cetasika, what cetasika is that?"],[8,1188.32,3.33,"that's why there must be the Vinaya, Sutta, Abhidhamma;"],[8,1192.19,8.37,"all are dhammas, abhidhammas - beyond what anyone can think about by oneself."],[8,1201.52,5.52,"There are many words for different languages and so on,"],[8,1207.04,9.84,"but what is the truth, the nature, the reality?[It's clear comprehension, understanding what is the purpose, etc.]"],[8,1216.88,4.61,"What realities are there? [The understanding, Ajahn.]"],[8,1221.8,9.32,"And other kusala cetasikas arising together, there must be only citta, cetasikas and rupa in truth."],[8,1231.12,5.44,"So, what is the nature of purpose, what is the reality? [It's an idea.]"],[8,1236.83,3.25,"An idea is object of thinking."],[8,1241.04,7.82,"So, what is the reality of what we call purpose?"],[8,1249.04,5.29,"No-one there at all, it has to be a cetasika. [Purpose is a sort of abstract term.]"],[8,1256.17,7.71,"Isn't it real? Is there any purpose now? Isn't it cetana?"],[8,1265.08,7.06,"[Sarah:] So it's all about the cetana and the viriya with the pañña."],[8,1273.51,2.57,"[A. Sujin:] Always a lump of realities,"],[8,1276.08,5.68,"that's why the Buddha pointed which one, what is what,"],[8,1281.76,4.67,"not just one reality, but there are many realities arising together,"],[8,1286.8,3.44,"that can be classified according to their nature,"],[8,1290.27,5.95,"as whether it is phassa or vedana or cetana or ekaggatta, see?"],[8,1297.52,7.99,"And in daily life, what do we say, which means purpose? I'll do, right?"],[8,1306.88,14.4,"All are purpose, cetana. [It comes closer and closer to the understanding of reality now.]"],[8,1321.28,3.27,"Or maybe sometimes not, when it's wrong purpose;"],[8,1328.72,7.14,"and it's different from the purpose to go to see the movies, see?"],[8,1338.56,10.98,"That's why clear comprehension is very important too, about gocara, see;"],[8,1351.76,9.12,"and can it be gocara? Until it is gocara sampajañña. [Anytime.] See."],[8,1368.73,8.44,"Sappaya sampajañña, see, all depends on sampajañña."],[8,1380.56,8.16,"So now, are we talking about sappaya, or satthaka, or gocara, or asammoha? See."],[8,1388.72,6.81,"All depends on understanding the truth, not just the word."],[9,4.32,3.28,"[A. Sujin] Is there attachment to oneself now?"],[9,8.79,1.81,"[Annie] I think there is. Yes."],[9,11.52,3.76,"[A. Sujin] Just thinking is not enough."],[9,15.28,9.68,"It must be very precise to really understand any word we are talking about, like self or oneself."],[9,24.96,4.16,"Is there I or self at this moment?"],[9,30.24,7.44,"Or none at all? [I think there is I.]"],[9,37.68,7.92,"Just think. So it's not precise."],[9,45.6,6.24,"Where's the I at this moment? [Yes, there is.]"],[9,51.84,3.68,"So it's only the idea and just thinking about"],[9,55.52,2.88,"everything like we used to think about this and that."],[9,58.81,7.25,"But actually, there can be more understanding about whatever appears now,"],[9,66.13,3.75,"not just thinking about it. Are you friendly now?"],[9,71.84,7.52,"Talking about friendliness, but now, are you friendly?"],[9,79.36,5.2,"Yes or no? So people talk about friendliness,"],[9,84.56,3.6,"having more and more friendliness, but what is it?"],[9,89.28,3.84,"Without understanding that which we are talking about,"],[9,93.12,4.24,"it's impossible to know more, further about that."],[9,97.36,8.72,"So what is the self now, if you think that you are not clinging to the self now,"],[9,106.08,4.16,"or are you? [Yes, I think I am.]"],[9,110.24,5.92,"To what? What is the self that you are clinging to? [Yes.]"],[9,116.16,5.84,"Like now. No you, or you? [I don't know.]"],[9,122.65,3.83,"This is the beginning of understanding whatever appears."],[9,126.48,6.24,"Otherwise, there's the purpose of going somewhere and trying to have very good time,"],[9,132.72,2.64,"splendid time, very rewarding."],[9,135.36,3.68,"No understanding, even of just \"what's appearing now?\""],[9,139.04,6.0,"or \"where's the self now?\", or \"is there self now?\", or \"is there no self now?\""],[9,145.92,3.12,"So when we're talking about friendliness,"],[9,149.04,5.6,"it's not just the word that anyone can think about it, being friendly. That's not enough."],[9,154.64,7.28,"But what is it? [To feel loved or accepted by others.]"],[9,161.92,4.24,"That is natural for everyone. The same feeling."],[9,166.16,2.0,"But what is the understanding?"],[9,168.16,6.72,"Because the Buddha taught the truth of whatever appears as it is."],[9,174.88,4.8,"That is what is meant by Enlightenment."],[9,179.68,8.88,"Understanding thoroughly, deeply, as it is, not as we guess or as we used to think about."],[9,188.56,6.64,"Even the self, see, it's not clear."],[9,195.2,3.76,"When it's not clear, it seems like there's no self,"],[9,198.96,9.44,"but actually there is so much self that it is not clear even to talk about it."],[9,208.4,8.56,"So did you go to the meditation center to have less attachment and more understanding,"],[9,216.96,4.8,"or do you still cling to get something without understanding?"],[9,224.48,4.32,"Even clinging is not clear."],[9,228.8,3.36,"Because without right understanding,"],[9,232.16,5.52,"who can tell the difference between clinging and being friendly?"],[9,237.68,4.88,"And that is the self who does not know."],[9,242.56,6.0,"When there is understanding, understanding is not anyone."],[9,248.56,8.08,"It's a reality which can understand that which hasn't been understood before."],[9,256.64,5.76,"That's why we learn, listen, and think over it whether it's"],[9,262.4,7.52,"worthwhile studying, developing understanding."],[9,269.92,14.0,"So the bhāvanā, it's translated usually as meditation. What does it mean? [I don't know.]"],[9,283.92,2.72,"So it begins with no understanding."],[9,286.64,8.88,"So it has more and more no understanding or ignorance."],[9,295.52,10.4,"When you think of a funny thing, you smile or laugh alone. Right? Anywhere."],[9,308.8,6.0,"Even there's silence, but the story is so funny."],[9,314.8,13.76,"So it can condition laughing, pleasant moment."],[9,328.56,4.96,"And what about being friendly in such or a certain place?"],[9,333.52,1.44,"What about now?"],[9,338.4,3.68,"No more or what?"],[9,342.08,6.32,"Or it can be anywhere and anytime. To anyone."],[9,348.4,6.88,"That is the development of mettā."],[9,355.28,6.24,"And what do you do in order to have more mettā?"],[9,361.52,7.92,"There, I mean in a retreat to have more mettā, what do you do?"],[9,369.44,9.04,"Not like now? Or what? [I don't know.]"],[9,378.48,10.64,"See, not understanding anything that can be understood anywhere at any time too."],[9,394.88,13.76,"And without understanding, can anyone know whether it's attachment or metta?"],[9,408.64,6.4,"You think that you can be friendly to those around you in the meditation center, right?"],[9,415.04,10.4,"When they all come out, do you still have such feeling of being friendly to all of them?"],[9,425.44,4.32,"Not only at the meditation center, but anywhere."],[9,429.76,9.68,"Or it's just only there that you can have such feeling of being friendly with them."],[9,439.44,10.16,"Like you, see, in the meditation center, you are friendly, right?"],[9,449.6,4.24,"And after that, are you still friendly, after retreat?"],[9,460.88,1.68,"Anything. Not different."],[9,462.56,5.36,"Like seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting, touching, here and there or anywhere."],[9,467.92,2.24,"Seeing is seeing."],[9,470.16,5.76,"If there is understanding right now, is this place meditation center?"],[9,475.92,2.32,"No or yes? [Yes.]"],[9,478.24,8.16,"No. No. Very natural. No rule."],[9,487.36,5.84,"No time to set friendliness or schedule to study."],[9,493.2,8.32,"We can talk about whatever appears anywhere, on the train, in the bus, or here."],[9,502.08,11.84,"Let's say seeing itself, can it be in the train, under the water, up in the sky?"],[9,513.92,7.6,"Seeing is seeing. So there can be the understanding that at moment it sees,"],[9,521.52,4.4,"there must be that which conditions its arising;"],[9,525.92,6.96,"to be seeing, not other moment at all."],[9,532.88,12.24,"Is that the self which sees now? Seeing, is it self? [No.]"],[9,545.12,5.28,"So what is it?"],[9,550.4,9.36,"This is the way to learn to have less attachment to what we used to take for I or a thing"],[9,559.76,1.92,"because of ignorance."],[9,565.44,5.28,"Otherwise, there would be no way to get rid of the idea of self at all."],[9,570.72,3.76,"No matter where you're going, to this or that place,"],[9,574.48,9.68,"without understanding, ignorance is there."],[9,584.16,17.28,"So many people have different sessions, ordinary life and meditation life, by the self."],[9,601.44,5.52,"As long as there is no understanding of whatever appears now as it is,"],[9,606.96,10.24,"there is the idea of something: self, people, things."],[9,617.2,9.76,"Close your eyes. What do you see? No one, right?"],[9,626.96,3.84,"But there's idea of I'm sitting here with many people."],[9,632.0,4.88,"But actually, it appears to seeing."],[9,636.88,4.0,"The visible object has to be object of seeing."],[9,640.88,4.24,"Seeing cannot see sound. It cannot see other thing else"],[9,645.12,4.8,"except that which appears at moment of seeing. Just that."],[9,649.92,2.64,"And after that, there's the idea of something"],[9,652.56,7.52,"because of memory of the marks, signs, shape, and form."],[9,660.08,8.32,"And one keeps that idea all the time, but actually it's gone completely."],[9,668.4,6.64,"So one lives in the world of ignorance, not knowing what's what in a moment"],[9,675.04,1.52,"because seeing is not thinking."],[9,676.56,7.04,"There can be thinking about that which is seen without seeing, like in the dream."],[9,683.6,5.44,"No seeing, but there is thinking about many things,"],[9,689.04,4.48,"and they seem as if they're appearing,"],[9,693.52,6.64,"but actually only memory of what is experienced."],[9,700.16,5.04,"Did you have a dream last night? [Yes.]"],[9,705.76,4.96,"It's not as real as now. It's not as real. [No.]"],[9,710.72,6.24,"Why? [When I'm dreaming, I feel like that's real though.]"],[9,716.96,6.08,"But what's the difference between the two?"],[9,723.04,5.12,"Can anyone see in a dream?"],[9,728.16,8.0,"Can there be seeing in a dream? [It feels like I'm seeing, but isn't it just thinking?]"],[9,736.16,6.16,"See the difference between dreaming and not dreaming at all. Like now."],[9,742.32,4.96,"Because the visible object appears to seeing before thinking."],[9,747.28,4.88,"But in a dream, there's no seeing. No visible object appearing like now."],[9,752.16,3.12,"It's only pure thinking."],[9,755.28,4.16,"The whole story about this and that."],[9,759.44,6.16,"It's like now. When there's no seeing and visible object, it's like dreaming."],[9,765.6,4.8,"Exactly the same. So the difference is that when it's not a dream,"],[9,770.4,4.4,"there is moment of seeing and visible object. That's all."],[9,778.56,9.52,"Yes, or hearing or smelling. Anything can be the object."],[9,788.08,3.6,"But not in a dream."],[9,791.68,7.28,"So it's not you. There are only different realities conditioned to arise."],[9,798.96,8.56,"This can be object of understanding when right understanding develops more and more."],[9,807.52,5.2,"But ignorance cannot experience that"],[9,812.72,5.84,"because it cannot understand anything, even it's appearing right now."],[9,818.56,6.4,"So we understand the difference between ignorance and right understanding."],[9,826.24,5.52,"So in what world have you been living?"],[9,831.76,8.24,"For quite a long, long time when there is no understanding. [Ignorance.]"],[9,846.67,4.4,"And the Teachings of the Buddha can condition right understanding"],[9,852.92,3.16,"about whatever appears now"],[9,856.08,5.68,"because it's the truth, the truthful words."],[9,861.76,8.16,"Nobody can change it because it's all about reality right now."],[9,869.92,10.96,"So one listens to the teachings or to someone else. See."],[9,880.9,4.26,"Have you heard the words, Buddham Saranam Gacchami? [No.]"],[9,886.07,2.25,"Dhammam Saranam Gacchami? [No.]"],[9,888.49,2.28,"Sangham Saranam Gacchami?"],[9,893.76,5.2,"Then why do you go to meditation center? What for?"],[9,898.96,4.48,"When you don't know anything about Buddha, Dhamma, and Sangha."],[9,903.44,8.16,"You just believe in someone else, leading you to somewhere unknown without understanding."],[9,912.88,8.88,"So first of all, we should know what does understanding understand."],[9,921.76,7.64,"Otherwise, we just talk about understanding, but what does it understand?"],[9,937.01,3.35,"So just all about daily life."],[9,940.72,5.96,"Seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting, touching, clinging, aversion, liking, disliking."],[9,946.81,4.63,"Everything in a day is taught."],[9,951.44,3.36,"Otherwise, who knows, right now?"],[9,954.8,5.76,"Is there clinging now, attachment now? Who knows?"],[9,960.56,7.92,"Is seeing not me? Who knows?"],[9,968.48,2.88,"So each word should be studied carefully"],[9,971.36,5.12,"because it will lead to more and more understanding of the whole Tipitaka."],[9,976.48,2.4,"But if there is no understanding of one word,"],[9,978.88,5.92,"it's impossible to understand more at all."],[9,984.8,1.84,"That's the way to understand."],[9,986.64,9.2,"Not just listen, but to really understand what that word represents."],[9,995.84,5.84,"Like seeing, it doesn't represent anyone at all."],[9,1001.68,4.24,"Just a reality which is conditioned to see."],[9,1005.92,3.76,"Without the eye base, could it arise?"],[9,1009.68,3.76,"Could whatever is appearing now appear?"],[9,1013.44,2.0,"So it's just in the moment."],[9,1015.44,8.56,"Seeing is not only conditioned by the eye base, but also by that which can be seen,"],[9,1024.0,6.4,"which impinges on the eye base to condition the seeing to arise and see it."],[9,1030.4,4.8,"That's all. Just that. It's gone."],[9,1035.2,6.48,"Seeing right now is not the seeing of a moment ago at all, different conditions,"],[9,1041.68,10.0,"different visible object arising and falling away in a split second."],[9,1051.68,7.84,"Just consider whether it's true, this moment, as we're just talking about."],[9,1059.52,6.0,"No one there - it's gone completely, like sound and hearing; they are all gone."],[9,1065.52,13.44,"So it's not me who hears, and what is heard is no-one's voice, it's only that which can be heard."],[9,1078.96,7.52,"This is way to have less and less attachment to what we take for self from birth."],[9,1086.48,6.72,"Everything is self or something permanent."],[9,1095.44,9.84,"Without seeing right now, can there be the idea of \"I see\", \"I am seeing\"?"],[9,1105.28,4.64,"While seeing just arises and it sees."],[9,1109.92,5.2,"But ignorance takes it for \"my seeing\" or \"I am seeing\"."],[9,1115.12,6.16,"But when it doesn't arise, where is the me who sees?"],[9,1121.28,5.2,"When there's thinking, it seems like \"I think\", but actually thinking is conditioned."],[9,1126.48,6.0,"We think differently all the time by conditions."],[9,1132.48,3.52,"With right understanding, without right understanding,"],[9,1136.0,5.36,"with attachment or with aversion - all day."],[9,1141.36,7.76,"Just in the moment, from moment to moment."],[9,1149.12,6.72,"And now we are talking about the truth of whatever is appearing now;"],[9,1155.84,7.12,"taught by the Buddha himself who had enlightened it long, long time ago."],[9,1162.96,3.12,"But the Teaching is still about reality right now,"],[9,1166.08,4.96,"so it can be understood any time when anyone hears it."],[9,1176.29,6.27,"[Lan] Is that like the practice of meditation of mindfulness?"],[9,1182.56,6.23,"What is arising passes away at the present moment?"],[9,1188.79,4.89,"[A. Sujin] It's too soon or early to talk about sati."],[9,1193.68,8.8,"See, what is that? See, sati. Can it arise without conditions?"],[9,1202.48,10.0,"Without the understanding of reality now, can sati arise?"],[9,1212.48,3.92,"Usually there is ignorance, not sati."],[9,1216.4,4.48,"Until the theoretical understanding or intellectual understanding is"],[9,1220.88,4.48,"firm enough to be condition for sati to arise."],[9,1225.36,6.56,"Because sati is also non-self, uncontrollable, like seeing and hearing."],[9,1231.92,6.0,"But when thinking about it, some would like to have it at will or"],[9,1237.92,3.68,"do something to get it, without understanding."],[9,1241.6,4.16,"But without the pariyatti, intellectual understanding,"],[9,1245.76,4.24,"there are no right conditions for sati to arise."],[9,1250.0,7.52,"That's why we learn to understand step by step, little by little, and we don't mind what is sati"],[9,1257.52,9.04,"because even right now there's no understanding of that which appears - which is not sati."],[9,1266.56,8.08,"And at moment of understanding the words of the Teachings,"],[9,1274.64,3.28,"isn't there sati with that understanding?"],[9,1281.12,5.76,"So there are many levels of sati to talk about."],[9,1286.88,7.24,"Intellectual level, or direct understanding, or the penetration of reality as it is."],[9,1294.12,8.68,"As the right understanding develops with sati, not just sati by itself."],[9,1302.8,3.68,"Without right understanding, no condition for sati to arise."],[9,1310.4,7.04,"We just want to have it, try to have it without any understanding that it is conditioned."],[9,1317.44,6.64,"And the Teachings of the Buddha are all about detachment."],[9,1324.08,4.88,"Because whenever there is ignorance, there cannot be detachment."],[9,1328.96,3.84,"Whenever there is attachment, there must be ignorance."],[9,1333.36,9.68,"So there can be detachment only when there is understanding, not ignorance."],[9,1343.04,7.52,"Ignorance cannot detach from anything because it doesn't know anything at all."],[9,1350.56,8.56,"Seeing sees. Ignorance cannot understand that as just a moment of a reality,"],[9,1359.12,5.36,"an element which is conditioned to arise and see just that,"],[9,1364.48,3.36,"not another thing, not another moment, only seeing."],[9,1367.84,4.64,"Then it's gone completely, it will never come back at all."],[9,1372.48,7.28,"Without this primary understanding, no condition for sati to arise."],[9,1379.76,2.96,"Because sati has to arise with right understanding"],[9,1382.72,4.8,"when we talk about the moment with sati which can understand whatever appears."],[9,1387.52,5.2,"It needs to have intellectual understanding."],[9,1392.72,6.0,"There are many people who do not know anything and they go to the meditation center,"],[9,1398.72,10.16,"wishing to understand or to get whatever they think about, but no understanding at all."],[9,1413.6,6.48,"Now there is hardness and the experiencing of hardness. Is that sati?"],[9,1420.08,4.4,"Is that? At this moment of holding the microphone. [Yes.]"],[9,1424.48,7.6,"No. Ordinary experience, the kaya viññana,"],[9,1432.08,10.72,"the body consciousness experiences hardness without any understanding, without sati."],[9,1442.8,7.76,"Like anyone in the world who doesn't have any understanding of reality,"],[9,1450.56,6.54,"can you say that that person has sati at moment of holding microphone?"],[9,1459.6,4.4,"When it's dana, sila."],[9,1464.0,8.56,"But while one is listening to the Teachings, at moment of understanding there is sati."],[9,1472.56,3.52,"Just that level, intellectual understanding,"],[9,1476.08,8.0,"not the direct understanding of a reality which one has heard about."],[9,1484.08,4.4,"So don't rush to do anything without understanding"],[9,1488.48,12.08,"because it's the self wishing, trying to get something, not to understand and detach from clinging."],[9,1500.56,9.04,"So the self is there, having more self without understanding."],[9,1509.6,3.68,"If anyone thinks of having sati without intellectual understanding,"],[9,1513.28,8.56,"it's not according to the Teachings of the Buddha: pariyatti, patipatti, and pativedha."],[9,1521.84,6.96,"There cannot be patipatti first and then pariyatti after."],[9,1528.8,5.52,"Because the meaning of patipatti - pati is particular,"],[9,1534.32,4.24,"and patti is to approach with understanding."],[9,1538.56,6.24,"Like seeing is seeing, hearing is hearing, thinking is thinking, attachment is attachment."],[9,1544.8,9.36,"This is said, but what is the moment of direct understanding of just one reality at a time?"],[9,1554.16,3.68,"Like now, seeing, hearing, they seem to arise together,"],[9,1557.84,4.64,"but actually different moments, far apart."],[9,1562.48,6.0,"The conditions for seeing are far away from the conditions for hearing."],[9,1568.48,6.48,"They're not as close as we think."],[9,1574.96,6.0,"And when one wants so much to have sati, isn't that clinging?"],[9,1580.96,7.36,"But when one knows - it's impossible to have direct awareness without the"],[9,1588.32,4.0,"firm foundation of the intellectual understanding,"],[9,1592.32,4.8,"because now we know that seeing is not permanent, right?"],[9,1597.92,5.76,"Or is it permanent? It's not permanent."],[9,1603.68,9.68,"This is very, very weak understanding because it's gone, arising and falling away all the time."],[9,1613.36,7.2,"And we just heard that seeing is not permanent, arising and falling away,"],[9,1620.56,5.36,"and it's not hearing, it's not thinking; this is what we learn, consider,"],[9,1625.92,5.76,"but not direct understanding of the moment when seeing arises and sees."],[9,1631.68,5.84,"At that moment of the clear comprehension of that,"],[9,1637.52,7.2,"there is no other thing at all, just one at a time as it is."],[9,1644.72,6.48,"No wish to have such experience. It is anatta."],[9,1651.2,3.44,"When there are right conditions, no one can stop its arising."],[9,1655.52,6.16,"But when there are no conditions, no one can have it arisen at all."],[9,1661.68,5.84,"Just trying very hard, but that is not the direct understanding with detachment,"],[9,1667.52,7.12,"but it's attachment, trying so hard."],[9,1674.64,7.2,"So instead of understanding, there will be more and more idea of self who's trying,"],[9,1681.84,12.48,"not to understand, but to get something and thinking that it's understanding, but it's not."],[9,1694.32,5.12,"Like now, when pañña develops, so great,"],[9,1699.44,8.96,"it can experience with detachment according to the level of pañña."],[9,1708.4,6.88,"While the intellectual understanding cannot know just that moment as it is"],[9,1715.28,7.12,"because there are many things in succession so fast, very elaborate,"],[9,1722.4,7.68,"that it's only thinking about seeing, not understanding the actual moment of seeing."],[9,1730.08,8.4,"And if one is trying so hard, it's impossible because it's done by attachment and ignorance."],[9,1738.48,4.32,"Until there is less and less ignorance and attachment,"],[9,1742.8,9.68,"then reality can appear to the developed pañña by itself naturally, anatta."],[9,1752.48,5.44,"And that's the moment to understand the meaning of anatta."],[9,1762.32,8.24,"Have you heard about the subtlety of the four noble truths? All of them. All four."],[9,1770.56,2.48,"But it seems like it's very easy."],[9,1773.04,8.56,"Just wanting to have and then one goes somewhere and thinks that one knows."],[9,1781.6,6.77,"But when it's known, only when time comes by conditions."],[10,5.01,3.86,"[Prakash] Ajahn, what's the difference between the sankhara-dhammas?"],[10,15.6,4.75,"So, we have the word just to represent a reality,"],[10,20.61,8.75,"without the word, who knows what is meant, this or that, hot or hard;"],[10,29.36,6.58,"that's why we have the word to represent what reality we are talking about."],[10,36.8,13.75,"So now, your question? [My question, sankhara-dhamma is the one which arises...]"],[10,52.14,4.42,"Okay now, we start again, about dhamma:"],[10,56.56,3.28,"we don't talk about that which is not real,"],[10,59.87,9.12,"we just talk about the truth, the reality, the ultimate reality."],[10,69.68,6.92,"We take this for table, but at moment of touching, it's hard - no table."],[10,77.36,6.63,"So, we learn to understand the reality which nobody can change at all;"],[10,84.8,6.32,"the seeing is a reality, sankhara-dhamma,"],[10,91.12,5.04,"because it cannot arise by itself or by anyone,"],[10,96.16,4.9,"but it can arise only by its proper conditions,"],[10,101.92,5.92,"and sankhara-dhamma, no matter it's seeing or hearing,"],[10,107.84,5.04,"there must be what is there together to condition its arising."],[10,112.88,5.12,"So now, remember that dhamma is a reality,"],[10,118.0,5.6,"but only one reality cannot arise alone by itself,"],[10,123.6,7.28,"it has other realities arising together, supporting or conditioning each other;"],[10,130.88,6.16,"without citta, cetasikas cannot arise, but citta is not cetasika,"],[10,137.04,5.09,"and without cetasikas, citta cannot arise."],[10,142.54,7.38,"So, whatever arises has its conditions or other realities arising together;"],[10,149.92,4.3,"have firm confidence on this, firmer - never change."],[10,155.76,7.05,"So, at moment of taste arising, there must be hardness or softness too,"],[10,163.16,5.88,"how could there be just that taste, sweetness, how come?"],[10,169.04,7.44,"That's why we take that the fruit to be so sweet, the fruit, see, and the sweetness;"],[10,176.48,5.28,"the apple is sweet, while the sauce is not sweet,"],[10,181.76,8.8,"there must be the source or the base or that which is there to condition such taste."],[10,190.56,10.56,"Can there be just taste without that apple or papaya?"],[10,201.12,5.52,"So, even taste cannot arise alone, but we don't know what conditions taste,"],[10,206.64,6.72,"until we learn, little by little - what are the main or the primary rupas?"],[10,213.36,7.04,"Without hardness, can there be taste, can there be sweetness, bitterness,"],[10,220.4,4.56,"or what is there as taste? It cannot arise alone."],[10,225.76,7.36,"Learn little by little, to have confidence of the truth, of dhamma first;"],[10,233.12,4.24,"all are dhammas, but all dhammas are not known yet;"],[10,237.36,2.88,"but whatever is real is real,"],[10,240.24,4.88,"but what the reality is, the truth of that reality, is not known yet."],[10,245.12,6.8,"So, we study Dhamma to understand more and more about just one reality."],[10,251.92,5.44,"What arises, to experience the object, or cannot experience the object,"],[10,257.36,1.76,"that is the beginning."],[10,259.12,7.52,"And then, how many different kinds of that which arises and experience the object?"],[10,266.64,5.04,"Two different kinds, one experience directly, as the chief,"],[10,271.68,4.08,"and the other also share or experience the same object,"],[10,275.76,3.44,"because they arise together, experiencing that object,"],[10,279.2,4.56,"but it's not the same quality, not the same reality;"],[10,283.76,4.24,"each one has its own characteristic."],[10,288.0,5.0,"Memory cannot feel, is there remembering?"],[10,293.19,4.96,"Yes, there is, and usually it's \"I remember\","],[10,298.16,5.04,"but remembering is remembering, not anyone at all."],[10,303.2,3.44,"That's why we learn about the truth, the hidden truth,"],[10,306.64,2.88,"which is covered by ignorance and attachment"],[10,309.52,8.08,"- the second Noble Truth, taking it instantly as something;"],[10,317.6,3.92,"how much ignorance is there?"],[10,321.52,4.08,"So, ignorance cannot understand the truth."],[10,325.6,6.48,"That's why the understanding only can wear away ignorance and attachment,"],[10,332.08,4.57,"so very, very slightly, unknown."],[10,338.96,3.92,"Is this the study of dhamma?"],[10,342.88,6.64,"Not just the word; the word is remembered,"],[10,349.52,7.52,"but when there is no understanding, how can that be the study of Dhamma?"],[10,357.04,4.64,"Just studying the word, remembering the word - not the understanding of Dhamma."],[10,366.72,7.12,"That's why some people can have a degree, high degree in Pali or anything,"],[10,373.84,3.36,"but what about understanding the truth,"],[10,377.2,6.4,"and when and what and where is the truth? They cannot find out that."],[10,385.76,5.68,"For example, what is real, what is the truth of this moment? No idea."],[10,393.36,4.64,"What is moment, and what is this moment, and what is the truth of this moment?"],[10,398.0,2.8,"No idea at all."],[10,400.8,3.12,"Without listening to the words of the Buddha,"],[10,403.92,7.69,"can anyone have the understanding of each moment as it is, not permanent at all?"],[10,413.44,8.55,"As conditioned moment, conditioned reality, different realities - all gone."],[10,422.57,4.29,"So, little by little, we'll come to understand what is meant by kamma"],[10,427.67,2.42,"and what is meant by vipaka;"],[10,430.26,4.77,"Not just the word, different words, but the reality,"],[10,435.05,8.54,"what is that which is the cause, kamma, and the result, vipaka."],[10,444.16,2.24,"Just talking about the cause and vipaka,"],[10,446.4,4.32,"and it seems that there is the understanding of kamma and vipaka,"],[10,450.72,3.44,"but not at all."],[10,454.16,11.24,"What is that reality which is kamma, and how can it be kamma, and what kind of kamma?"],[10,466.4,4.16,"So now, we don't talk about sankhara-khandha,"],[10,470.56,6.64,"we are talking about sankhara-dhamma, how careful it has to be."],[10,477.2,4.32,"That's why if the understanding of sankhara-dhamma is not clear,"],[10,481.52,2.91,"it's mixed up with other words, other ideas;"],[10,485.01,7.63,"that's why we have to learn just one word at a time - dhamma is whatever is real."],[10,492.64,6.72,"Why is it real? It's there, seeing, so seeing is real;"],[10,499.36,3.0,"seeing arises, otherwise there could be no seeing;"],[10,502.5,4.75,"learn little by little to have confidence of the truth"],[10,507.46,4.46,"- sacca-parami, it's so very important."],[10,511.92,6.4,"That's why don't move on to other words, other chapters, so very rapidly, quickly"],[10,518.32,5.92,"- it doesn't have firm understanding of each word of truth."],[10,524.24,6.4,"So, when we talk about dhamma, we don't talk about other things, we just talk about dhamma."],[10,530.64,7.36,"And when we talk about khandha, we talk about what khandha are."],[10,538.0,3.68,"And sankhara-dhamma, visankhara-dhamma... just the word,"],[10,541.68,4.64,"but what are they? No answer because no understanding,"],[10,546.32,4.96,"but there can be the answer - all realities are dhamma,"],[10,551.28,8.24,"all dhammas - all - whatever arises is real and is conditioned,"],[10,559.52,9.28,"so, all kinds of dhamma which arises is sankhara-dhamma - just another word for dhamma."],[10,568.8,2.96,"So, we weren't talking about sankhara-khandha,"],[10,571.76,3.2,"we were just talking about sankhara-dhamma;"],[10,574.96,6.32,"Otherwise, they are all mixed, isn't that true? [Yes, Ajahn]."],[10,581.28,2.88,"So, when there is the understanding of sankhara-dhamma,"],[10,584.16,4.49,"we can tell what sankhara-dhamma is not sankhara-khandha."],[10,589.13,3.97,"So, we learn another bit more about what is khandha."],[10,593.91,6.87,"Is vedana-khandha dhamma? [Yes.]"],[10,601.21,5.27,"Is vedana-khandha sankhara-dhamma? [Yes.]"],[10,606.48,3.19,"That's why it has to be firm,"],[10,609.91,6.65,"understanding is understanding, it shouldn't be changed to - no understanding."],[10,616.56,3.36,"That's why it's the way to prove how much understanding"],[10,619.92,5.52,"or how firm understanding of the truth is between the two words;"],[10,625.44,5.28,"it can prove how much confidence of the truth is there."],[10,630.72,7.36,"What are sankhara-khandha, and what are sankhara-dhamma?"],[10,638.08,7.48,"So, first of all, sankhara-dhamma should be so firmly established - never change;"],[10,645.56,7.51,"sankhara-dhamma, whatever dhamma, whatever reality, whatever arises is sankhara-dhamma,"],[10,653.32,4.04,"because it needs conditions for its arising,"],[10,657.36,7.04,"and the conditions must be realities too - not other things."],[10,664.53,6.34,"For example, seeing, the eye is real, it's a dhamma."],[10,670.88,5.36,"So, all are dhammas, whatever is real, are [is] dhamma."],[10,676.24,7.84,"So, is the eye-base sankhara-khandha? [No, Ajahn.]"],[10,684.08,3.36,"Is it sankhara-dhamma? [Yes.]"],[10,688.6,6.28,"Understanding the difference between sankhara-dhamma and sankhara-khandha;"],[10,694.88,3.44,"but before we talk about sankhara-khandha, we should"],[10,698.32,4.48,"have firm understanding of sankhara-dhamma;"],[10,702.8,6.08,"no change, so no matter we talk by way of sankhara-khandha or dhatu and so on and on,"],[10,708.88,7.44,"no change of the truth, sankhara-dhamma is that which arises and falls away."],[10,716.32,3.06,"And some are sankhara-khandha,"],[10,720.27,6.45,"and the next, very, very subtle, on and on and on, little by little;"],[10,726.72,3.28,"otherwise, it's not studying dhamma,"],[10,730.0,5.36,"it's just reading, remembering the word only;"],[10,735.36,7.15,"quite much different between remembering the word and understanding the truth of that reality."],[10,747.44,11.52,"So now, shall we review - what is dhamma? [Dhamma is that which is real.]"],[10,758.96,7.84,"Whatever is real; how do you know that it's real? [It's appearing now.]"],[10,766.8,7.28,"It's there appearing, and later on we'll know that which does not appear is also dhamma."],[10,774.08,4.8,"Little by little, but having firmer understanding about the truth;"],[10,778.88,5.76,"what is there had to arise, no matter it's experienced or not,"],[10,784.64,5.42,"but there must be conditions for whatever arises, whether it's experienced or not,"],[10,790.32,4.08,"including what is experienced and what is not experienced,"],[10,794.4,4.72,"but what arises has to have conditions for its arising."],[10,799.12,7.2,"And they arise together too - nothing can arise alone, no matter what at all;"],[10,806.32,3.6,"firm confidence that we're talking about just one reality"],[10,809.92,3.52,"while there are other realities arising together,"],[10,813.44,3.04,"but [since] we cannot talk about all at once,"],[10,816.48,3.28,"so, we just talk about one kind of reality,"],[10,819.76,4.52,"to understand clearer and clearer about the truth"],[10,824.28,4.92,"- that nothing can be taken for someone or something at all"],[10,829.2,6.0,"because it's so short - as soon as it has arisen, it's gone instantly."],[10,836.08,2.0,"And this is the world,"],[10,838.08,2.48,"and this is the truth of life,"],[10,840.56,2.47,"and this is the ultimate truth;"],[10,844.08,5.28,"eons and eons ago and on and on ahead, no one can change dhamma"],[10,849.71,5.95,"- dhamma is dhamma, and all dhammas are anatta;"],[10,856.0,4.4,"it cannot be anyone because it's conditioned to arise,"],[10,860.4,6.72,"as soon as it has arisen is gone, no more conditions to stay longer."],[10,867.12,3.84,"That's why learning to understand that ignorance is there,"],[10,870.96,6.31,"so great, so enormous, that it hinders the truth of what is there,"],[10,877.27,3.93,"taking that which is not permanent for permanent."],[10,881.2,2.4,"Nothing appears to arise and falling away now"],[10,883.6,6.28,"because ignorance cannot understand each different reality which arise and fall away."],[10,890.88,8.52,"That's why there's the person who developed great paramis to enlighten the truth"],[10,900.03,4.26,"- the enlightenment, in your land;"],[10,904.64,6.84,"and spread and shared his understanding with the others, now throughout the world;"],[10,912.35,4.69,"and not just only this world, other worlds too, in his time;"],[10,917.04,4.96,"deva world or brahma world - the truth is the truth."],[10,922.0,4.8,"So, be truthful to the truth, respect the truth"],[10,926.8,3.68,"because what the Buddha respected was the truth"],[10,931.39,3.09,"- no one can change the truth."],[10,934.48,4.08,"So now, we learn to understand the hidden truth,"],[10,938.56,3.36,"it's been hidden for quite a long, long time,"],[10,941.92,3.2,"and now the word of truth is heard,"],[10,945.12,7.72,"but it's so subtle that it takes very careful considering, again and again and again."],[10,953.84,3.36,"We have talked a lot about dhamma and seeing,"],[10,957.2,3.96,"dhamma and whatever dhamma, kamma and vipaka and so on"],[10,961.16,5.64,"- not enough at all, as long as it's not directly experienced;"],[10,966.8,6.32,"kamma is a word, but what is the reality that word refers to?"],[10,973.12,6.16,"And vipaka - it's a word, but what is the reality which is vipaka?"],[10,980.16,8.07,"Not just the word translated, but the understanding of this moment - so deep;"],[10,988.4,3.32,"even about what we take for, or have heard about, kamma"],[10,992.7,5.54,"- it's there right now, but what it is it's not known,"],[10,998.24,5.52,"until we learn little by little to understand what is there, real;"],[10,1003.76,4.88,"until we understand that the realities are so very different,"],[10,1008.64,8.55,"from time to time and only once in samsara - arisen and fallen away instantly."],[10,1017.8,5.24,"So, being true to the truth, sacca-parami;"],[10,1023.04,4.78,"with viriya-parami, courageous;"],[10,1027.82,3.62,"khanti-parami, patient, great patience."],[10,1031.44,6.32,"To let go of ignorance and attachment which hinder the truth,"],[10,1037.76,3.67,"hide the truth all the time, it covers up the truth"],[10,1041.82,3.65,"- now is arising and falling away, nothing is permanent."],[10,1045.46,3.29,"Can that be realized? [Yes.]"],[10,1049.84,3.52,"But not now, but by understanding."],[10,1053.52,6.11,"So, is understanding a reality, is it real?"],[10,1060.39,5.07,"What kind of reality is it? [It is nama.]"],[10,1066.02,7.3,"Nama-dhamma, right? Is it citta? [Yes, Ajahn.]"],[10,1073.69,5.75,"No, citta does not understand the truth,"],[10,1079.44,6.42,"it just experiences the obect, never changes."],[10,1086.0,7.84,"Is there understanding? [I don't understand the question.]"],[10,1093.84,5.44,"See - I don't understand, so there has to be understanding, right?"],[10,1101.2,4.75,"That's why, not forgetting, that we are learning about the truth,"],[10,1106.53,5.95,"understanding is not not-understanding, right?"],[10,1112.48,5.92,"There are two kinds: not-understanding and understanding,"],[10,1118.4,5.44,"what is real? [Both are real.]"],[10,1123.84,5.84,"Both, right, at moment of not-understanding it's not-understanding"],[10,1129.68,8.08,"- a reality which does not understand, which cannot understand, which never understands;"],[10,1137.76,3.92,"is it a reality? [Yes.]"],[10,1141.68,5.76,"What is there in life is a reality, complex,"],[10,1147.44,6.8,"it never knows that what are there, since is not-understanding."],[10,1154.24,5.98,"It's a reality - ignorance, avijja;"],[10,1160.73,7.83,"vijja is understanding, and a-vijja no-understanding, avijja, right?"],[10,1168.56,7.68,"So, what kind of reality is it? [Nama-dhamma?]"],[10,1176.24,9.12,"Sure? [Yes.] Sure? [Yes, Ajahn.] Sure?"],[10,1185.36,2.55,"It's firm now, it's real"],[10,1188.65,6.31,"- not understanding, not being able to understand - it's a reality, avijja;"],[10,1194.96,5.12,"it's dhamma, it experiences the object with no-understanding;"],[10,1201.2,7.49,"so, it's not citta, it's cetasika;"],[10,1208.69,0.03,"and it is akusala cetasika."],[10,1208.72,3.12,"So, we learn to understand the cetasikas,"],[10,1211.84,2.52,"because there are many cetasikas;"],[10,1214.36,6.29,"each has its own quality, characteristic, function."],[10,1220.98,5.66,"So, all kinds of cetasika cannot be citta;"],[10,1226.64,2.88,"citta is just the chief of experiencing,"],[10,1229.52,4.22,"it does not like, it does not dislike, it does not understand, it doesn't anything,"],[10,1233.89,4.66,"but it's that which experiences the object clearly,"],[10,1238.56,4.33,"at any moment, since eons and eons ago."],[10,1242.88,4.8,"And it arises with different kinds of cetasikas;"],[10,1247.68,4.4,"sometimes it arises with ignorance, avijja,"],[10,1252.08,7.52,"and sometimes it arises with right understanding, pañña or vijja - no one."],[10,1259.6,4.72,"That's why we just don't talk about kamma or vipaka, about the word,"],[10,1264.32,4.76,"but what about the understanding, what is kamma, and what is vipaka"],[10,1270.13,8.51,"- now, vipaka is also there, who knows?"],[10,1278.64,6.08,"Learn to understand what is the cause, kamma, and what is the result, vipaka;"],[10,1284.72,3.28,"and there are many, many realities too;"],[10,1288.0,2.4,"more precise about each reality,"],[10,1290.4,3.49,"not mixing it with the other."],[10,1294.2,5.62,"And this is the virtue, the great virtues of the Buddha;"],[10,1302.64,2.4,"His great compassion"],[10,1305.04,5.91,"- no one could understand the truth if He hadn't taught it,"],[10,1310.95,5.69,"if He hadn't said anything about the truth at all:"],[10,1316.64,5.38,"phra-pañña-khun, phra-borisut-khun, and phra-maha-karuna-khun"],[10,1322.02,6.46,"- wisdom, compassion, and virtue."],[10,1328.48,4.56,"So now, you know who is Buddha;"],[10,1333.04,4.48,"not just the one to just pay respect to,"],[10,1337.52,9.6,"but understand His great virtues for anyone to have understanding;"],[10,1347.12,4.24,"and understanding is pañña cetasika."],[10,1363.99,3.77,"[A. Sujin:] So now, do you respect the Buddha?"],[10,1367.76,2.8,"At moment of understanding."],[10,1371.58,6.66,"I appreciate your wholesome parami; sawadee ka."],[11,6.37,6.55,"[Jill] You say how important it is to understand sati."],[11,12.92,5.96,"[A. Sujin] Not just sati. [No, all realities.] Yeah, in order to develop sati."],[11,20.6,2.48,"[In the beginning of the development of sati,"],[11,23.08,3.44,"there is no clear distinction: this is nāma, this is rūpa...]"],[11,27.32,5.24,"Excuse me, if it’s clear, it’s vipassanā ñāṇa, not only the beginning of satipaṭṭhāna."],[11,33.76,7.16,"It has to be like this, because all dhammas are like something behind the black curtain."],[11,40.92,3.84,"So black and so dark, even though it is now appearing,"],[11,44.76,3.4,"but the understanding has not grown yet."],[11,48.16,4.48,"So when there’s no light of understanding,"],[11,52.64,4.52,"how can the realities behind the black curtain appear? See?"],[11,57.16,7.08,"It’s like that because it seems so very easy, like “seeing now sees.”"],[11,64.24,4.4,"But the understanding of it as just a reality,"],[11,69.36,5.32,"if there is no understanding of what the Buddha taught in the very beginning,"],[11,75.28,4.24,"it’s just as if there’s nothing there behind the black curtain"],[11,79.52,6.56,"because it seems like everyday life, that there are people and things and I all the time,"],[11,86.08,2.52,"but it’s not like that at all."],[11,88.6,5.32,"So paññā has to grow little by little, so very little,"],[11,93.92,3.48,"because each time there is seeing and hearing,"],[11,97.4,5.76,"there is always ignorance and attachment after seeing and hearing. All the time."],[11,103.68,5.24,"So why didn’t the Buddha incline to teach after his enlightenment?"],[11,108.92,4.4,"Because it’s against the current of life,"],[11,113.32,7.08,"because it has to start with detachment from the very beginning,"],[11,120.4,3.92,"because it’s very difficult to become detached"],[11,124.32,3.8,"from everything that one is used to being attached to,"],[11,128.12,4.6,"from life to life, for eons and eons, not just this one life."],[11,132.72,6.36,"So it’s so very difficult even to have such a beginning of detachment—"],[11,139.08,6.12,"from not knowing, not understanding what it’s about and how to develop it."],[11,145.72,4.24,"Because many people would like to get a result in this life"],[11,149.96,3.4,"or as soon as there is the understanding of realities,"],[11,153.36,5.8,"but that is not the way. Because where is the attachment? Right there."],[11,159.16,7.72,"It comes all the time as soon as there are conditions for it to arise through any doorway."],[11,166.88,5.96,"So one has to be wise to the moment of being attached"],[11,172.84,4.68,"and remember all the time that it has to be only one way,"],[11,177.52,5.96,"detachment with right understanding of the reality which appears."],[11,183.48,6.72,"So how very long the way has to go. One has to be so very patient."],[11,190.2,6.32,"So that one can understand the core of the Teachings. Being patient comes first."],[11,197.52,0.8,"Khanti pen tama ying ying in Thai."],[11,200.88,4.0,"Because without khanti, one will never be successful at all."],[11,205.72,2.52,"So it has to be paññā which knows"],[11,208.24,5.8,"that it’s not by the “I” who tries so hard to get the understanding,"],[11,214.04,5.12,"but it’s the understanding which will gradually eliminate the idea of self"],[11,219.72,1.52,"from the very beginning;"],[11,221.24,7.24,"not doing, not wanting, not going away from this moment without any understanding."],[11,229.0,5.68,"So when we talk about nāma and rūpa, we don’t talk about what’s in the book only,"],[11,234.68,3.04,"whether it’s citta, cetasika, or rūpa."],[11,237.72,6.52,"But now we have known from books; we learn about reality in daily life, in everyday life."],[11,244.24,7.12,"Because when there is the beginning of life, paṭisandhi, the birth consciousness,"],[11,251.36,7.12,"there must be many different types of citta arising from time to time."],[11,259.04,3.56,"And without understanding it, what is there?"],[11,262.6,4.2,"Ignorance and wrong view of self, all the time."],[11,266.8,6.0,"So it’s just about keeping on developing understanding in order to become detached."],[11,272.8,4.96,"Just in order to become detached from wanting to do, wanting to get."],[11,277.76,3.0,"But developing understanding—that’s the only way."],[11,280.76,3.88,"Because only understanding can work its way,"],[11,285.56,4.88,"being more and more detached from the reality which appears"],[11,290.44,8.36,"with just understanding of the characteristic of reality as we have heard or as we have learnt,"],[11,298.8,4.84,"that there are only two types of reality, not self."],[11,303.64,4.4,"They are rūpa, which cannot experience,"],[11,308.04,5.92,"but is the object of experiencing, and there is attachment to it instantly."],[11,314.68,2.96,"So in one’s life, in the plane of the five khandhas,"],[11,317.64,7.4,"there are rūpas through the five doorways just for attachment, without understanding."],[11,325.56,5.92,"So right understanding learns to understand that"],[11,331.48,4.6,"without all these realities appearing, there is no citta."],[11,336.08,3.56,"But when citta arises, these are now appearing."],[11,339.64,8.88,"For example, visible object right now is absolute visible object"],[11,349.08,8.36,"because it’s that dhātu, element, which can impinge on the eye sense, not on the other senses."],[11,357.44,3.12,"So that citta can see it. Just that."],[11,361.2,5.44,"So we have been living for quite a long, long time, eons and eons,"],[11,366.64,4.56,"and when there is the understanding of all these things... just for this?"],[11,371.2,6.64,"Just for seeing visible object and hearing sound and everything that goes away. See?"],[11,377.84,5.92,"All the time unknowingly, just for this, in the circle of life and death, without understanding."],[11,383.76,6.44,"So it’s not a matter of trying so hard to develop it, but understanding it,"],[11,390.2,4.4,"and it will lead to direct awareness."],[11,394.6,4.04,"And then one knows that it’s not you who is aware,"],[11,398.64,5.56,"but it’s time for right awareness to arise, and it is aware at that moment."],[11,404.2,4.88,"So understanding begins to know that it’s so true."],[11,409.08,3.4,"Hardness is just hardness. It’s not visible object."],[11,413.0,4.84,"So when we talk about the noble truth—this is one—"],[11,418.88,3.96,"the hardness, visible object, and everything in life."],[11,422.84,4.72,"Just learn to understand that they are true. They are so true—when?"],[11,428.32,4.84,"When one appears through one doorway. Just that, only that."],[11,433.76,7.88,"And this is the way to help or to support awareness and other kusala, not just satipaṭṭhāna."],[11,442.6,7.12,"And this is the way to eliminate the idea of the “I” who is trying so hard"],[11,449.72,5.88,"because as long as one is trying, for years and for so long, it doesn’t work!"],[11,455.6,6.24,"Because it’s so foolish to do something without any result at all."],[11,461.84,5.16,"Better to lie down or go and have something instead. See?"],[11,467.68,2.84,"So we just come and talk about realities,"],[11,470.52,5.44,"just to have paññā understand better and better, and paññā works its way."],[11,475.96,5.4,"It becomes detached from wrong view, becomes detached from clinging,"],[11,481.36,7.96,"becomes detached from going away from this moment to select other objects for right understanding."],[11,490.16,4.12,"So it’s not the easy way, because people do not understand this."],[11,494.28,5.88,"As soon as they hear about satipaṭṭhāna, they’d like to do it instantly,"],[11,500.16,3.44,"trying so hard to get it. But that is wrong."],[11,504.68,4.04,"Quite wrong, because it’s the self who’s trying."],[11,509.4,7.36,"And when they learn about the āyatanas, the dhātu, and the paṭicca-samuppāda,"],[11,516.76,3.16,"they can memorize all this,"],[11,521.36,8.52,"but not understand that when anything appears, that object is also āyatana,"],[11,530.4,3.92,"and the eye sense or ear sense is also āyatana."],[11,534.32,3.88,"Why? Because without these coming together,"],[11,538.76,3.36,"there cannot be hearing or anything in the world appearing at all."],[11,543.16,3.32,"So we can understand āyatanas not just by the book,"],[11,546.48,7.52,"but by awareness and by understanding the characteristic of realities."],[11,554.0,5.08,"It goes deeper and deeper to the moment when there is no self"],[11,559.08,5.44,"and when realities appear and the understanding of the āyatanas is there."],[11,565.16,4.8,"So it’s not just the word in the book, no matter whether it’s about dhātu, element."],[11,570.64,1.2,"Because hardness,"],[11,572.56,5.84,"we can say it’s an element without any direct understanding or direct awareness."],[11,578.4,4.88,"But when it’s there, paññā develops to see that it is real,"],[11,583.28,2.68,"so it’s dhātu. We don’t have to use any word"],[11,586.48,5.4,"because at the moment of enlightenment, all ariyas, like the Buddha himself,"],[11,592.84,2.92,"had no word, no thinking."],[11,595.76,7.64,"But it’s the direct experiencing of the true nature of realities which cannot be hidden anymore"],[11,603.4,4.8,"because paññā has developed so that reality can appear to paññā."],[11,609.16,4.08,"Reality arises and appears, but it goes away so fast."],[11,613.24,1.88,"But we don’t have to think about that."],[11,615.76,6.32,"Just develop understanding by knowing the moment when awareness arises"],[11,622.08,3.06,"and when there is no awareness. That’s all. This is the beginning."],[11,625.14,2.5,"[Nina] It’s so difficult to know the difference."],[11,627.64,4.56,"[A. Sujin] When awareness does not arise, it’s impossible to think about it."],[11,632.2,4.24,"But whenever it arises, one knows the difference instantly."],[11,636.44,4.84,"That it’s different when touching and hardness appear,"],[11,641.28,6.32,"and there is no thinking about the dhātu or the reality right then"],[11,647.6,6.04,"because one always thinks about it as something all the time, and it passes so fast."],[11,654.36,4.08,"So it depends on direct awareness to be aware,"],[11,658.44,6.84,"even just very little and very slight, because there is no change, no difference."],[11,665.92,2.08,"Just then, when it is aware, and that’s all."],[11,669.04,3.24,"Becoming detached again little by little, little by little."],[11,680.88,5.44,"Earlier you were saying, develop paññā to become detached from reality."],[11,686.32,3.0,"[A. Sujin] From clinging. Because without understanding,"],[11,689.32,2.44,"how can there be detachment? [Right.]"],[11,692.72,4.44,"There can never be detachment by the self, or by the idea of self."],[11,699.44,6.24,"[Right, but what is the importance of becoming detached as opposed to"],[11,705.68,2.24,"understanding the true nature of reality?]"],[11,707.92,6.6,"When there is no understanding, is there attachment or detachment? [Attachment.]"],[11,715.2,1.84,"But when there is understanding,"],[11,717.04,5.6,"one does not know the moment when it develops detachment by understanding."],[11,726.24,5.52,"By itself. It’s not another time of trying to become detached. [Right.]"],[11,739.08,5.24,"No-self, so it’s there; it understands at the same time."],[11,744.32,5.2,"It becomes detached, and it grows little by little."],[11,751.88,10.36,"[Is it attachment to realities that is the problem of wrong view, that exacerbates or"],[11,763.16,1.24,"makes us have more wrong view?]"],[11,765.44,4.44,"We are talking about wrong view of self, right?"],[11,770.48,5.2,"But when it does not arise, can there be the understanding of the reality"],[11,776.2,1.88,"of wrong view of self?"],[11,778.6,4.56,"But when there is awareness, you don’t have to make anything arise at all."],[11,783.16,2.44,"There can be wrong view arising,"],[11,786.12,5.72,"so awareness can know right then the characteristic of nāma,"],[11,792.36,4.72,"the mental element, no-self, which is there,"],[11,797.08,3.84,"but that is the element of “I” being there."],[11,801.6,6.32,"So one sees realities, as we’re used to talking about, like lobha and wrong view and everything,"],[11,808.8,3.68,"when there is awareness of that particular one."],[11,813.88,7.96,"So we could say that we all have wrong view of self, but that’s only words."],[11,822.68,8.52,"But when there is awareness, it shows that at that moment it’s the clinging, it’s the self there."],[11,831.2,5.48,"Even hardness here, when there is nothing in the world at all, just hardness."],[11,836.68,3.64,"I, it’s still I. It’s me. It’s mine."],[11,840.32,4.52,"And when it’s heat, like someone has a high temperature,"],[11,846.0,7.32,"fever or illness, and heat is there, it’s me. See? It’s me."],[11,853.32,2.04,"And then we know that it’s not only about words,"],[11,855.36,5.36,"but when that particular object appears, and there is still the idea of self,"],[11,860.72,5.92,"we know that paññā will eliminate it when it knows more clearly that it’s not me."],[11,866.64,3.12,"It’s only dhātu. It’s only a reality."],[11,870.68,6.24,"[Nina] I have trouble, really, with the worry being me, and you said it’s only nāma."],[11,876.92,4.16,"[A. Sujin] But it’s the truth. Remember that it’s the truth."],[11,881.08,3.52,"No matter how we think this way or that way, the truth is that."],[11,885.24,5.56,"So coming to the truth little by little to see what is true."],[11,893.96,5.48,"Right. Because we know a lot about theory. We know a lot from books,"],[11,899.44,5.88,"but it's not the direct awareness of anyone in a day."],[11,906.12,4.64,"So we know that only when it develops in a day,"],[11,910.76,6.32,"it arises, and it turns out to be realities instead of people and things."],[11,919.56,4.52,"It’s so difficult; you’re praising the wisdom of the Buddha by saying this."],[11,924.76,3.99,"Otherwise, using the term Buddha would have no meaning."],[11,928.75,5.49,"[Jill] Nina, because of your accumulations of worry about your beloved’s health,"],[11,934.24,1.36,"you can’t stop it."],[11,935.6,5.44,"[A. Sujin] The purpose is not to stop thinking or worrying about him."],[11,941.04,2.64,"But understanding any moment as it is."],[11,945.52,3.64,"Who doesn’t care for the dear ones as long as attachment is there?"],[11,951.2,7.6,"We know the different degrees of ariyas. Sotāpanna is not sakadāgāmi, not anāgāmi, not an arahant."],[11,962.36,0.84,"You do not have troubles."],[11,964.72,4.6,"[So long as we don’t know the difference between nāma and rūpa, we cannot yet"],[11,970.16,1.95,"really be aware of worry as non-self.]"],[11,972.11,4.41,"Yes, yes. [Because we don’t know the difference between nāma and rūpa.]"],[11,976.52,3.88,"Yes! Because when it does not know, it does not know. You cannot do anything."],[11,987.68,6.36,"It’s like a test in everyday life, whether or how much you cling to the result,"],[11,994.04,3.32,"or you do not cling now to the sense objects,"],[11,997.36,4.68,"but you cling to knowing the difference between nāma and rūpa."],[11,1002.6,5.48,"And it hinders instantly. And so one knows that lobha is there."],[11,1008.08,3.88,"Lobha always hinders. It’s the black curtain."],[12,2.5,10.01,"[Q:] At the moment when saddha is there, are the cetasikas of metta and mudita also there?"],[12,12.53,7.28,"[A. Sujin:] Okay, so now, studying just one word at a time;"],[12,19.84,4.9,"we use many, many paññatti for each different moment,"],[12,24.76,3.22,"but they have their own different aspects too."],[12,28.0,5.58,"For example, is metta a cetasika?"],[12,36.48,3.7,"That's why we should learn about just one word at a time"],[12,40.2,7.02,"to understand the differences of the same characteristic at different levels and of different aspects."],[12,47.24,7.5,"Can you metta a tree?"],[12,54.76,6.74,"Can anyone metta a tree or a flower or the food?"],[12,63.44,8.7,"So, no one can have metta towards that which is not a being, right?"],[12,72.16,3.14,"The nature of metta is adosa cetasika"],[12,75.32,7.38,"because as long as anger is not there, even if you hear some very bad words,"],[12,82.72,3.7,"there can be metta, see? Different."],[12,86.44,5.02,"Being friendly is different from getting angry."],[12,91.48,8.3,"At the moment when there is anger,"],[12,91.48,8.3,"that means that there is no metta towards that person, right?"],[12,99.8,5.82,"But actually, the reality of it is adosa cetasika."],[12,105.64,4.58,"That's why we have to understand that there is no metta cetasika,"],[12,110.24,5.22,"but there can be dosa and adosa, which are different."],[12,115.48,6.62,"So at the moment of having no-dosa,"],[12,115.48,6.62,"whether it is the moment of attachment"],[12,122.12,2.54,"- and there can be attachment to anything -"],[12,124.68,5.78,"while for metta, karuna, mudita, and upekkha, the four brahma-vihara,"],[12,130.48,6.1,"it means the moment of having the feeling of kindness"],[12,130.48,6.1,"or being kind to the beings which are the object at that very moment."],[12,143.08,8.66,"When someone gets the best things in life, or something very good or very pleasant, do you have karuna?"],[12,151.76,3.82,"But when you see a sick person or poor people,"],[12,155.6,4.98,"there can be the moment of feeling sympathetic to that person."],[12,160.6,4.06,"And with understanding, there can be more and more friendliness"],[12,164.68,5.5,"and karuna when that person gets something bad."],[12,170.2,5.66,"That's why, for the Buddha, he had karuna for all beings"],[12,175.88,3.66,"because those beings could not understand the truth"],[12,179.56,7.14,"when they couldn't hear the right words or the true words about whatever is appearing now."],[12,186.72,5.98,"So you can understand that very moment, what reality is there. See?"],[12,192.72,6.86,"Karuna, when people get something bad, sickness or whatever, losing money, for example."],[12,199.6,5.46,"But when people are living happily and have everything they like, enjoying life,"],[12,205.08,5.3,"do you have karuna or do you have mudita?"],[12,210.4,2.18,"These are just examples in life,"],[12,212.91,5.91,"what moment is karuna and what moment is metta and what moment is mudita."],[12,218.84,7.02,"When someone gets good things and you appreciate or rejoice, not with lobha,"],[12,225.88,5.1,"but understanding the truth, that all must be conditioned to be such and such."],[12,231.0,8.1,"It can be upekkha or metta or mudita, but when one is in hardship, it is karuna."],[12,239.12,7.74,"Sympathizing with that person so much about his kamma, which conditioned such a situation."],[12,246.88,7.66,"And there can also be kindness too, to help, see? Being friendly."],[12,254.56,5.74,"But metta and lobha are very close: it is said that they are close friends"],[12,260.32,4.18,"because one cannot see the danger of lobha."],[12,264.52,6.06,"But actually, the moment of lobha cannot be metta."],[12,270.6,8.94,"So is there an example to understand the difference between metta and lobha?"],[12,279.56,5.62,"When you help just this person, not the other person at all,"],[12,285.2,5.86,"who is in the same situation, is that metta or lobha?"],[12,291.08,4.7,"That's why metta does not have limitations at all."],[12,295.8,7.1,"It's not limited to that person only or this person only, but to any being."],[12,303.02,6.86,"So at the moment of getting angry, is that metta?"],[12,309.8,8.06,"And when you like that thing or that person so much, is that metta?"],[12,317.88,4.7,"Pañña can understand the difference between moments of metta and moments of lobha."],[12,322.6,5.06,"For example, parents love, are attached, to their own children,"],[12,327.68,3.66,"but what about others' children?"],[12,331.36,5.46,"That's why lobha can condition dosa."],[12,336.84,4.1,"When the person you like so much changes or something like that, see,"],[12,340.96,9.3,"it brings sorrow, not from kindness or metta, but from attachment."],[12,350.28,3.58,"Understanding the difference between metta and lobha in a day"],[12,353.88,7.26,"can condition more moments of kindness instead of attachment."],[12,361.16,8.06,"And what about today? How many moments of metta or karuna or mudita or upekkha?"],[12,369.24,1.86,"It's not from your own thinking,"],[12,371.12,6.7,"but from understanding the truth of each different reality."],[12,377.84,4.9,"And the understanding of no-self, no-one at all, only suññata,"],[12,382.76,10.78,"can condition more and more metta in a day, and less and less akusala realities."],[12,393.56,8.16,"So there's no one who knows besides the understanding which knows exactly the difference between akusala and kusala."],[13,7.06,6.32,"[Tam B.] I would like to ask a question about whether there can be kusala while dreaming."],[13,25.47,4.94,"Okay, can citta be kusala? [Citta can be kusala...]"],[13,31.12,6.19,"So, what citta is dreaming? [The citta that thinks.]"],[13,37.72,5.7,"Okay, dreaming is thinking. What doorway? [Through the mind door.]"],[13,43.7,2.69,"See, that's how we understand the truth."],[13,47.12,6.1,"Can the mind-door-citta be kusala? [Yes.]"],[13,54.08,4.2,"So, why not being kusala while dreaming?"],[13,59.79,6.93,"Not only akusala citta. Like now, not only akusala citta right now."],[13,66.72,5.28,"What is the difference between dreaming and now?"],[13,76.32,6.48,"Can there be the moment of realization of the truth in a dream? [No.]"],[13,84.0,4.37,"That's why the difference between dreaming and not dreaming"],[13,89.28,4.28,"is the moment of understanding, right? [Yes.]"],[13,94.16,5.99,"Can there be any understanding in a dream? [No.]"],[13,100.45,7.71,"Really? So, does this mean that while dreaming there are only akusala moments?"],[13,108.72,4.19,"Did you dream last night? [Yes.]"],[13,112.99,8.97,"About? Only akusala? Or one can dream about kusala events too?"],[13,123.84,3.97,"So, what did you dream about last night? [I can't remember.]"],[13,127.93,2.39,"Some kind, someday, can't it be remembered?"],[13,137.14,7.85,"Is it wholesome or not wholesome? [I can even think about Dhamma in a dream.]"],[13,145.2,7.2,"So, can there be other kusala moments, not just dreaming about Dhamma discussions. [I don't know.]"],[13,152.4,7.77,"So now, is it wholesome thinking or unwholesome thinking right now? [Mostly unwholesome.]"],[13,160.88,4.04,"So, in a dream, mostly...? [For sure, Ajahn.]"],[13,165.36,4.11,"See, can't there be some moments of kusala as well, like now?"],[13,170.85,6.9,"Can anyone stop citta to be wholesome while dreaming? [Cannot be stopped.]"],[13,178.62,8.61,"No matter what doorway it is, citta which is wholesome or unwholesome arise by conditions."],[13,199.13,3.21,"And Sotapanna? [Still has dreams.]"],[13,202.56,7.2,"Kusala or akusala? [I think he still has akusala cittas...]"],[13,209.76,3.99,"So, you mean that citta is akusala while dreaming?"],[13,215.04,8.08,"Or it can be wholesome citta while dreaming too, in a dream, just like now,"],[13,224.08,2.99,"if you don't talk about the sense door in between,"],[13,228.08,7.6,"many moments of mind door, wholesome or unwholesome."],[13,236.48,3.0,"For those who have no understanding at all,"],[13,240.53,3.78,"more conditions for unwholesomeness in dreams."],[13,248.8,12.64,"Where did the Buddha say: no kusala in dreams? Is it his words? See."],[13,261.44,6.5,"And if the dream keeps on going without waking up at all, all day, all night,"],[13,268.7,3.95,"unwholesome moment or what? Or by conditions?"],[13,273.49,2.93,"Just like now, this is daydreaming"],[13,276.96,4.84,"because there are moments of the other sense-doors in between."],[13,283.61,7.16,"Can you think with friendliness? [Yes.]"],[13,292.24,7.13,"Can't it be in a dream, without seeing or hearing, the processes of sense door in between?"],[13,301.9,1.44,"Thinking to help."],[13,305.12,8.51,"Thinking of going to listen; considering, discussing about Dhamma."],[13,314.87,2.42,"Can't that be in a dream as well?"],[13,323.28,9.47,"Are you thinking of helping someone now, to understand the truth? [Sometimes, yes.]"],[13,333.84,5.12,"Can that be through the mind door? [It has to be mind door, Ajahn.]"],[13,339.84,14.48,"At any moment or just not in dreams? [Yes, like now.] Yeah."],[13,356.56,2.37,"Can't there be only dreaming now,"],[13,359.2,7.79,"when there are no sense door's processes at all in between? [Can be, Ajahn.]"],[13,367.65,3.76,"Can't there be kusala moments, just like now,"],[13,371.58,4.21,"without the sense door in between the mind door processes?"],[13,378.56,3.76,"What is the difference between this moment of kusala thinking"],[13,382.32,3.44,"and the moment thinking to help someone or doing"],[13,385.85,14.09,"something which is wholesome in a dream? [It's very blurred.]"],[13,400.48,7.02,"Do you know now whether the past moment was kusala or akusala? [Can be, Ajahn.]"],[13,407.77,0.84,"Really? [Yes.]"],[13,409.04,5.24,"What about the present moment, kusala or akusala? [Akusala.]"],[13,414.65,2.92,"How do you know? [Because there was doubt, Ajahn.]"],[13,418.24,5.38,"Really? Can there be doubt in a dream? [There can be.]"],[13,424.48,3.37,"Can there be no doubt in a dream? [Yes.]"],[13,428.16,3.73,"Exactly the same, mind door;"],[13,432.32,3.92,"not seeing, not hearing, not smelling,"],[13,436.66,11.7,"not touching; only thinking. [But like the arahat, he has no dreams anymore.]"],[13,449.81,5.34,"And before becoming arahat, can there be good dreams?"],[13,464.03,6.26,"Or about teaching, talking, discussing Dhamma with someone."],[13,472.32,6.61,"Not about killing, stealing, hating, harming."],[13,483.28,4.13,"Can there be dreaming about talking Dhamma with others? [Yes.]"],[13,488.8,5.4,"Is it wholesome or unwholesome dreaming? [Even now...]"],[13,494.36,6.78,"Not now, in a dream. Anagami... [Having a Dhamma discussion with a friend in a dream...]"],[13,501.7,3.49,"Is it akusala moment? [Not sure, Ajahn.]"],[13,506.17,4.48,"Citta has to be kusala or akusala, or vipaka or kiriya."],[13,511.84,6.83,"So now, is citta kusala or akusala? [Because there's still doubt.]"],[13,518.95,9.03,"The same. The same. Just like dreaming. See. Just like now. Exactly."],[13,528.29,9.71,"Kusala is kusala, akusala is akusala, kiriya is kiriya, vipaka is vipaka. Who knows?"],[13,539.12,2.81,"It has to be sati and sampajanna"],[13,544.56,6.04,"which can know the exact moment, as object, as it is."],[13,552.0,1.43,"So now, while talking,"],[13,554.04,8.51,"is there irritation in between, unpleasant feeling in between, kusala or akusala in between?"],[13,563.2,4.68,"Just one citta cannot be of two kinds, like vipaka and kiriya,"],[13,568.4,2.51,"or kusala and akusala mixed at all."],[13,573.99,6.65,"So, thinking now, isn't it like thinking in a dream?"],[13,581.84,5.91,"How do you know that it's different? When there is another doorway appearing,"],[13,589.6,8.48,"otherwise when there are no sense door objects or sense door cittas arising in between at all,"],[13,598.24,3.2,"how can one know whether it's a dream or not a dream?"],[13,606.13,8.88,"Like now, see, what is there is not clear, right?"],[13,615.76,2.31,"Whether it's wholesome or unwholesome."],[13,619.6,9.45,"The same as in a dream. [Yes. I think when the citta is akusala, it's very clear.]"],[13,629.76,5.19,"Really? So, is there ditthasava now? [Yes.]"],[13,635.28,4.46,"Who knows? The same as in a dream."],[13,641.19,6.45,"No certain, no exact, no clear understanding of what is there."],[13,648.0,3.46,"That's why we say, \"I'm thinking\" or \"I'm dreaming,\""],[13,651.62,4.04,"because no other processes, sense door ones, in between at all."],[13,657.6,3.8,"Otherwise, how could it be known that it's a dream?"],[13,662.21,4.39,"Because thinking is thinking, through the mind door."],[13,667.28,3.46,"While there are no other doorways, sense doorways, in between,"],[13,671.04,3.65,"how can it be known whether it's dreaming or not dreaming?"],[13,676.46,1.59,"Isn't it right?"],[13,678.87,3.77,"Without the sense door in between,"],[13,684.02,5.52,"how can it be known whether it's dreaming or not dreaming?"],[13,702.0,6.02,"So, can you say that there are sense door processes in between the mind-door processes?"],[13,710.72,1.84,"Aren't we dreaming about it now,"],[13,712.56,5.04,"through the mind door and there are also sense doors processes in between? [Yes.]"],[13,719.52,4.99,"What is more? To be known that it was not a dream or that it was a dream."],[13,725.78,5.93,"How can it be known whether it's a dream or not a dream? [Not knowing whether it's true or not true.]"],[13,734.56,5.41,"What do you mean by true or not true? Dreaming dreams about what?"],[13,740.94,3.91,"Not the moment of thinking. Not the moment of dreaming."],[13,745.76,6.72,"That's why what doorway arise more than the other doorways, to be taken for dreaming,"],[13,752.88,2.75,"daydream or night dream? [Mind door.]"],[13,755.94,5.97,"So, is there daydreaming now or night dreaming now? [Now it's daydreaming.]"],[13,762.2,2.02,"See, the same, thinking."],[13,766.24,5.44,"Just the word. Isn't it? Thinking has to be thinking."],[13,772.67,7.89,"It cannot see, it cannot hear; it thinks, and so much fantasy thinking, by conditions."],[13,783.12,5.52,"That's why last night I dreamt about... See, who knows?"],[13,788.64,3.42,"And tonight, what the dream will be about?"],[13,792.48,8.16,"Unknown, like now; what kind of thinking in between sense door processes?"],[13,801.2,5.58,"Can it be expected? Can it be known? Not at all, just like in a dream."],[13,807.52,5.12,"No one knows what tonight's dream will be about."],[13,815.14,9.15,"But it's thinking, and for the one who is insane, what about his thinking?"],[13,825.44,5.25,"Just like common people, ordinary one, the mad man?"],[13,841.28,2.22,"Yes, but thinking is thinking."],[13,844.1,4.66,"And thinking can be kusala by conditions or akusala by conditions. [Yes.]"],[13,849.37,5.15,"Even right now, the akusala moment is unknown, and the kusala moment is unknown."],[13,855.28,2.21,"Is it different from thinking?"],[13,860.33,4.79,"Can the moment of kusala be known now? [Now it's mostly akusala.]"],[13,865.12,2.79,"How do you know that mostly it's akusala?"],[13,870.2,4.88,"[Because...] more conditions."],[13,875.66,7.05,"So, more conditions to condition thinking, no matter while dreaming or just like now."],[13,882.72,5.48,"Exactly the same, by conditions. Thinking is thinking for sure."],[13,889.68,5.51,"But when there are sense-door's processes in between, it thinks about that,"],[13,896.16,3.54,"about the same object of sense-door."],[13,900.88,3.07,"And who can stop the dreaming"],[13,904.82,3.38,"conditioned by the accumulation of today's sense-door-processes"],[13,908.7,6.58,"or yesterday or last life or long time ago? Who knows? Fantasy thinking."],[13,916.4,6.98,"And for the mad man, fantasy thinking, but thinking is thinking."],[13,925.07,12.21,"Can thinking be different from thinking now, the thinking itself? [Can you say it again?]"],[13,937.28,9.84,"Can the thinking now also be the thinking in a dream? Or cannot be in a dream?"],[13,947.12,6.48,"It is only thinking, but it's different by conditions."],[13,953.6,8.96,"For the wise one and the ignorant one, can they think the same?"],[13,962.56,4.0,"Are there the same conditions for different people? [Not the same conditions.]"],[13,966.56,4.88,"That's why thinking cannot be anything else, it is thinking only,"],[13,971.44,8.16,"and there are so many, many, uncountable object of thinking, by conditions."],[13,979.6,7.8,"That's why even we say, \"I'm dreaming,\" it's thinking without sense door processes in between,"],[13,987.4,4.24,"for longer than in daydreaming."],[13,992.64,6.88,"Because even now, we think that we are talking and thinking, but what about seeing?"],[13,999.52,6.4,"It seems it's there all day. How come?"],[13,1005.92,7.44,"And who knows what is there after the seeing, kusala or akusala?"],[13,1013.36,7.44,"So now, what is this moment, kusala or akusala? Can it be known?"],[13,1020.8,3.36,"If it's not known, it's the same like dreaming:"],[13,1024.16,5.92,"it's not known whether it's kusala or akusala."],[13,1030.08,10.32,"Like now, going shopping and going to read the book on Dhamma, see."],[13,1040.4,6.48,"And in the dream, can there be moment of reading?"],[13,1046.88,9.35,"Not just like when it's not a dream, but the idea is there."],[13,1056.23,9.29,"Doesn't one in a dream go somewhere, like now; kusala or akusala?"],[13,1065.52,4.16,"Helping others in a dream."],[13,1069.68,5.04,"And what is moment of helping others now?"],[13,1074.72,9.04,"Kusala moment or akusala moment?"],[13,1083.76,4.08,"So, thinking is thinking. It can think about anything,"],[13,1089.04,7.68,"and it's not just only unwholesome thinking which has conditions to arise"],[13,1096.72,8.88,"because thinking can be wholesome or unwholesome, no matter in a dream or not in a dream."],[13,1105.6,4.96,"What about thinking about the good deeds that you have done, see,"],[13,1110.56,5.12,"and thinking about kusala moments in a dream, about that which you have done?"],[13,1115.68,12.08,"The same, kusala. Kusala cannot be akusala, for sure."],[13,1127.76,5.12,"But while there's sense door in between, like now,"],[13,1132.88,4.96,"it seems like there are sense door processes more than mind-door ones."],[13,1137.84,5.84,"But in truth, mind-doors are more than sense-doors. Isn't that right? [Yes.]"],[13,1143.68,5.68,"Exactly the same as dreaming. But what is more?"],[13,1149.36,5.84,"The sense-doors are more or the mind-doors are more? Or what appears more?"],[13,1155.2,6.64,"The object which is seen or the object of thinking? Who knows?"],[13,1161.84,4.48,"But thinking can be kusala, for sure."],[13,1166.32,3.6,"Just like now, how many moments of kusala?"],[13,1169.92,6.0,"Less or more than akusala? The same as in dreaming."],[13,1175.92,1.48,"And what is more?"],[13,1177.4,8.76,"The attachment and ignorance following the seeing process or in the process of seeing? See."],[13,1186.16,7.44,"And seeing sees all day. What about dreaming? It's not all day. It's not all night."],[13,1195.04,6.63,"So, what's more in a day or in a dream? [Akusala.]"],[13,1201.67,2.08,"Both in a day and in a dream."],[13,1203.76,8.72,"And can there be kusala in between the sense door process in a day? [Yes.]"],[13,1212.48,4.64,"So, the same holds for dreaming, in a dream."],[13,1217.12,10.16,"There can be moment of kusala as there can be moment of kusala while there's no dreaming."],[13,1227.28,6.4,"But the mind-door processes condition the idea of dreaming."],[13,1233.68,5.84,"Even now, the mind-door processes are more than sense-door processes."],[13,1239.52,4.56,"But the sense-door processes seems to be there all day, there seems to be seeing all day,"],[13,1244.08,2.8,"and the other processes of sense-doors too."],[13,1246.88,6.72,"So, we don't take it for a dream, but life is a dream."],[13,1253.6,9.27,"No matter it's night dream or day dream, thinking is there."],[13,1268.64,4.16,"It doesn't matter what we call it, day or night dream."],[13,1272.8,5.44,"It is as it is. Kusala is kusala. Akusala is akusala."],[13,1278.24,3.28,"What about heaven, Brahma plane?"],[13,1286.32,3.75,"Is there mind door?"],[13,1290.07,6.65,"There can be doubt whether they dream or not, see."],[13,1296.72,6.24,"What is longer, night or day? See."],[13,1302.96,7.84,"It's not a matter of using any word to represent the thinking in different manners,"],[13,1310.8,5.6,"but the truth is that citta is citta."],[13,1316.4,3.44,"Thinking is not seeing, that's all."],[13,1319.84,6.32,"No matter we take it for a dream or not a dream, here or there, heaven or hell, see."],[13,1326.16,7.04,"Who knows? Thinking is always thinking. It cannot be changed."],[13,1333.2,4.0,"It is conditioned to arise and falls away instantly,"],[13,1337.2,6.88,"no matter in a dream or not in a dream; that's the way it is."],[13,1344.08,7.84,"But the idea about it is there."],[13,1351.92,6.64,"Does anyone sleep during the day, not at night? [Many people.]"],[13,1358.56,7.68,"Many people, but sleeping is sleeping. Mind-door processes."],[13,1366.24,8.08,"We can think a lot without paying any attention to any sense door object at all,"],[13,1374.32,5.28,"while there are so many sense door processes too, in between."],[13,1379.6,7.6,"But when we talk about the word \"dream\", it's just thinking, more thinking than the other doorways."],[13,1387.2,7.52,"And thinking can think about anything, even if it hasn't appeared in this life."],[13,1394.72,7.52,"There can be moment of such thinking about that which hasn't been seen before at all in this life."],[13,1402.24,11.2,"But by conditions, thinking can think about anything. Isn't it true? [Yes.]"],[13,1413.44,6.8,"Even right now, thinking can think about anything, like we are thinking about dreaming."],[13,1420.24,5.6,"What is it? Whether it can be kusala or whether it cannot be kusala,"],[13,1425.84,8.24,"or it can be either, by conditions; the javana moments."],[13,1434.08,4.96,"So many conditions for each moment to arise."],[13,1439.04,8.72,"So, we consider again and again, can there be kusala citta while dreaming?"],[13,1447.76,11.36,"If not, why not? Because it's thinking. It's mind-door process. It can think about anything."],[13,1459.12,16.72,"Tonight, dreaming about kusala deeds, paying respect in a dream to the person who deserves it."],[13,1475.84,4.64,"Is it wholesome, at that moment?"],[13,1480.48,16.0,"It's not killing. It's not bad words towards that person who deserves respect."],[13,1496.48,13.2,"So, can there be kusala citta in a dream? If not, why not?"],[13,1509.68,5.68,"Can anyone stop conditions for kusala to arise in mind-door processes,"],[13,1515.36,5.2,"no matter it's in a dream or not in a dream?"],[13,1520.56,6.08,"What we call dreaming is moment when there's no sense door processes,"],[13,1526.64,12.48,"for as long or as much as in daylight, during the day."],[13,1539.12,6.48,"Let's see tonight's dream, whether it's kusala or akusala."],[13,1545.6,7.04,"Just like now. Mind door."],[13,1552.64,7.76,"What is this moment, kusala or akusala? [It is kusala Ajahn.]"],[13,1560.4,3.6,"And the previous moment? [Akusala.]"],[13,1564.0,3.48,"And the next moment? [Akusala, mostly.]"],[13,1570.72,6.8,"If you don't say dreaming, is thinking still kusala or akusala?"],[13,1577.52,12.56,"By conditions. [Now there's attachment to little Tiger.]"],[13,1590.08,9.52,"In a dream, and now, is there any kusala towards Tiger? [Yes.]"],[13,1599.6,3.12,"So, can it be a dream?"],[13,1602.72,3.6,"Let's see tonight, after that,"],[13,1606.32,10.48,"whether it's kusala or akusala dreaming. [Usually I don't remember my dreams.]"],[13,1616.8,5.12,"Tonight's? Not yet."],[13,1621.92,9.6,"Kusala or akusala? Who knows until it's there."],[13,1631.52,5.12,"So, tomorrow there can be any hint of kusala or akusala in a"],[13,1636.64,6.56,"dream after tonight. [I think it's not that easy, Ajahn.]"],[13,1644.56,5.36,"But when you can remember what was the dream about,"],[13,1649.92,3.76,"there can be moment of knowing whether it was kusala or akusala."],[13,1653.68,5.12,"Just like now, who knows whether this moment is kusala or akusala?"],[13,1658.8,1.8,"But it can be known."],[13,1660.6,9.47,"[Jonothan] Doesn't it require pañña to understand moments of kusala from akusala?"],[13,1670.07,14.92,"[A. Sujin] That's why it conditions doubt about dreaming, whether it's kusala or akusala."],[13,1684.99,0.03,"Just like now. [Thank you, Ajahn.]"],[13,1685.02,0.34,"Kha! Sawadee kha, everyone."]]};
